\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They were little\u8217\'20\'19: photos show children illegally working in US slaughterhouse\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 775 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2023\par 21:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Images released by US labor department show conditions over 100 children faced at Packers Sanitation Services Incorporated\par \par \uc2 Harrowing photos released by the US labor department taken at a slaughterhouse plant in Nebraska show the conditions more than 100 children faced while illegally working for Packers Sanitation Services Incorporated (PSSI) before the department cracked down on the company for violating child labor laws.\par \par \uc2 The pictures show employees covered in protective gear, using chemicals to spray down and sanitize equipment. In some of the pictures, made public on Sunday by the television news show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/government-investigation-into-slaughterhouse-cleaning-company-that-hired-children-60-minutes-transcript-2023-05-07/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60 Minutes}}}\uc2 , some of the employees appear to be young children, wearing protective face glasses and holding buckets.\par \par \uc2 In February, the labor department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20230217-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fined}}}\uc2  PSSI $1.5m for employing at least 102 children ages 13 to 17 across 13 meat-packing plants in eight states. The fine amounts to $15,138 for each child, the maximum penalty under federal law. The Wisconsin-based company is one of the largest food sanitation companies in the US and is contracted by meat plants to sanitize facilities. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pssi.com/about/#:~:text=PSSI%20is%20North%20America's%20leading,725%20partner%20plants%20every%20day."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  it works with more than 725 partner plants.\par \par \uc2 The department started its investigation into PSSI in August 2022 after a middle school in Grand Island, Nebraska, notified police that a 14-year-old student came to school with acid burns on her hands and knees. The girl told staff that she was working night shifts at a local slaughterhouse plant. Teachers also noticed that other students were falling asleep in class after reportedly working at the plant at night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seemed to be known within the community that minors either are or were working overnight shifts. They told us about children that were falling asleep in class, that they had burns, chemical burns. They were concerned for the safety of the kids. They were concerned that they weren\u8217\'20\'19t able to stay awake and do their job, which is learning in school,\u8221\'20\'1D Shannon Rebolledo, a labor department investigator, told 60 Minutes.\par \par \uc2 When the labor department visited the plant \u8211\'20\'13 which is run by the meat producer JBS and is one of the largest beef production plants in the country \u8211\'20\'13 during the night shift, they \u8220\'20\'1Cnoted the difference in the appearance of these workers\u8221\'20\'1D that were coming in for the late shift.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were little,\u8221\'20\'1D Rebolledo said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey looked young.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An audit of PSSI found more children were working at other plants, leading the labor department to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/OPA/newsreleases/2022/11/SOLWHDPSSI%20FILINGS.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sue}}}\uc2  the company for violating federal labor laws. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kstp.com/kstp-news/local-news/labor-dept-pssi-settle-suit-alleging-child-labor-at-meatpacking-plants/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled}}}\uc2  with the department in December, agreeing to strengthen its child labor policies.\par \par \uc2 An anonymous former PSSI manager told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/feds-expand-probe-migrant-child-labor-slaughterhouses-rcna72930"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2  in February that the plant hired many undocumented migrant workers, some of whom used fake identities when applying to the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this industry, you have a lot of people who are undocumented workers. A lot of times it\u8217\'20\'19s because they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to pay well enough to hire people in America who want to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D the manager said.\par \par \uc2 Rebolledo told 60 Minutes that she believes the hiring of children \u8220\'20\'1Cwas the standard operating procedure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no way this was just a mistake, a clerical error, a handful of rogue individuals getting through. This was the standard operating procedure,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that she believed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe number [of children who were working] is likely much higher\u8221\'20\'1D than what the department ultimately found.\par \par \uc2 In statements, PSSI said that leaders were unaware that children were being employed and \u8220\'20\'1Chas a strong corporate commitment to our zero-tolerance policy against employing anyone under the age of 18, and fully shares the [labor department\u8217\'20\'19s] objective of ensuring full compliance of all locations\u8221\'20\'1D, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/pssi-hired-same-child-twice-clean-slaughterhouses-document-rcna71633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs soon as we became aware of the DoL\u8217\'20\'19s allegations, we conducted multiple additional audits of our employee base, and hired a third-party law firm to review and help further strengthen our policies in this area,\u8221\'20\'1D the company said in a separate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/17/business/child-labor-packers-sanitation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  in February.\par \par \uc2 PSSI appointed a new CEO, who took over at the end of April. The company also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pssi.com/2023/04/pssi-announces-leadership-transition/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a $10m fund \u8220\'20\'1Cdedicated to enhancing the wellbeing of children in the communities we serve and helping reduce the prevalence of the rising problem of unauthorized underage workers amid record levels of unaccompanied minors entering the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In March, the labor department announced an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/osec/osec20230324"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreement}}}\uc2  made with the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  where the two agencies will collaborate to \u8220\'20\'1Cidentify geographies and employers where children are being exploited\u8221\'20\'1D. The labor department reports a 69% rise in illegal child labor since 2018.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230509ej590028n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
