\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Focus organizing drives on workers without college degrees, US unions told\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,388 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2023\par 10:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Experts say union upsurge for journalists and graduate students is pleasing but blue-collar workers require assistance too\par \par \uc2 Union supporters have had plenty to applaud with regard to organizing college- educated workers, notching up dozens of unionization victories involving graduate students, adjunct professors, journalists, nurses and workers at museums, non-profits and video-game companies.\par \par \uc2 But some labor supporters who laud these victories are warning that something is awry, that there isn\u8217\'20\'19t nearly enough unionization of non-college-educated, lower-paid workers, whether factory workers or fast-food workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s great to have a union upsurge among anybody, but the strongest segment of the labor force which is unionizing seems to be people who have had some college or are college-educated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Kazin, an expert on social movements at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe bulk of the labor force did not go to college. They\u8217\'20\'19re arguably the ones that need unions the most.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kazin said that if unions are serious about building a fairer economy, they need to do more to organize workers without college degrees. \u8220\'20\'1CThere needs to be a dramatic breakthrough at a place like \uc2 Walmart\uc2  or some auto plant in the south,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 There are, of course, campaigns to unionize blue-collar and lower-paid workers, the best-known example being last year\u8217\'20\'19s unionization victory at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 8,300-employee warehouse on Staten Island. Several unions, including the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  and the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2 , are mounting and steadily winning union drives for blue-collar workers.\par \par \uc2 In March, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  unionized more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2022/03/us-foods-workers-in-charlotte-join-teamsters/#:~:text=2022.03.,seniority%2C%20job%20security%20and%20respect."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50 truck drivers in North Carolina at US Foods}}}\uc2 , a food service company, while \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  unionized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://therealnews.com/i-dont-want-to-work-two-jobs-college-of-william-mary-dining-services-workers-win-union-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 300 cafeteria workers last fall at William and Mary College}}}\uc2  in Virginia. Even though union victories in the south are difficult and unusual, the unionization victories for educated workers are getting more media and attention, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thetech.com/2022/04/08/grad-students-unionize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3,800 graduate student workers at MIT unionizing}}}\uc2  or workers at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chicagotribune.com/business/ct-biz-art-institute-employees-vote-form-union-20220111-xlkqgftg2rhsdjyw2catl6hnvu-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Art Institute of Chicago voting 142 to 44 to unionize}}}\uc2  or workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://techcrunch.com/2022/12/02/activision-blizzard-workers-in-albany-vote-to-form-the-companys-second-union/#:~:text=Just%20seven%20months%20ago%2C%20QA,be%20included%20in%20the%20unit."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Activision Blizzard in Albany, New York, voting 14 to 0 to unionize}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Union campaigns have spread like wildfire from university to university, museum to museum and newsroom to newsroom as those workers often get the union bug through social media or from friends at universities or museums that just unionized. Unionization has also spread rapidly among \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , where many workers and are in college or have been to college.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, unionization hasn\u8217\'20\'19t taken off nearly as rapidly at many blue-collar, lower-paid workplaces. No other Chipotle restaurant has unionized since workers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/08/25/chipotle-restaurant-in-michigan-votes-to-unionize-in-a-first-for-the-chain.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lansing, Michigan, voted last August to make theirs the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first unionized Chipotle}}}\uc2 . Only one \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse is unionized in the US, just two \uc2 Apple\uc2  stores and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/trader-joes-oakland-unionizes_n_64419c18e4b0d84038875869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 . Those companies have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/26/amazon-trader-joes-starbucks-anti-union-measures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mounted fierce anti-union counterattacks to slow}}}\uc2  and they hope stop the spread.\par \par \uc2 Chris Rosell, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 organizing director, says one reason unionization of blue-collar workers often doesn\u8217\'20\'19t catch fire is that it\u8217\'20\'19s frequently easier for anti-union consultants to scare and deter those workers. \u8220\'20\'1CBlue-collar workers often aren\u8217\'20\'19t as educated about this union-busting stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey could be more susceptible to these kinds of tactics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rosell said the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  often run elaborate campaigns that seek to inoculate workers from the pressures and propaganda from anti-union consultants. He said the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, hopes to double the union\u8217\'20\'19s membership and focus organizing on such area trucking, warehouses and sanitation work.\par \par \uc2 Erica Smiley, executive director of Jobs with Justice, a labor rights group, says it\u8217\'20\'19s often harder to unionize blue-collar workers because they tend to have less economic security than educated workers and have greater fear of what will happen to them if they\u8217\'20\'19re retaliated against, perhaps getting fired, for seeking to unionize. \u8220\'20\'1CRetaliation for blue-collar workers means they often have to find another job immediately to avoid being homeless, while white-collar workers might have more money saved up,\u8221\'20\'1D Smiley said.\par \par \uc2 For such reasons, Smiley said, \u8220\'20\'1Cit takes longer to get a majority of workers to get excited in blue-collar workplaces,\u8221\'20\'1D She added that this means unions need to provide \u8220\'20\'1Ca greater level of resources to offset the instability and fear of retaliation\u8221\'20\'1D that blue-collar workers face.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want higher-wage sector workers to continue organizing\u8211\'20\'13anyone who wants a union should get a union,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe intervention I would argue for is that we need to figure out more ways to invest in sustaining blue-collar workers who want to stick their necks out and unionize.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Labor leaders talk plenty of their ambitions to unionize new semiconductor plants and electric vehicle battery plants, but just one EV battery plant, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vindy.com/news/local-news/2022/12/ultium-workers-overwhelmingly-vote-to-unionize/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ultium Cells in Warren, Ohio, has unionized, in a 710-to-16 vote}}}\uc2  last December. The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  has vowed to unionize more such battery plants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust because we\u8217\'20\'19re not seeing many wins yet in blue-collar doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean things aren\u8217\'20\'19t happening \u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Cindy Estrada\uc2 , a former \uc2 UAW\uc2  vice-president who was recently named director of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcioconvention.org/news/building-the-movement-to-meet-the-moment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Transformational Organizing}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of stuff happening on the ground. I\u8217\'20\'19m excited about this moment.\u8221\'20\'1D That center will seek to spearhead and coordinate large, more innovative unionization campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Estrada voiced confidence that her center will work with various unions to organize thousands of workers in new jobs created by the infrastructure act, the Chips Act to encourage semiconductor production in the US, and the climate-change provisions of the Inflation Reduction Act. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re looking at how do we capture this moment right now when federal dollars are subsidizing whole industries,\u8221\'20\'1D Estrada said. She talked of \u8220\'20\'1Csectoral strategies\u8221\'20\'1D to unionize electric bus factories and battery plants as well as workers modernizing the electric grid and making schools more energy-efficient.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have this narrative about manufacturing that it\u8217\'20\'19s going to rebuild the middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D Estrada said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not going to happen unless workers have democracy in the workplace and an ability to bargain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With regard to unionizing lower-paid workers, Victor Narro, a UCLA professor of labor studies, says far more efforts should be undertaken to unionize fast-food, warehouse and car wash workers. \u8220\'20\'1CWe missed the opportunity to go deep and broad in those industries,\u8221\'20\'1D Narro said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to still try to figure out strategies for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said unions should run more campaigns like \uc2 SEIU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.labor.ucla.edu/what-we-do/research-tools/campaigns-and-research/justice-for-janitors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highly successful Justice for Jantitors effort}}}\uc2 , which unionized over 100,000 janitors in 29 cities, often using citywide efforts that targeted not just cleaning contractors, but wealthy building owners.\par \par \uc2 Narro acknowledged that lower-wage, less educated workers are often more reluctant to stick their necks out and fight for a union. \u8220\'20\'1CThey live on the balance,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re fearful of retaliation. We have to figure out how to have good strong laws to stop retaliation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joseph McCartin, a labor historian at Georgetown, said it was difficult to know for certain whether there is far more organizing of educated workers than blue-collar workers. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to pin down how much of this is our perception of what\u8217\'20\'19s happening on the ground,\u8221\'20\'1D McCartin said. (The white-collar efforts usually get more media attention.) \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of efforts going on among \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse workers in different parts of the country. While there\u8217\'20\'19s no new breakthrough, that work is going on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Richard Bensinger, a former \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  organizing director who helps oversee the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  unionization campaign, said the various campaigns often reinforce and encourage other efforts: \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers I talked to at a factory in Buffalo told me they were inspired by what\u8217\'20\'19s happened at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bensinger said that whether for white-collar workers or blue-collar ones, \u8220\'20\'1Cunionizing involves risk-taking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere should be a lot more organizing activity right now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy advice is to dig deep and spend money. We have to take advantage of this moment. This should be a springboard to massively more organizing. We should listen to what workers are telling us \u8211\'20\'13 this is a moment in history to organize.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230505ej55001gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
