\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Bernie Sanders unveils plan for $17-an-hour US minimum wage\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 724 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2023\par 18:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18In the richest country in the history of the world, nobody should be forced to work for starvation wages,\u8217\'20\'19 Vermont senator says\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders on Thursday announced a proposal to raise the federal minimum wage to $17 an hour, saying the potent inflation Americans have faced over the past two years makes it necessary for the government to institute higher wages for workers.\par \par \uc2 Sanders intends to next month formally introduce legislation raising the minimum wage over a five-year period to a level $2 higher than the $15 an hour Joe Biden and many Democrats have pushed for in recent years. But there is no sign of Republicans wavering in their opposition to the proposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result of inflation, $15 an hour back in 2021 would be over $17 an hour today,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders, an independent senator who caucuses with the Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the year 2023, in the richest country in the history of the world, nobody should be forced to work for starvation wages. That\u8217\'20\'19s not a radical idea. If you work 40-50 hours a week, you should not be living in poverty. It is time to raise the minimum wage to a living wage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congress has not approved a minimum wage increase since raising the level to $7.25 an hour in 2009, where it remains for workers in 20 states. Voters in several states and cities across the country have approved raising their minimum wage to $15 an hour, but progress on a national increase has remained elusive.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, Democrats attempted to raise the minimum wage to $15 an hour as part of a large spending bill intended to help the US economy recover from the Covid pandemic, but the effort failed, in part {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/03/05/democrats-15-minimum-wage-hike-473875"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 due to the defections}}}\uc2  of eight Democratic lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Biden later that year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/27/joe-biden-minimum-wage-raise-federal-contractors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed an executive order}}}\uc2  raising the minimum wage for federal contractors, which affected as many as 390,000 workers, but the president has not said if he supports the increase to $17 an hour. A White House spokesman did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 In the two years since, Americans have faced the highest inflation since the 1980s, with consumer price increases hitting an annualized peak of more than 9% in June 2022, though they have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/apr/12/cpi-inflation-rate-march-prices-fed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moderated in recent months}}}\uc2 . While workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/us-wage-growth-slows-4d4a328c345dd4a2e04fbc222d101ac7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also increased over that period}}}\uc2  in part because of a tight labor market, the pace has not kept up with inflation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a home healthcare worker, I make just $12 an hour. I worked in fast food for over 30 years and I never, never made $15 an hour. And now $15 isn\u8217\'20\'19t even enough for what we\u8217\'20\'19re going through today,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cookie Bradley, a founding member of the Union of Southern Service Workers, who joined Sanders in the announcement.\par \par \uc2 Although Sanders was supported by the heads of major labor groups the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  and \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 SEIU\uc2 ), he said little about how he planned to overcome objections both from Republicans and reluctant Democrats.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a popular issue. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s a state in the country where people do not believe we should raise the minimum wage. I would hope that every member of Congress understands that and there will be political consequences if they don\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans, who took control of the House of Representatives this year, have shown at best lukewarm enthusiasm for a minimum wage rise, and have instead focused on trying to convince Americans that Biden is to blame for the rapid inflation. In 2021, Republican senators introduce {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/26/republicans-minimum-wage-bills-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two proposals}}}\uc2 , one that would raise the federal minimum wage to $10 an hour, and another that would give a tax credit for workers who make less than $16.50 an hour. Neither went far in the Senate, which Democrats currently control.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 SEIU\uc2  president, \uc2 Mary Kay Henry\uc2 , said her millions of members would be keeping an eye on which lawmakers support Sanders\u8217\'20\'19s proposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to be watching any congressperson, senator or in the House, that dares to say that they are not going to vote yes for Senator Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 bill, because they need to be held accountable at the ballot box,\u8221\'20\'1D Henry said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230504ej54002bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
