\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Far-right California county\u8217\'20\'19s bid to hand count votes will cost millions\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano \par \uc2 739 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 April 2023\par 10:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The move to a costly and experimental hand-count system comes as half the workforce is readying to strike over wages\par \par \uc2 In Shasta county, a deep red enclave in far northern California, officials are intensifying their push to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/far-right-county-throws-out-voting-machines-with-nothing-to-replace-them"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replace voting machines}}}\uc2  with a costly and experimental hand-count system that could cost an additional $4m over two years.\par \par \uc2 The decision of the far-right majority on the region\u8217\'20\'19s governing body, the Shasta county board of supervisors, to press ahead with the controversial plan comes as half the county\u8217\'20\'19s workforce is preparing to strike over wages. Officials on the board recently said the county did not have enough money to pay requested wage increases for workers.\par \par \uc2 The move has deepened divisions in a small county where public spending budgets are tight, with critics denouncing the price tag of an overhaul based on lies about election fraud.\par \par \uc2 In a tense meeting that saw one county supervisor served with recall paperwork, the board\u8217\'20\'19s ultra conservative majority renewed their support for a system that will cost three times more than the voting machines the county previously used.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to have free and fair elections in Shasta county,\u8221\'20\'1D said Patrick Jones, the chair of the board of supervisors, at a meeting on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CApparently money seems to be more important than making sure our elections are fair.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The board of supervisors has pushed the rural county of 180,000 people into the national spotlight with its decision this year to upend the county\u8217\'20\'19s voting system without a replacement, and attempt to create a new system from scratch.\par \par \uc2 Conspiracy theorists who believe that voting machines helped to steal the presidency from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have seized on the county with high-profile figures in the movement, such as the MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell, offering their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/03/mike-lindell-shasta-county-california-dominion-voting-systems"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some in Shasta, which has became a hotbed for far-right politics in the pandemic years, have cheered the board\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 Since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s loss, a group of residents had spoken regularly at county meetings, urging the board to cut ties with \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 , the company at the center of baseless conspiracy theories about election fraud. They argued that the machines were a threat to elections both nationally and locally.\par \par \uc2 Their vision became a reality shortly after an ultra-conservative majority took hold of the board of supervisors and, against the advice of colleagues and elections staff, decided in a 3-2 vote to cut ties with Dominion and pursue a hand tally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have disenfranchised roughly 110,000 voters and that is truly the epitome of denying our residents their first amendment right and they should be outraged,\u8221\'20\'1D said supervisor Mary Rickert, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/far-right-county-throws-out-voting-machines-with-nothing-to-replace-them"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted against the decision}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meetings on the matter have drawn large crowds, including election deniers and dozens of residents who begged the county not to do away with Dominion machines, pointing out that the supervisors themselves had been elected by voters using the technology.\par \par \uc2 The official who oversees voting had warned against a hand-count system, arguing that it is \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptionally complex and error prone\u8221\'20\'1D and could cause the county to miss state elections deadlines, and ultimately disenfranchise voters.\par \par \uc2 Cathy Darling Allen, Shasta\u8217\'20\'19s registrar of voters, told officials in March the new system would require at least 1,200 additional temporary employees, funding to pay them, and a space large enough to accommodate them.\par \par \uc2 This week the county\u8217\'20\'19s deputy executive told the board that moving to a hand-count would increase costs by a minimum of $3.8m in the fiscal year 2024-2025, which she described as a conservative estimate.\par \par \uc2 But despite financial concerns and protests from residents, the county board has once again opted to move ahead with the effort, and this week agreed to fund seven new positions to implement it. Rickert, the supervisor, again urged the board to reverse its previous decision, which she deemed \u8220\'20\'1Creckless and irresponsible\u8221\'20\'1D and unsuccessfully tried to a call a vote to do so.\par \par \uc2 Her constituents are deeply concerned, she said recently.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had many people come up to me and say \u8216\'20\'18whats going on\u8217\'20\'19? These are people that are rock solid conservative as you will find \u8211\'20\'13 ranchers and farmers,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThose are the people who are most upset, they see total fiscal irresponsibility with their tax dollars.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230429ej4t0015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
