\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New York City home care aides push to end 24-hour shifts: \u8216\'20\'18Destroyed my body\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 954 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2023\par 14:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers receive wages only for 13 hours of work on their 24-hour shifts, with the remaining 11 hours amounting to unpaid labor\par \par \uc2 Zhu Nu Jun has worked as a home care aide in New York City for eight years, working three 24-hour shifts a week. That increased to four 24-hour shifts a week last year.\par \par \uc2 It can be brutal and intense work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had enough of these long hours of very difficult work that have destroyed my body,\u8221\'20\'1D she said \u8220\'20\'1CMy fingers are already deformed. I have a knee problem, my eyesight has worsened, my hair is falling out. I can\u8217\'20\'19t even pick up a pen with my right arm due to all the work of carrying patients and this has happened to many workers I know. Only New York City has the 24-hour one shift.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the tough labor is only part of the issue that she faces. Many home care workers in New York city also say that their industry is set up to practice large-scale wage theft, with some of their work hours effectively being unpaid.\par \par \uc2 Home care workers claim the 13 hours of pay they receive for 24-hour shifts are supposed to include at least five hours of uninterrupted sleep and meal breaks, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t occur given the lack of enforcement and often serious medical needs their patients have.\par \par \uc2 Jun says according to New York state department of labor calculations, she\u8217\'20\'19s actually owed $235,000 in unpaid back wages for work she has done on these shifts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt night, I can\u8217\'20\'19t sleep for even one hour. The patient, day and night, needs to get to the bathroom. I have to carry the patient to their wheelchair and then the bathroom,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Recently, home care workers in New York City protested outside city hall to demand a vote on a bill that would limit the number of hours that can be assigned to those who currently work 24-hour shifts and are only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/nys-highest-court-its-legal-to-pay-home-health-aide-workers-for-13-hours-of-a-24-hour-shift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compensated for 13 hours}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Around the US, only New York City has these shifts. This is exploitation\par \par \uc2 Zhu Nu Jun\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legistar.council.nyc.gov/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=5555482&GUID=C2F0BEF5-D16A-4A77-93E8-E514FB54ACA1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2 , which has a majority of support in the city council, has yet to receive a vote and workers are calling on the New York City council president, Adrienne Adams, to allow one. The legislation would limit the number of hours assigned to home care workers to 12-hour shifts.\par \par \uc2 Jun was one of the protesters outside New York city hall demanding a vote on legislation to ban the 24-hour shift exemptions for home care workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re glad this bill exists because it makes us feel like we\u8217\'20\'19re finally being treated like human beings,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CAround the US, only New York City has these shifts. This is exploitation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wage theft in the home care industry in the US is a rampant issue, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nelp.org/blog/home-care-workers-call-for-end-to-wage-theft/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high reports}}}\uc2  among workers of overtime violations, working without getting paid and minimum wage violations. Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://asamnews.com/2023/04/12/wage-theft-women-home-health-workers-new-york-intro-0175-2022/#:~:text=By%20all%20estimates%2C%20the%20amount,of%20nearly%20%24116%2C500%20per%20worker."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 554 wage theft }}}\uc2  violations filed with the New York department of labor from home care workers total over $64.5m, with estimates the industry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://asamnews.com/2023/04/12/wage-theft-women-home-health-workers-new-york-intro-0175-2022/#:~:text=By%20all%20estimates%2C%20the%20amount,of%20nearly%20%24116%2C500%20per%20worker."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 owes billions of dollars}}}\uc2  to home care workers for the unpaid 11 hours of 24-hour shifts.\par \par \uc2 Workers and advocates have criticized the use of 24-hour \u8211\'20\'13 shifts, calling it a racist and sexist practice permitting the exploitation of a workforce largely consisting of immigrant women of color.\par \par \uc2 Home care workers are paid through Medicaid funding, with worker advocates claiming the current system benefits insurance companies and home care agencies at the expense of the workers. Assemblyman Harvey Epstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/home-health-care-workers-call-hochul-end-24-hour-shifts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  it would cost Medicaid an additional $1bn a year to cover the cost of the rest of the 24-hour shift, money which he noted was being saved by Medicaid and the state off the backs of the workers not receiving pay for those hours.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe insurance companies and agencies benefit from this system. We don\u8217\'20\'19t know exactly how much money goes to the agencies and insurance companies,\u8221\'20\'1D said JoAnn Lum, an organizer with National Mobilization Against Sweatshops \u8220\'20\'1CThe attitudes to justify or rationalize these abusive conditions are part of a racist, sexist perspective in our society to maintain these 24-hour shifts that don\u8217\'20\'19t value or recognize the workers to address those conditions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Home care workers have been fighting for years to eliminate 24-hour shifts in New York City, impacting a workforce of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.phinational.org/wp-content/uploads/legacy/clearinghouse/PHI-495%20NY%20ExecSummary.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 130,000}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 2019, a court of appeals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/nys-highest-court-its-legal-to-pay-home-health-aide-workers-for-13-hours-of-a-24-hour-shift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  it was legal to pay home care workers for 13 hours out of 24-hour shifts, upholding a New York state department of labor exemption. The court decision overruled lower-court decisions from class action lawsuits filed in 2017 that deemed the exemption illegal.\par \par \uc2 After the ruling, a state bill to address the 24-hour shifts was introduced in 2021, but the bill did not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nyassembly.gov/mem/Harvey-Epstein/story/91855#:~:text=The%20bill%20prohibits%20this%20inhumane,a%20single%20hour%20for%20themselves."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 receive}}}\uc2  a vote in the state house or senate.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, home care workers were pushing for a 50% wage increase proposed in the Fair Pay for Home Care Act, but only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/ny-health-budget-only-partially-delivers-on-home-care-wages-and-coverage-for-undocumented-immigrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  a $3 raise to $18 an hour included in the New York state health budget.\par \par \uc2 Opponents to the city council legislation include the home care agency industry which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.littler.com/publication-press/publication/new-york-city-council-seeks-disrupt-home-care-industry-limiting-hours"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  the bill will worsen home care aide shortages and negatively impact healthcare of the elderly and disabled who rely on home care workers. 1199 \uc2 SEIU\uc2 , which represents home care workers, has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://documentedny.com/2022/09/13/24-hour-shifts-healthcare-new-york-199seiu/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  the city council legislation claiming they do so because they favor addressing the 24-hour shifts at the state level.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230423ej4n000ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
