\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US hotel workers face unwelcome guests: union busters hired by bosses\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,190 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par 09:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Consultants hired by \u8211\'20\'13 and staying at \u8211\'20\'13 Fairmont Sonoma Mission Inn & Spa to suppress workers\u8217\'20\'19 union organizing drive\par \par \uc2 In the heart of California\u8217\'20\'19s wine country, the Fairmont Sonoma Mission Inn & Spa offers guests access to on-site geothermal mineral pools, an exclusive golf club and farm-to-table dining.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike the Native Americans who revered the site as a sacred healing ground, you\u8217\'20\'19ll live in harmony with nature through vast open spaces, beautifully landscaped grounds, majestic redwood trees and inspiring sunsets,\u8221\'20\'1D boasts the resort\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fairmont.com/sonoma/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That purported serenity on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jun/20/california-native-americans-governor-apology-reparations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stolen Native American land}}}\uc2  has not extended to the workers at the luxury resort where union avoidance consultants hired by and staying at the hotel for the past several months have been trying to suppress their union organizing drive.\par \par \uc2 Late last year, workers started trying to organize a union with \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 2 in response to staffing issues that have persisted through the Covid-19 pandemic, stagnant pay as housing costs in the area have soared, and issues such as neglected infrastructure. Around 250 workers at the hotel would be included in the bargaining unit.\par \par \uc2 Workers say these issues had gone unaddressed for years until the hotel started rolling out changes to try to temper some of the grievances aired in support of the unionization effort. Amid these efforts in response to the union campaign the hotel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://olmsapps.dol.gov/query/orgReport.do?rptId=850230&rptForm=LM20Form"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hired}}}\uc2  several union avoidance consultants who have been staying at the hotel on and off since November 2022, surveilling workers, holding anti-union meetings and trying to dissuade workers from supporting the effort.\par \par \uc2 Tony Arguello, a banquet server at the resort for 10 years, had to move an hour away from the resort because rent in the Sonoma area has soared in recent years.\par \par \uc2 Arguello explained that right before the Covid-19 pandemic, the hotel hired a third-party firm to evaluate the efficiency of each employee, which he said resulted in the hotel consolidating jobs, adding extra duties to individual workers without any change in pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy co-workers and I tried to negotiate, negotiate and appeal to our managers and ask for solutions to real problems in our operations and we can\u8217\'20\'19t really get anywhere,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 When the union campaign first started at the hotel in October 2022, Arguello said he was brought into an office with a manager and told \u8220\'20\'1Cif you don\u8217\'20\'19t like it, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to be here\u8221\'20\'1D after he cited some of the issues workers had at the hotel in response to prodding by the manager over the start of the union campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving union busters in the hotel with great frequency, it\u8217\'20\'19s challenging because they have a megaphone and full access to employees, while people who are organizing, we have limited time, like on our break, when we can talk about this, and we can\u8217\'20\'19t have union organizers or reps in the hotel,\u8221\'20\'1D added Arguello.\par \par \uc2 But he said workers were still optimistic about gathering enough union authorization cards to file for and win a union election.\par \par \uc2 Several workers described the effect that the union avoidance consultants have had on the campaign and working conditions at the hotel. Among the consultants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://olmsapps.dol.gov/query/orgReport.do?rptId=850230&rptForm=LM20Form"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hired}}}\uc2  by the hotel are several with a record of opposing unionization efforts from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/article/news/union-organizers-and-workers-decry-union-busting-consulting-firms-hired-b/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quest Consulting}}}\uc2 , LKLS Consulting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/in/eduardo-padilla-4605b19a/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Libra Management Consulting}}}\uc2  and Lighto Labor.\par \par \uc2 According to a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/union-avoidance/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 , employers spend $433m per year on union avoidance consultants to bolster employer union-busting efforts.\par \par \uc2 Miriam Gonzalez, a housekeeper at the hotel for 17 years, said she pushed back against the union avoidance consultants who had been frequently approaching her and her co-workers in the hotel hallways, asking them why the hotel had all of a sudden implemented a new system to reduce the number of rooms each worker had to clean and introduced a wage increase early.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI asked him: \u8216\'20\'18Why are you doing this now, why have you become so friendly all of a sudden?\u8217\'20\'19 And he said it was because the company was scared of the union, that the threat of the union is there and that\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re doing this,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gonzalez.\par \par \uc2 She said the union avoidance consultants are a constant presence in the hotel. An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/10SiaSFdHD1uWVeNKo45060wrsyBCc7uz/view?usp=share_link"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-union flyer}}}\uc2  distributed to workers portrayed the union organizing drive as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdesperation\u8221\'20\'1D effort to gain members and charge dues.\par \par \uc2 We can see right through what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing. All that stuff we get it within a couple of months of trying to form a union\par \par \uc2 Banquet cook Aaron Brumley\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe union wants to bring to Sonoma the same \u8216\'20\'18fight\u8217\'20\'19 and divisive conflict they typically use in the city,\u8221\'20\'1D the flier claims.\par \par \uc2 The flier also claims consultants were hired just to explain the unionization process to workers, but workers say they have gone beyond doing that, given their ongoing presence in the hotel and their constant interrogation of workers.\par \par \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 2 has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/20-CA-313884"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  several unfair labor practice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/20-CA-310743"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges}}}\uc2  against the hotel alleging constant surveillance of union activity, threatening employees with loss of benefits for supporting the union, conferring new benefits and raises on workers, and soliciting and promising to resolve grievances to undermine the union effort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt first HR told us they were neutral, that the consultants were just laying out the process of unionizing. I thought they would go away after that, but instead they\u8217\'20\'19ve stayed,\u8221\'20\'1D added Gonzalez. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that creates fear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bobby Phillips, a front desk agent at the hotel, said he supported the union because his father had been a union member throughout his life and he had experienced the benefits and safety net that it had provided his family. He frequently has checked the union avoidance consultants in and out of the hotel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re still there now,\u8221\'20\'1D said Phillips. \u8220\'20\'1CI know a lot of other co-workers are annoyed by them bugging them and inhibiting their work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He criticized the hotel spending thousands of dollars to hire and put up the union avoidance consultants in the hotel in response to workers asking for neutrality.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s upsetting because it\u8217\'20\'19s deceptive to people who haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard about the union yet. I think they\u8217\'20\'19re tricking them into thinking it\u8217\'20\'19s a bad thing,\u8221\'20\'1D added Phillips.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Brumley, a banquet cook at the hotel for 11 years, claimed the banquet kitchen was finally remodeled in November 2022, once the union campaign was launched, after workers had been asking to get the kitchen fixed for years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnytime we asked for repairs, we were just literally ignored for years about things that needed to be done,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brumley. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can see right through what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing. People laugh about it, almost on a daily basis, the fake smiles, the pats on the back, the raises, all that stuff we\u8217\'20\'19ve been asking for this for 10 years and we get it within a couple of months of trying to form a union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Fairmont Sonoma Mission Inn & Spa did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230422ej4m0012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
