\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Many of us are struggling\u8217\'20\'19: why US universities are facing a wave of strikes\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 864 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2023\par 10:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Last year saw 15 strikes, the highest number of strikes in academia in at least 20 years, and the surge has continued into 2023\par \par \uc2 Thousands of workers at universities have gone on strike in 2023 amid new union contract negotiations in demand of pay increases that align with the effect high inflation rates have had on the cost of living.\par \par \uc2 The strikes are a continuation of wave of industrial action in higher education in the US last year. In late 2022, 48,000 graduate workers and post-doctoral researchers went on strike throughout the University of California system, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/10/university-of-california-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest strike}}}\uc2  in US higher education history. There were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/college-university-strike-wave-continues-its-swell-into-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15 academic strikes}}}\uc2  in the US in 2022, the highest number of strikes in academia in at least 20 years.\par \par \uc2 This uptick in strikes coincides with a surge in union organizing at US academic institutions. Since early 2022, graduate and undergraduate workers at 20 private academic institutions, representing over 25,000 workers, have won union elections filed with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This strike surge has continued into 2023. Around 700 graduate workers at \uc2 Temple University\uc2  in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.insidehighered.com/news/2023/03/14/temple-strike-ends-after-grad-students-accept-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on strike}}}\uc2  on 31 January before reaching a new union contract agreement in March 2023. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blockclubchicago.org/2023/01/23/uic-faculty-reach-deal-with-university-to-end-strike-after-winning-pay-raises-other-benefits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1,500 faculty members}}}\uc2  at University of Illinois Chicago went on strike in January 2023, winning a new contract after several days on strike.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rutgersaaup.org/media-resource-center/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Over 9,000}}}\uc2  faculty staff, adjunct lecturers, and graduate workers represented by Rutgers AAUP-AFT, Rutgers Adjunct Faculty Union and AAUP-BHSNJ went on strike at three campuses of \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2  in New Jersey starting on 10 April. The unions reached an agreement to end the strike on 15 April, which was the first strike in the school\u8217\'20\'19s 257-year history as union contract negotiations stalled after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/news/rutgers-faculty-strike-updates-timeline-20230410.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 months}}}\uc2  of bargaining without a contract.\par \par \uc2 The unions criticized Rutgers\u8217\'20\'19 role in soaring rent costs in the area given the university is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/19Ua7OpyS3zKzWvBgrQ90cq5YeddVVGfU/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest landlord}}}\uc2  in the New Brunswick, New Jersey, area. The university system has also been criticized for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.levernews.com/rutgers-puts-wall-street-before-teachers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poor investments}}}\uc2  of endowment funds and overspending on sports programs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the core of our fight is privileging just contracts for the most vulnerable workers and for us, this contract fight is the graduate students and the adjunct track, they are the lowest paid,\u8221\'20\'1D said Donna Murch, an associate professor of history and New Brunswick chapter president of Rutgers AAUP-AFT.\par \par \uc2 Murch estimated around 70% of the university had shut down due to the strike. She cited the strike and picket protests have received an outpouring of support from the community, students and local unions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re committed to a vision of intersectional organizing, where we figure out how to bring together a broad spectrum of people that how to organize, come together to fight for a broad spectrum of the workforce,\u8221\'20\'1D added Murch.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2  administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tapinto.net/towns/new-brunswick/articles/rutgers-holloway-holds-off-seeking-court-order-against-faculty-92cd9172-534c-4154-bc9b-9a47f147149e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened}}}\uc2  to take legal action in response to the strike through a court injunction over claims the strike was illegal but has held off on the action as the New Jersey governor, \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , has intervened and encouraged both sides to reach an agreement at the bargaining table. The president of Rutgers, Jonathan Holloway, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/news/rutgers-faculty-strike-updates-timeline-20230410.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the strike \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disappointing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://academeblog.org/2023/03/30/open-letter-to-rutgers-president-jonathan-holloway/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open letter}}}\uc2  from hundreds of scholars around the US was written in response to Holloway\u8217\'20\'19s threat of an injunction to halt the strike and asking him to reconsider his support of David Cohen as the university\u8217\'20\'19s lead negotiator, who has a poor relationship with labor unions following his tenure as former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s head of labor relations.\par \par \uc2 On 11 April, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wgntv.com/news/chicago-news/governors-state-university-faculty-on-strike-tuesday/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 280 faculty and staff}}}\uc2  at Governors State University in Illinois went on strike, joining {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox32chicago.com/news/johnson-joins-striking-faculty-staff-at-chicago-state-university-im-here-to-show-solidarity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around 100 faculty}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Chicago State University\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newschannel20.com/news/local/eiu-professors-consider-strike-amid-high-workload-outdated-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 300 faculty}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Eastern Illinois University\uc2  who began striking earlier this month in demand for fair pay increases.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://record.umich.edu/articles/court-denies-injunction-to-halt-graduate-workers-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost an attempt}}}\uc2  to obtain a court injunction against 2,300 graduate workers who began striking on 29 March, after a judge denied the request to issue an injunction to halt the strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe feel this a really precedent setting decision because public sector workers don\u8217\'20\'19t have the right to strike in the state of Michigan, it\u8217\'20\'19s illegal here, but the judge said injunctive relief is not appropriate and we hope it will strengthen the resolve for other workers and make them more willing to go on strike,\u8221\'20\'1D said Amir Fleischmann, contract committee chair for Graduate Employees\u8217\'20\'19 Organization 3550, which represents graduate workers at the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The workers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.geo3550.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Bargaining-Platform-Guide.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing }}}\uc2  for wage increases to $38,000 a year for graduate workers, additional support services for international students, parents, and students with disabilities, and stronger sexual harassment protections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of us are struggling,\u8221\'20\'1D added Fleischmann. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are on strike for a better university. This is a public institution that is supposed to serve the public. We\u8217\'20\'19re putting forward a vision of this university where no matter your economic class, no matter your social identity, you will come here and thrive as a graduate student.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230421ej4l001jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
