\par\par \uc2 Environment\par \b \uc2 The US needs 1m more electricians to hit climate goals. Can it recruit more women?\b0\par\par\uc2 Danielle Renwick \par \uc2 1,404 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par 13:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Women face barriers in the sector, including harassment and exclusionary unions, but they would help resolve a crucial labor shortage and could also help close the gender wage gap\par \par \uc2 As a child, Cora Saxton liked to make things \u8211\'20\'13 forts, whittled wood carvings, a flying saucer even \u8211\'20\'13 so when she became an electrician at 49, it felt like a perfect fit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI like the puzzle-solving and being able to look back at the end of the day and see the physical result of your hard work,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 This made it easier to bear some of the indignities \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Csubtle challenges\u8221\'20\'1D, she called them \u8211\'20\'13 of working in an overwhelmingly male field. \u8220\'20\'1CLittle stuff, like people walking by you to find the boss on the job\u8221\'20\'1D not realizing she was the boss, having tools and ladders taken out of her hands by pushy colleagues. \u8220\'20\'1CI call it \u8216\'20\'18roostering\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Saxton, who now works at the California non-profit Grid Alternatives, thinks she had it pretty easy compared with other women in her field. She\u8217\'20\'19s heard horror stories about threatening notes left in lockers, tools being stolen and destroyed \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Ceven people getting their hard hats peed in\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 The trades in general and electric work specifically are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/cps/cpsaat11.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly male}}}\uc2 . Only 2% of electricians are women, according to the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ). It\u8217\'20\'19s also a sector facing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://grist.org/energy/electrician-shortage-electrify-everything-climate-infrastructure-labor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 massive labor shortage}}}\uc2  as the country looks to transition away from fossil fuels and toward electrifying cars and buildings.\par \par \uc2 According to Rewiring America, an electrification non-profit, the United States will need {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rewiringamerica.org/policy/jobs-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1 million more electricians}}}\uc2  to make updates such as installing solar panels, heat pumps and electric vehicle charging stations to help the country meet its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/climate/#:~:text=Reducing%20U.S.%20greenhouse%20gas%20emissions,clean%20energy%20to%20disadvantaged%20communities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate goals}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those are a lot of job opportunities for something so badly needed. As author and journalist Bill McKibben put it in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/15/opinion/ezra-klein-podcast-bill-mckibben.html?showTranscript=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CIf you know a young person who wants to do something that\u8217\'20\'19s going to help the world and wants to make a good living at the same time, tell them to go become an electrician.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The gender wage gap\par \par \uc2 Getting more women working as electricians would help resolve a crucial labor shortage, but it could also help close the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2023/03/01/gender-pay-gap-facts/#:~:text=The%20gender%20gap%20in%20pay,%2D%20and%20part%2Dtime%20workers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gender wage gap}}}\uc2 . In 2021 the median annual pay for an electrician was just over $60,000, compared with about $45,000 for all occupations, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/construction-and-extraction/electricians.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . But some master electricians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/10/31/what-it-takes-to-earn-100k-a-year-as-an-electrician-in-new-york-city.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earn}}}\uc2  six-figure salaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are 80,000 openings for electricians each year on average over the next decade just to replace workers who either retire or transition to different jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sam Calisch, Rewiring America\u8217\'20\'19s head of research. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is all before the IRA\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the Inflation Reduction Act, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s signature climate bill, which is expected to increase demand for electricians by creating incentives for Americans to electrify their homes and buy electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Experts point to a lack of investment in technical schools and a culture that emphasizes four-year college degrees as the main path to a successful career as a few reasons there aren\u8217\'20\'19t enough electricians to meet demand. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t do a good job marketing ourselves as an industry in general, but particularly with women,\u8221\'20\'1D said Allie Perez, a plumber and founder of Texas Women in the Trades.\par \par \uc2 Perez, who has an eight-year-old daughter, founded Texas Women in the Trades in 2013 because she was tired of being the only \u8220\'20\'1Cyoung, brown woman\u8221\'20\'1D in most professional settings. She also wanted to help connect more young women like herself with well-paid jobs that they might not have envisioned for themselves. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t share [enough] stories of women in the trades to show that they are also moms, daughters, friends and cousins and that they are able to support their families on this kind of work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barriers to more women in the industry include widespread {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hechingerreport.org/the-jobs-where-harassment-and-discrimination-never-stopped/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harassment and abuse}}}\uc2 , lack of visibility, exclusionary unions, childcare and a lack of support for caregivers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat relationship-based, white male network \u8211\'20\'13 hiring, retaining and training people, and keeping people on the core crew from project to project \u8211\'20\'13 is the culture at most construction companies,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Connie Ashbrook\uc2 , a retired construction worker and co-chair of the National Taskforce on Tradeswomen\u8217\'20\'19s Issues. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re not friends with the boss, or if you\u8217\'20\'19re not friends with significant numbers of your co-workers, then you don\u8217\'20\'19t get to hear about the jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2009, Ashbrook was part of a successful effort to convince state officials to invest $2m in diversifying its highway construction workforce. Funds went toward pre-apprenticeship programs and supportive services, like childcare and accessible human resources contacts. Though gains in hiring more women were modest, a 2022 report on the initiative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/56c3899b4d088e9a22122e13/t/63cb0a5f9f46fe36db0e7848/1674250850068/Kelly+2022+Program+Evaluation+December+2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  it significantly improved retention rates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the highest-paid blue-collar work you can get without a college degree,\u8221\'20\'1D Ashbrook said. \u8220\'20\'1CNot having access to these careers keeps women in poverty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The childcare gap\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost childcare is set up to be very nine-to-five supportive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kate Krug, executive vice-president of \uc2 Nontraditional Employment for Women\uc2  (New), an organization in New York that trains and places women, transgender and non-binary people in the skilled construction, utility and maintenance trades. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you have to be out the door by 5am, you have to pay someone to sit with your kids until it\u8217\'20\'19s time to go to school.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said that\u8217\'20\'19s why her organization offers students wraparound services. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s having a program manager who makes sure that you are ready for job interviews \u8211\'20\'13 you know, do you have childcare? Do you need childcare? Do you have a backup to your childcare? Do you have backup to the backup of your childcare?\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Tonya Hicks, who grew up in public housing in Mississippi, had to overcome discrimination on the basis of her gender and race \u8211\'20\'13 she is Black \u8211\'20\'13 in her quest to become an electrician. (Only about 7% of electricians are Black, according to \uc2 BLS\uc2  data.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen and minorities have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.archives.gov/publications/prologue/1997/summer/american-labor-movement.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 systematically kept out}}}\uc2  of the unions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt began as racism, and then just as time goes on, you know, people hire who they know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As an apprentice, Hicks was often relegated to cleaning the on-site office trailers. When she struggled to find work locally, she drove from her home in Meridian, Mississippi, to sites in Jackson and Birmingham, leaving her young son with her mother for stretches at a time.\par \par \uc2 Her endurance paid off: in 2000, at age 28, she started her own firm, Power Solutions, in Atlanta. Today she has a staff of nine that specializes in renewable energy projects and home retrofits and, starting last year, began manufacturing electrical vehicle chargers. She also runs Women Do Everything, a networking group for women in the Stem field and blue-collar, male-dominated industries like hers.\par \par \uc2 Grid Alternatives, where Saxton works, recruits {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gridalternatives.org/what-we-do/workforce-development/women-in-solar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 female volunteers and trainees for solar installations}}}\uc2  and offers women-only trainings. \u8220\'20\'1CThat may encourage people who would otherwise perhaps be intimidated or just scared to try it,\u8221\'20\'1D Saxton said. \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, we need men to be mentors and to support women.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/06/17/fact-sheet-the-biden-harris-administration-launches-the-talent-pipeline-challenge-supporting-employer-investments-in-equitable-workforce-development-for-infrastructure-jobs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed}}}\uc2  a commitment to getting more women into the trades; in November, plans were announced to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commerce.gov/news/blog/2022/10/secretary-raimondo-calls-more-women-construction-industry-nabtu-tradeswomen-build"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 double}}}\uc2  the number of women working in the construction industry over the next 10 years.\par \par \uc2 The IRA climate legislation offers tax incentives for contractors to hire apprentices \u8211\'20\'13 something experts say could help reduce women\u8217\'20\'19s higher {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/WB/media/AdvancingOpportunitiesWomenthroughApprenticeship-jan2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropout rates}}}\uc2  from apprenticeship programs. In February, the program office connected to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/4346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chips and Science Act}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 legislation designed to boost the semiconductor industry in the US \u8211\'20\'13 released its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nist.gov/system/files/documents/2023/02/28/CHIPS_NOFO-1_Fact_Sheet_0.pdf#:~:text=On%20February%2028%2C%202023%2C%20the,U.S.%20economic%20and%20national%20security."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first funding opportunity}}}\uc2 , which stipulates that all applicants hoping to receive more than $150m must submit a plan to provide access to childcare for workers.\par \par \uc2 Hicks, the founder of Power Solutions, compared the task of transitioning the economy away from fossil fuels to the labor shortages during the second world war, when millions of women took jobs in factories. Of course, after the war, many women returned to their homes. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only difference now is that we\u8217\'20\'19re not going back,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 This article is co-published with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nexusmedianews.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nexus Media News}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230420ej4k00106\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
