\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Iowa state senate votes to allow children to work longer hours and serve alcohol\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Carrie Wong \par \uc2 446 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 April 2023\par 21:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In a move meant to combat a labor shortage, children under age 16 can now work six hours a day\par \par \uc2 In a pre-dawn session on Tuesday, the Iowa state senate voted to allow children to work longer hours and serve alcohol, the latest move by Republican-controlled statehouses to combat a labor shortage by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/11/us-child-labor-laws-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 loosening child labor laws}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Iowa bill would expand the number of hours that children under 16 can work from four to six a day, allow minors to work in previously prohibited industries if they are part of a training program, and allow 16- and 17-year\u8211\'20\'13olds to serve alcohol with a parent\u8217\'20\'19s permission.\par \par \uc2 It passed the state senate by a vote of 32-17, two Republicans joining every Democrat in opposition. The vote took place just before 5am, after protests and delay tactics by Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do know slavery existed in the past but one place it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist, that\u8217\'20\'19s in this bill,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adrian Dickey, the Republican responsible for shepherding the bill to passage, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iowacapitaldispatch.com/2023/04/18/senate-moves-child-labor-bill-after-all-night-debate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa Capital Dispatch}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt simply is providing our youth an opportunity to earn and learn, at the same timeframe as his classmates do, while participating in sports and other fine arts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats and labor advocates decried the bill, which they say will endanger children by allowing them to work in dangerous fields such as roofing, excavation and demolition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo Iowa teenager should be working in America\u8217\'20\'19s deadliest jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1648345426360414209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Zach Wahls, the senate minority leader. \u8220\'20\'1CIowa Republican politicians want to solve the \u8230\'20\'26 workforce crisis on the literal backs of children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Labor unions have held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/2023/02/27/amid-union-protests-iowa-lawmakers-consider-changes-to-child-labor-bill/69951320007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests}}}\uc2  against the bill. Charlie Wishman, president of the Iowa Federation of Labor, said efforts to loosen child labor laws around the US were \u8220\'20\'1Ca lazy way of dealing with the fact that certain states don\u8217\'20\'19t have enough workers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In March, the Arkansas governor, \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/08/arkansas-bill-child-labor-protections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed legislation}}}\uc2  to roll back child labor protections. Lawmakers in Ohio, Minnesota and Wisconsin are also considering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/11/us-child-labor-laws-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 loosening regulations}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCan we let kids be kids?\u8221\'20\'1D Wishman asked. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was about 120 years ago when we decided that we wanted to make sure that kids spent the majority of their time in school and not in a workplace, and especially not in a dangerous workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wishman cited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washington.edu/news/2011/02/09/working-more-than-20-hours-a-week-in-high-school-can-harm-grades-uw-researcher-finds/#:~:text=But%20students%20who%20began%20working,to%20their%20non%2Dworking%20peers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research}}}\uc2  that has found serious adverse effects for teenagers working more than 20 hours a week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese legislators don\u8217\'20\'19t care about that because it\u8217\'20\'19s not their kids,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis law is intended for somebody else\u8217\'20\'19s kids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230418ej4i00233\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
