\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18War of attrition\u8217\'20\'19: why union victories for US workers at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  have stalled\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,515 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par 08:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A year after a \u8216\'20\'18historic\u8217\'20\'19 victory in Staten Island, New York, hope for a wave of union victories is looking less momentous\par \par \uc2 A year ago, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in Staten Island, New York won a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D victory \u8211\'20\'13 overcoming a multimillion-dollar campaign by the multibillion-dollar corporation to win the right to organize \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first-ever union.\par \par \uc2 A year on from that victory \u8211\'20\'13 which labor leaders had hoped would trigger a wave of union victories \u8211\'20\'13 is looking less momentous and another union election win at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has remained elusive.\par \par \uc2 The company has continued to aggressively oppose unionization and organizing efforts at its warehouses. Critics charge US laws and issues at the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ), the federal agency charged with enforcing US labor law, have stymied progress for the new labor movement.\par \par \uc2 And in the meantime, the Amazon Labor Union (ALU) has suffered from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/21/business/amazon-labor-union.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internal strife }}}\uc2  and disagreements over future strategies and tactics. The Staten Island win made a star of the ALU president, Chris Smalls, who \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s management had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2020/apr/02/amazon-chris-smalls-smart-articulate-leaked-memo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 personally denigrated.}}}\uc2  Since then several union leaders have resigned in protest over Smalls\u8217\'20\'19 focus on traveling and public appearances and raised concerns that rushing union elections at other sites had come at the cost of focusing on the first union contract fight at JFK8.\par \par \uc2 Even the victory at the JFK8 warehouse in Staten Island still faces issues. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  appealed and delayed accepting the election results at JFK8, and has yet to begin bargaining with the Amazon Labor Union.\par \par \uc2 In the last year, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has opposed and fought subsequent union elections and union organizing campaigns at other sites and continues to fight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commondreams.org/news/amazon-off-duty-access-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges}}}\uc2  of unfair labor practices filed by workers involved in these campaigns. Charges have ranged from worker firings to workplace access for workers organizing.\par \par \uc2 The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/amazon-anti-union-spending-2022_n_6426fd1fe4b02a8d518e7010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent over $14.2m}}}\uc2  on anti-union consultants in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a very stark demonstration of all the flaws in the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  process and how the current law really plays into the hands of the anti-union employers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rebecca Givan, a professor of labor studies and employment relations at \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2 , on the long delays in resolving \uc2 NLRB\uc2  charges and getting \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to the bargaining table since the union election win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt demonstrates the objectives of the \uc2 National Labor Relations\uc2  Act are so far from being fulfilled, and to really rebound, labor law reform is needed,\u8221\'20\'1D Givan added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact employers can spend an unlimited amount to fight organizing and hide a great deal of that spending, the fact that workers who are organizing have no right to equal time, and the fact that employers can use every trick imaginable to delay, delay, delay and try to win a war of attrition. It demonstrates all of the holes in current labor law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re fighting to be able to work with respect and to be treated like a human being and not like a little robot\par \par \uc2 Anna Ortega\par \par \uc2 So far, no \uc2 Amazon\uc2  union campaign has come close to replicating the Staten Island victory. ALU came up short in union elections in Albany, New York, at another warehouse in Staten Island, and pulled a union election petition shortly after filing in California, though the union is currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unionizeamazonkcvg.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supporting}}}\uc2  a union campaign in Kentucky and at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s air hub outside Cincinnati, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Cause, another independent union organizing effort, has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://amazoncause.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing }}}\uc2  to organize workers at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in the Fayetteville, North Carolina, area since January 2022.\par \par \uc2 The Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union came up short in the rerun of a union election in March 2022 at an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in Bessemer, Alabama, after the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  ordered a new election due to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s misconduct during the first election. The second election results have yet to be finalized. Unfair labor practice charges are still being adjudicated and objections to the elections, which include 400 contested ballots that could sway the result, are yet to be decided.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, efforts to pass sweeping labor law reforms in Congress have stalled. The House passed the Joe Biden-backed pro-union Pro Act in 2021, but the bill did not reach a Senate vote. Reintroduced in the House and Senate this year, the act now faces a House under Republican control that is unlikely to vote in its favor.\par \par \uc2 With unionization efforts stalled, organizing at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has extended beyond the goal of formally winning union elections.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://athenaforall.org/#s3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Athena Coalition}}}\uc2 , consisting of numerous worker centers and non-profits, has focused on supporting workers at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and their efforts in garnering support for petitions and organizing walkouts supporting concrete demands at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  sites in Georgia, California, Illinois, Minnesota and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 The differing organizing avenues share similar goals; improving the grueling working conditions at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , from addressing high injury rates and poor treatment of injured workers, constant surveillance of workers and productivity pressures, the lack of job security and high turnover at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  sites, issues with adequate bathroom breaks, to lagging pay rates.\par \par \uc2 Anna Ortega has worked at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s KSBD air hub in San Bernardino, California, since June 2021. Initially, she declined to get involved in organizing efforts with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://warehouseworkers.org/wwrc_campaigns/worker-power/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inland Empire Amazon Workers United}}}\uc2  at the site in late 2021 but decided to do so after seeing the impact of a petition effort on compensating workers for site closures.\par \par \uc2 Since then, a group of workers at the site has petitioned, rallied and organized walkouts for improved heat protections for workers who work outside on the air ramps, improved policies for how injured workers are treated, and a $5-an-hour wage increase.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re fighting to be able to work with respect and to be treated like a human being and not like a little robot,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ortega.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Crane started working at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  at STL8 outside of St Louis, Missouri, as a packer in July 2021. A single mother with seven kids, two of whom also work at the same \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse, said she had seen numerous injuries and been injured on the job while trying to keep up with productivity demands at the warehouse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to lower our rate of work and give us a few more breaks, we need better accommodations for those who have injuries, and treat your employees like they actually care, because right now I don\u8217\'20\'19t feel like they care, they\u8217\'20\'19re more worried about getting as many boxes as they can,\u8221\'20\'1D said Crane. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s designed to give customers their packages fast. They don\u8217\'20\'19t care about their employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s designed to give customers their packages fast. They don\u8217\'20\'19t care about their employees\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Crane\par \par \uc2 She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.riverfronttimes.com/news/to-make-amazon-pay-st-peters-fulfillment-center-workers-will-strike-38948939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 participated }}}\uc2  in a one-day walkout in November 2022 as part of a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://makeamazonpay.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Make Amazon Pay}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D campaign to highlight working conditions and lagging wages at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Workers have also organized walkouts and petitions over health, safety and economic concerns at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouses in Georgia, Minnesota and Illinois.\par \par \uc2 In Joliet, Illinois, the worker center Warehouse Workers for Justice, has been organizing and supporting workers at the MDW2 \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers still have concerns about the way that the company is addressing health and safety,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tommy Carden, an organizer at Warehouse Workers for Justice. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Amazon\uc2  needs to start treating them with more respect, paying them better, and giving them a healthier and safer workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers at the site have held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/amazon-joliet-walkout/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walkouts}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wwj.salsalabs.org/supportmdw2workers/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests}}}\uc2  over racism at the site and to demand overtime compensation and better pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to be able to be paid fairly for their work, that means getting $25 an hour, a living wage,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maria Alfaro, organizing director at Warehouse Workers for Justice. \u8220\'20\'1CThey say despite \uc2 Amazon\uc2  relying on us, we\u8217\'20\'19re still invisible because we have low pay, unsafe work conditions and little job stability and so they want to see that change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, workers engaged in similar walkouts and protests in late 2022, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsbtv.com/news/local/metro-atlanta-amazon-warehouse-workers-accuse-company-unfair-labor-practices/DCOXYVTIBBBKFBHNFIXEC3FGLA/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  several unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Amazon\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s one of the companies that really talks about a big game about how good they treat their workers, and yet, when you actually talk to workers, it\u8217\'20\'19s the total opposite,\u8221\'20\'1D said Aliss Lugo, an organizer with United for Respect at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , who has been organizing \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in Georgia where workers have held walkouts and submitted petitions over working conditions and policies such as security issues in parking lots to better bathroom access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very difficult, but we\u8217\'20\'19re still doing it because I think it just shows how fed up and tired workers are of the situation at work,\u8221\'20\'1D added Lugo. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re looking for ways to bring their demands to the front, to put pressure on the company, from meeting with shareholders, talking to the press and elected officials, and to raise awareness. This really needs to be a community effort to uplift these workers and bring the issues that they\u8217\'20\'19re speaking about forward in any way possible outside of a traditional union election process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230408ej48000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
