\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Workers protest \uc2 Energizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to close Wisconsin plants\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 921 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2023\par 08:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The closure would lead to hundreds of job losses in a community of just under 3,000 people in Fennimore\par \par \uc2 Workers and union leaders are calling for a boycott of \uc2 Energizer\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the battery maker famous for its \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Energizer\uc2  bunny\u8221\'20\'1D adverts \u8211\'20\'13 over its plans to shut down plants in Wisconsin and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2023/03/teamsters-win-protections-at-energizer-continue-fight-to-save-jobs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 move}}}\uc2  jobs offshore to Singapore, the UK, and a non-union plant in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Using the hashtag #BadBunny the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  called this week for a protest boycott. \u8220\'20\'1CThe name of their company is a joke. The only thing they are \u8216\'20\'18energizing\u8217\'20\'19 is another economy in another country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Teamsters general president Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien.\par \par \uc2 Easter is coming. One {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BadBunny?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BadBunny}}}\uc2  may not be celebrating\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ExposeEnergizer?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ExposeEnergizer}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BoycottTheBunny?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BoycottTheBunny}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MMRyRCafEm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MMRyRCafEm}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Teamsters (@Teamsters) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Teamsters/status/1643659871038865410?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In December 2022, Chris Udelhoven, who has worked at \uc2 Energizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Fennimore, Wisconsin plant for 43 years in various positions, said workers were informed via a short paragraph that \uc2 Energizer\uc2  planned to shut down the plant and another in Portage, Wisconsin over the next 18 to 24 months, a move that would eliminate around 600 jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone was in total shock,\u8221\'20\'1D said Udelhoven. \u8220\'20\'1COur workers come from all the surrounding counties. Many people have other family members who work here. It\u8217\'20\'19s a big hit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said her sister also works at the plant, with the job losses impacting surrounding businesses in the town of Fennimore, which has a population of just under 3,000 people, hitting friends and families hard.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to stay here in Wisconsin, we don\u8217\'20\'19t want them leaving here, we want the jobs to stay here where they are. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know where all these people are going to find jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D added Udelhoven. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are continuing to fight to keep these plants open, getting the communities involved into that fight with us, contacting government officials, anybody they can to help keep these facilities open.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rob Krantz, who owns and operates Krantz Auto Parts in Fennimore, Wisconsin and used to work at the plant under RayoVac before \uc2 Energizer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bizjournals.com/stlouis/news/2019/01/02/energizer-now-owns-competing-rayovac-batteries.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acquired}}}\uc2  the company in 2018, pulled all \uc2 Energizer\uc2  products from his store in protest after the plant shutdown announcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re a small rural community that is going to lose over 300 jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D said Krantz. \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be devastating to every business in our town, including mine. All I see here by the move is more corporate greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Offshoring has been a contentious political issue as manufacturing in the US has experienced steep job losses in recent decades, decimating communities throughout the midwest. After an initial decline at the beginning of the Covid-19 pandemic, there are currently just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/CES3000000001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under 13m manufacturing jobs}}}\uc2  in the US, a slight increase from pre-pandemic numbers.\par \par \uc2 The safety net for workers impacted by offshoring, the Trade Adjustment Assistance program, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/20/business/economy/trade-adjustment-assistance-jobs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lapsed}}}\uc2  due to a lack of funding by Congress in July 2022. The scheme covered 107,454 workers impacted by offshoring in 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is corporate greed at its worst,\u8221\'20\'1D said Teamsters eastern region vice-president Rocco Calo. \u8220\'20\'1CWe look at what\u8217\'20\'19s happened with supply chains, with goods being transported, the problems that we have, it makes no sense to me that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to bring jobs offshore, and then transport the goods back into this country. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s a really smart business move.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Teamsters have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2023/03/teamsters-win-protections-at-energizer-continue-fight-to-save-jobs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized }}}\uc2 Energizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision given the $10m in public subsidies the company has received since 1999 in six states and ongoing federal contracts \uc2 Energizer\uc2  has with the US military and Department of Veterans Affairs.\par \par \uc2 The union pointed to \uc2 Energizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s solid financial performance. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2023/03/teamsters-win-protections-at-energizer-continue-fight-to-save-jobs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  a gross profit of $1.1bn in 2022 and paid out $93m to shareholders through dividends in 2022. In August 2021, \uc2 Energizer\uc2  entered an agreement to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://seekingalpha.com/news/3728739-energizer-enters-into-75-million-share-repurchase-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spend $75m }}}\uc2  on stock buybacks. \uc2 Energizer\uc2  CEO \uc2 Mark LaVigne\uc2  received an increase in total compensation from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.execpay.org/news/energizer-holdings-inc-2021-compensation-630"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  $6m }}}\uc2  in 2021 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.salary.com/ENERGIZER-HOLDINGS-INC-Executive-Salaries.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  over $9m}}}\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The Teamsters have negotiated with \uc2 Energizer\uc2  on economic protections for workers impacted by the shutdowns, including extended health coverage, severance, and set schedules to retain workers through 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe made it very clear to \uc2 Energizer\uc2  it was our goal to keep these plants open,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bryan Rademacher, President of Local 695. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to do everything we can in hopes we can do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  of Wisconsin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=1196115544603393"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2 Energizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to close the plants in the state in a recent Senate help committee meeting, noting that the closures came just after \uc2 Energizer\uc2  had requested government funds for research and development. She has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.baldwin.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/baldwin_letter_to_ftc_on_energizer_acquisition.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  requested}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  to scrutinize \uc2 Energizer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acquisition of Rayovac in 2018 over the plant closures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m disturbed by a trend that I\u8217\'20\'19m seeing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Baldwin. \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems to me that when seeking support from the government, these billion dollar corporations talk up their American facilities and workers, all the while, some of these corporations, like \uc2 Energizer\uc2 , are making plans to move a union facility to a non-union state or foreign country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Energizer\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CLast week, we entered into an agreement with the union which provides for a package that includes severance, health insurance coverage and job placement assistance. As we\u8217\'20\'19ve said from day one, our colleagues are our main concern, and we will continue focusing on them. We are pleased that negotiations with the union have concluded so our colleagues can have the clarity they expect and deserve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230407ej47000p4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
