\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Wall Street Journal reporter arrested in Russia\b0\par\par\uc2 Vivian Ho and Simon Jeffery \par \uc2 1,345 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 March 2023\par 12:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Evan Gershkovich is the first reporter for a US news outlet to be arrested on espionage charges in Russia since the cold warDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal reporter Evan Gershkovich has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/30/russia-arrests-wall-street-journal-reporter-on-espionage-charges-evan-gershkovich"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested on espionage charges}}}\uc2 , Russia\u8217\'20\'19s top security agency has said \u8211\'20\'13 the first reporter for a US news outlet to be arrested on espionage charges in Russia since the cold war.\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich had been detained in the Ural Mountains city of Ekaterinburg while allegedly trying to obtain classified information, the federal security service (FSB) said.\par \par \uc2 The security service alleged that Gershkovich \u8220\'20\'1Cwas acting on the US orders to collect information about the activities of one of the enterprises of the Russian military-industrial complex that constitutes a state secret\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal said it \u8220\'20\'1Cvehemently denies\u8221\'20\'1D the allegations.\par \par \uc2 My friend and thoroughly professional journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/evangershkovich?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @evangershkovich}}}\uc2  has been arrested by the FSB on obviously bogus espionage charges. Journalism is not a crime. Evan should be released immediately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QcYFkOECKg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QcYFkOECKg}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Pjotr Sauer (@PjotrSauer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PjotrSauer/status/1641350845202677762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich\u8217\'20\'19s\par \par \uc2 arrest comes amid bitter tensions between Moscow and Washington over the fighting in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich could face up to 20 years in prison if convicted of espionage.\par \par \uc2 Fox News chief called factchecks of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election lies \u8216\'20\'18bad business\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The top executive at Fox News was furious one of the network\u8217\'20\'19s reporters was factchecking Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims about the 2020 election, writing in a December 2020 email that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/29/fox-news-trump-fact-check-election-lies-dominion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it was \u8220\'20\'1Cbad business\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Suzanne Scott, the chief executive of Fox News, was responding in early December 2020 to an on-air factcheck by Eric Shawn, one of the network\u8217\'20\'19s anchors. \u8220\'20\'1CThis has to stop now,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote to Meade Cooper, another Fox executive. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is bad business and there clearly is a lack of understanding [sic] what is happening in these shows. The audience is furious and we are just feeding them material. Bad for business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The email emerged as part of a tranche of internal communications obtained by the voting equipment company Dominion in its $1.6bn defamation lawsuit against Fox. Dominion displayed a copy of the message in a court hearing last week as its lawyers argued that Fox knowingly aired false statements about Dominion because it was concerned about losing viewers to rival networks such as \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  and One America News (OAN). The Guardian obtained a copy of the message and the slideshow that was presented in court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Fox News spokesperson said Scott\u8217\'20\'19s objection in the email was not about pushing back on election claims. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about factchecking \u8211\'20\'13 the issue at hand is one host calling out another,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Paris breathes easier as refuse workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike called off and rubbish cleared\par \par \uc2 The smell of spring is once again in the air in Paris. It makes a change from the stench of overflowing bins that had hung over the French capital for the last three weeks after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/29/paris-breathes-easier-as-refuse-workers-strike-called-off-and-rubbish-cleared"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refuse collectors went on strike}}}\uc2  and up to 10,000 metric tonnes of festering rubbish piled up on the streets.\par \par \uc2 Hours after the CGT trade union announced it was suspending the industrial action and lifting a blockade of incinerators serving the city, much of the rubbish had gone.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The strike, part of a wave of protests and industrial action against \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pension law, was reportedly called off after the number of refuse collectors taking part dwindled. Strikers in France lose their wages when they stop work, and strike funds, mostly financed by donations, are insufficient to compensate for lost pay.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Union leaders said they would discuss resuming more powerful industrial action in the future if the government does not revoke a new law raising the official retirement age to 64 and requiring workers to have contributed to the system for longer to be eligible for a full pension. The CGT union has called on all members to take part in another day of national action next Thursday, 6 April.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has a respiratory infection and will need to spend \u8220\'20\'1Ca few days\u8221\'20\'1D in hospital for treatment, following what the Vatican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/29/pope-francis-taken-hospital-respiratory-infection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said were breathing difficulties}}}\uc2 . The Vatican initially said the checkup had been scheduled, but Italian media questioned that, saying a TV interview with the pope scheduled for Wednesday afternoon had been cancelled at the last moment. The Vatican said tests showed he did not have Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The governor of Kentucky has said deaths are expected after two US army Black Hawk helicopters crashed during a routine training mission over the state. Crew members were flying two HH-60 Black Hawk helicopters, operated by the 101st Airborne Division, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/two-us-army-black-hawk-helicopters-crash-kentucky-training-mission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crashed at about 10pm on Wednesday in Trigg county}}}\uc2 , Fort Campbell\u8217\'20\'19s public affairs office said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Strict rules on hairstyles at schools in Japan have attracted criticism after a teenager was separated from other students at a graduation ceremony because he had plaited his hair into cornrows to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/30/japan-school-stirs-debate-over-hairstyle-rules-after-boy-with-cornrows-separated-from-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  pay tribute to his Black heritage.}}}\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day:\par \par \uc2 carbon capture and storage projects could reduce the cost of tackling the climate crisis by 70%\par \par \uc2 Carbon capture and storage (CCS) is a group of technologies that can capture the carbon dioxide produced by major factories and power plants \u8211\'20\'13 preventing them from reaching the atmosphere and contributing to global heating \u8211\'20\'13 then transport them, bury them or reuse them.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 International Energy Agency\uc2 , CCS projects could reduce global carbon dioxide emissions by almost a fifth and reduce the cost of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/mar/30/what-is-carbon-capture-usage-and-storage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tackling the climate crisis by 70%.}}}\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Mediterranean diet \u8216\'20\'18can reduce heart attacks in people at higher risk\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A Mediterranean diet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2023/mar/29/mediterranean-diet-can-reduce-heart-attacks-in-people-at-higher-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can lower the risk of a heart attack}}}\uc2 , stroke or early death for hundreds of millions of people who have an increased possibility of cardiovascular disease, a global review of evidence suggests.\par \par \uc2 A diet rich in olive oil, nuts, seafood, whole grains and vegetables has previously been linked to a number of benefits, and its effectiveness in helping healthy people to live longer is well known.\par \par \uc2 However, until now there has been limited evidence of how it might help those at increased risk of cardiovascular disease. These include hundreds of millions of people living with obesity, type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure or high cholesterol, and those who are physically inactive, smoke or consume harmful levels of alcohol.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: how Timothy Snyder became the leading interpreter of our dark times\par \par \uc2 Historians are not supposed to make predictions but the Yale professor Timothy Snyder has become known for his dire warnings \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/30/how-timothy-snyder-became-the-leading-interpreter-of-our-dark-times-putin-trump-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many of them have been proven correct}}}\uc2 , writes Robert P Baird.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Ice, ice baby\par \par \uc2 Melting ice around Antarctica will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/30/melting-antarctic-ice-predicted-to-cause-rapid-slowdown-of-deep-ocean-current-by-2050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cause a rapid slowdown}}}\uc2  of a major global deep ocean current by 2050 that could alter the world\u8217\'20\'19s climate for centuries and accelerate sea level rise, according to scientists.\par \par \uc2 Their research suggests if greenhouse gas emissions continue at today\u8217\'20\'19s levels, the current in the deepest parts of the ocean could slow by 40% in only three decades.\par \par \uc2 This, the scientists said, could generate a cascade of impacts that could push up sea levels, alter weather patterns and starve marine life of a vital source of nutrients.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Creating a sustainable surf paradise\par \par \uc2 Locals in Tarfaya, a tiny Moroccan town just across the strait from the tourism hotspot that is the Canary Islands, are determined to make their small fishing port as popular as the Spanish archipelago.\par \par \uc2 How? Through surfing. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the Canaries you can hardly surf because it\u8217\'20\'19s so crowded,\u8221\'20\'1D said surfing instructor Salim Maatoug. \u8220\'20\'1CHere in Tarfaya we have 300km [200 miles] of waves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230330ej3u0018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
