\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Morning Mail: public sector pay push after NSW Labor win, the rise of AI recruiters, US tornado deaths\b0\par\par\uc2 Charlotte Graham-McLay \par \uc2 1,050 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2023\par 20:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Want to get this in your inbox every weekday? Sign up for the Morning Mail here, and finish your day with our Afternoon Update newsletter\par \par \uc2 Good morning. We have plenty of analysis from the New South Wales election for you this morning as Australia\u8217\'20\'19s mainland is now wall-to-wall Labor. Counting resumes today with plenty of seats still in doubt, but not the result. The incoming premier, \uc2 Chris Minns\uc2 , is being urged to lift public sector wages and overhaul working conditions as a first priority. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a golden opportunity for a new government, a young government, to look at what the future can be,\u8221\'20\'1D a \uc2 Health Services Union\uc2  spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, survivors of clergy abuse say delays to their cases are \u8220\'20\'1Cgutless\u8221\'20\'1D, we dig into the artificial intelligences that may be determining your chances in a job application, and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deal to store nuclear weapons in Belarus makes the state a nuclear hostage, Ukraine says.\par \par \uc2 Australia\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 NSW election |\par \par \uc2 Chris Minns{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/mar/27/golden-opportunity-nsw-labor-under-pressure-to-deliver-promised-public-sector-wage-rises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will face immediate pressure from union leaders}}}\uc2  to come good on his promise to lift public sector wages. \uc2 Matt Kean\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/mar/26/matt-kean-rules-himself-out-of-contention-to-be-the-next-leader-of-the-nsw-liberal-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled himself out}}}\uc2  of the NSW Liberal leadership. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/mar/27/nsw-election-trends-a-decisive-labor-win-uneven-swings-and-a-large-crossbench"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Ben Raue\u8217\'20\'19s analysis}}}\uc2  of a \u8220\'20\'1Cdecisive\u8221\'20\'1D Labor win. Minor parties {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/mar/27/legalise-cannabis-and-independents-buoyed-by-nsw-election-result-despite-no-teal-wave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are still on the hunt}}}\uc2  as vote-counting continues.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Clergy abuse |\par \par \uc2 Survivors of abuse by clergy and their families have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/mar/27/its-gutless-clergy-abuse-survivors-and-their-families-outraged-by-legal-stays-that-thwart-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried as \u8220\'20\'1Cgutless\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  the legal stays that thwart their civil claims.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robot recruiters |\par \par \uc2 A third of Australian companies rely on artificial intelligence to help them hire the right person. But studies show it\u8217\'20\'19s not always a benign intermediary. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/mar/27/robot-recruiters-can-bias-be-banished-from-ai-recruitment-hiring-artificial-intelligence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can bias ever be banished from AI?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Family violence |\par \par \uc2 Domestic violence shelters in Queensland {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/mar/27/unprecedented-domestic-violence-shelters-reach-capacity-amid-queensland-housing-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are struggling to make space for new arrivals}}}\uc2  due to the housing crisis, with some women staying in refuges for years.\par \par \uc2 World\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine war |\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/26/russia-accused-of-taking-belarus-nuclear-hostage-missile-deal-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused Russia of destabilising Belarus}}}\uc2  and making its smaller neighbour into \u8220\'20\'1Ca nuclear hostage\u8221\'20\'1D after \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to station tactical nuclear weapons on Belarusian territory.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Big twister |\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/mississippi-tornado-biden-declares-emergency-after-deadly-storm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared a federal emergency}}}\uc2  for swathes of Mississippi hit by a devastating tornado as rescue workers continued to search for survivors. The death toll from catastrophic storms in parts of the US\u8217\'20\'19s deep south has reached at least 26 people.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  tanks |\par \par \uc2 The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/mar/26/elon-musk-twitter-value-leaked-memo-less-than-half-paid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is worth less than half of what Elon Musk paid for it six months ago}}}\uc2 , having lost more than A$30bn in value, according to calculations based on a leaked memo from the billionaire.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asylum seekers |\par \par \uc2 At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/26/refugees-trying-to-reach-italy-die-after-boat-sinks-off-coast-of-tunisia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 29 people from sub-Saharan Africa died}}}\uc2  while trying to reach Italy after two boats carrying them across the Mediterranean sank off the coast of Tunisia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trans rights |\par \par \uc2 The anti-trans activist known as Posie Parker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/25/anti-trans-activist-posie-parker-ends-new-zealand-tour-after-violent-protests-erupt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelled a planned Wellington event and left New Zealand}}}\uc2  after chaotic and at times violent protests that ended her appearance in Auckland before she began speaking.\par \par \uc2 Full Story\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s kids are hooked on vapes \u8211\'20\'13 what are we doing about it?\par \par \uc2 The health minister has accused the vaping industry of creating a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew generation of nicotine addicts\u8221\'20\'1D amid rising reports of vaping addiction in teenagers and nicotine poisoning in toddlers. Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s medical editor, Melissa Davey, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2023/mar/27/australias-kids-are-hooked-on-vapes-what-are-we-doing-about-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explores what Australia\u8217\'20\'19s vaping crackdown \u8211\'20\'13 expected within the year \u8211\'20\'13 could look like}}}\uc2 , and the impact of vaping on kids.\par \par \uc2 In-depth\par \par \uc2 Held every night over the month of Ramadan, food stalls at an annual market in Sydney sell everything from camel burgers to tandoori chicken, sweets including knafeh and drinks including Kashmiri tea and sahlab. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/mar/26/ramadan-2023-lakemba-night-markets-haldon-street-nights-festival-sydney-australia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mostafa Rachwani visits the Lakemba markets}}}\uc2  and, while he hears their growth from a low-key gathering to a full-scale festival has been welcomed by some, while others lament that \u8220\'20\'1Cit isn\u8217\'20\'19t a Muslim event any more\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Not the news\par \par \uc2 The ocean of information that exists on brain health is so deep that sifting through it all can be its own brainteaser. Is it really all about sauerkraut? And do those brain training games do anything? Dr \uc2 Ginni Mansberg{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/mar/27/excellent-evidence-that-this-works-how-mind-experts-protect-their-brains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaks to 22 mind experts from around the world and shares their tips}}}\uc2  from sleep to supplements.\par \par \uc2 The world of sport\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Australian rugby |\par \par \uc2 Hooker Brandon Smith has questioned whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/mar/26/joseph-suaalii-wont-help-wallabies-beat-all-blacks-says-roosters-teammate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rugby Australia\u8217\'20\'19s decision to sign his Sydney Roosters teammate Joseph Suaalii}}}\uc2  on a big-money contract will move the Wallabies any closer to their former glory.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 AFL |\par \par \uc2 Western Bulldogs forward Jamarra Ugle-Hagan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/mar/26/afl-to-investigate-alleged-racial-abuse-aimed-at-bulldogs-jamarra-ugle-hagan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was allegedly the target of \u8220\'20\'1Charmful and abhorrent racist remarks\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  from a St Kilda fan, in a case that has sparked an AFL investigation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Twenty20 cricket |\par \par \uc2 South Africa have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/mar/26/south-africa-chase-down-west-indies-in-record-breaking-t20-international"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 produced the highest successful Twenty20 international run chase}}}\uc2  to defeat West Indies in a remarkable contest at Centurion in which Johnson Charles and Quinton de Kock also made history.\par \par \uc2 Media roundup\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smh.com.au/politics/nsw/doomed-from-the-start-how-the-liberal-campaign-went-from-bad-to-worse-20230326-p5cvc7.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoomed from the start\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , reads the Sydney Morning Herald\u8217\'20\'19s analysis of the Liberals\u8217\'20\'19 election defeat. Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s premier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theage.com.au/politics/victoria/china-bound-andrews-told-to-stay-in-his-lane-amid-call-for-trip-transparency-20230326-p5cvab.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daniel Andrews, flies to China today}}}\uc2  but has been criticised for not releasing his itinerary or inviting the media to scrutinise the four-day visit, according to the Age. And Northern Territory News reports that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ntnews.com.au/truecrimeaustralia/police-courts-nt/nt-corrections-breaks-record-for-prison-population-police-watch-houses-used-for-overflow/news-story/20fe02ddd415139d5d743df73ae015e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the NT\u8217\'20\'19s prison population has surged}}}\uc2  to an all-time high, with 1% of the population behind bars.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening today\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Oliver Schulz |\par \par \uc2 A bail hearing will be held in Sydney for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/20/former-sas-soldier-oliver-schulz-arrested-alleged-war-crime-accused-of-killing-afghan-civilian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former SAS soldier charged with the war crime of murder}}}\uc2  over the killing of an Afghan civilian.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Charlie Teo |\par \par \uc2 The Sydney neurosurgeon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/feb/20/charlie-teo-denies-lying-to-inquiry-over-surgeries-that-left-patients-with-brain-injuries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will return to a disciplinary hearing}}}\uc2  to face questions about two surgeries.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive this Morning Mail update to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/sep/23/morning-mail-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up-inbox-subscribe?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 . And finish your day with a three-minute snapshot of the day\u8217\'20\'19s main news. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/oct/13/afternoon-update-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for our Afternoon Update newsletter here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prefer notifications? If you\u8217\'20\'19re reading this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/ng-interactive/2018/may/15/the-guardian-app?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in our app}}}\uc2 , just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/guardian-australia-s-morning-mail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 click here and tap \u8220\'20\'1CGet notifications\u8221\'20\'1D on the next screen}}}\uc2  for an instant alert when we publish every morning.\par \par \uc2 Brain teaser\par \par \uc2 And finally, here are the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s crosswords to keep you entertained throughout the day \u8211\'20\'13 with plenty more on the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Puzzles app for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/app/id1487780661?mt=8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iOS}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=uk.co.guardian.puzzles&hl=en_GB&gl=US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Android}}}\uc2 . Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16500"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/29026"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230326ej3q001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
