\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers at over 100 US stores walk out ahead of shareholder meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 367 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par 14:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers hold protest in Seattle outside of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 headquarters in response to the company\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive anti-union efforts\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers at over 100 stores around the US walked out on Wednesday ahead of the company\u8217\'20\'19s annual shareholder meeting and held a protest in Seattle outside \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 headquarters.\par \par \uc2 The actions were launched in response to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 aggressive anti-union efforts against worker organizing, which have included allegations of firing dozens of workers in retaliation for union organizing, intimidation, store closures, withholding benefits, schedule cuts and delays in bargaining a first union contract. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has denied or rejected all allegations and charges of labor law violations.\par \par \uc2 More than 7,500 workers at over 280 stores in the US have won union elections, but the union campaign has slowed down since taking off in early 2022 amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/22/starbucks-amazon-workers-union-drive-retaliation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks\u8217\'20\'19 opposition.}}}\par \par \uc2 The actions come a week ahead of the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  chairman and former CEO Howard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/mar/07/howard-schultz-testify-senate-starbucks-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schultz\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled }}}\uc2  testimony before the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  health, education, labor, and pensions (Help) committee over the company\u8217\'20\'19s union busting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas like me are the ones who keep our stores running. We remember our customers\u8217\'20\'19 regular orders, make the lattes, clean up spills, and are often the bright spot of our customers\u8217\'20\'19 days. We are the heart and soul of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sarah Pappin, a Seattle Starbucks worker. \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of celebrating the law-breaking former CEO hellbent on silencing us, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  should respect our right to organize and meet us at the bargaining table. We are \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , and we deserve better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the shareholders\u8217\'20\'19 meeting, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers are asking shareholders to vote to approve a resolution for a third-party assessment of the company\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assets-global.website-files.com/5ecd0982c9d00e2865ce6691/63248b3fe565a97b35be665d_Starbucks%20Worker%20Rights%20Commitment%20Proposal%20FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing}}}\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is violating its own commitments in its global human rights statement on collective bargaining rights and non-interference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  celebrates their provenance and record profits this week, my partners have to deal with the reality that we are being nickel-and-dimed to extract as much labor as cheaply as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maria Flores, who has worked at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in Queens, New York, for three years.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230322ej3m001y3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
