\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Hard to ignore Julie Su\u8217\'20\'19: Biden\u8217\'20\'19s labor secretary pick fights for confirmation\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,564 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 March 2023\par 15:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Supporters fear Su, the deputy labor secretary, might have a hard time getting the needed Senate votes as some business groups oppose her nomination\par \par \uc2 Julie Su has come a long way since she first made headlines in 1995 when she, then just 26 years old, was lead lawyer for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.dol.gov/2021/08/02/what-the-el-monte-case-means-to-me"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 72 Thai workers who were essentially kept in slavery}}}\uc2 , toiling 18 hours a day at a sweatshop just outside Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Last week Joe Biden nominated Su to be secretary of labor, the government\u8217\'20\'19s top labor position, a move that many labor, immigrant and women\u8217\'20\'19s groups vigorously cheered, while a few business groups \u8211\'20\'13 but not many \u8211\'20\'13 opposed the nomination. Now some supporters fear that she might have a hard time mustering the needed votes in the Senate to be confirmed.\par \par \uc2 Su, the 54-year-old daughter of immigrants, has served as deputy labor secretary since 2021, having been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/transactional/senate-confirms-calif-labor-secretary-su-dols-no-2-spot-2021-07-13/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 narrowly confirmed 50 to 47}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a huge fan,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the nation\u8217\'20\'19s main labor federation. \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine someone more prepared. She\u8217\'20\'19s been working hand in glove with \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the current labor secretary, who is leaving to head the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/02/16/1155348338/labor-secretary-marty-walsh-resigns-nhl-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Hockey League Players\u8217\'20\'19 Association}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe has the expertise,\u8221\'20\'1D Shuler added. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s a hard worker. She\u8217\'20\'19s creative. We know that she will defend workers, especially the most vulnerable. This pick is a home run.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When Biden nominated her, Su explained \u8220\'20\'1Cmy mom came to the United States on a cargo ship\u8221\'20\'1D from China because she couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford a passenger ticket. Born in Madison and growing up outside Los Angeles, Su went to Stanford and Harvard Law School, and then became a lawyer for an LA-based advocacy group \uc2 Asian Americans Advancing Justice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt Harvard, we were taught to think like lawyers, but we did not learn to think like human beings,\u8221\'20\'1D Su often says. In 2001, Su, who is fluent in Mandarin and Spanish, won a \uc2 MacArthur Foundation\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cgenius\u8221\'20\'1D grant for her innovative work as a workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights advocate.\par \par \uc2 Immediately before becoming deputy secretary, she headed California\u8217\'20\'19s labor and workforce development agency under Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , and before that she oversaw California\u8217\'20\'19s labor enforcement under Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor Jerry Brown. She was known for aggressively cracking down on restaurants, garment factories and car washes that cheated workers out of wages. She also went after trucking companies that improperly classified their drivers as independent contractors in part to deny them minimum wage and overtime pay protections.\par \par \uc2 Kent Wong, director of the UCLA Labor Center, said: \u8220\'20\'1CShe did extraordinary work in reaching out to unions and community partners, in strengthening enforcement of wage laws and in really identifying the pernicious problem faced by so many low-wage workers of color who were routinely becoming victims of wage theft.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As California\u8217\'20\'19s top labor official, Su expanded apprenticeship programs to train workers without college degrees and helped run the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.labor.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/sites/338/2021/02/ca-future-of-work-report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 business/labor Future of Work Commission}}}\uc2 . That panel proposed ideas to help the workforce of the future, such as creating a \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia Job Quality Index\u8221\'20\'1D to define high-quality jobs and help workers know who are good employers offering good benefits.\par \par \uc2 When Su was under consideration to be deputy secretary of labor, Allen Zaremberg, president of the California chamber of commerce, praised her \u8220\'20\'1Cprofessionalism\u8221\'20\'1D and said: \u8220\'20\'1CJulie Su has always been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/californias-su-rises-in-biden-labor-chief-race-as-unions-split"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open to the views of employers}}}\uc2  and is willing to listen to the concerns of the business community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So far the \uc2 US Chamber of Commerce\uc2  and most other business groups have not taken a position on Su\u8217\'20\'19s nomination. But the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.franchise.org/media-center/press-releases/ifa-statement-on-julie-su-nomination-to-head-us-department-of-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Franchise Association was quick to oppose her}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDeputy Secretary Su has been consistently hostile to small businesses throughout her career,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Michael Layman\uc2 , the franchise association\u8217\'20\'19s senior vice-president of government relations. He faulted her for supporting California law AB5, which made it harder for businesses to classify workers as independent contractors, a law that upset \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lorena Gonzalez\uc2 , president of the California Labor Federation, said she had long been impressed with how Su maintained good communications and relations with business. \u8220\'20\'1CShe brought a perspective that labor law enforcement isn\u8217\'20\'19t just good for workers, it\u8217\'20\'19s also good for high-road businesses that are doing things right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2017, when Su was California\u8217\'20\'19s labor commissioner, she told me in an interview: \u8220\'20\'1CI passionately believe that our enforcement is good for employers. The legitimate businesses that are complying with the law are frustrated with the bad guys that aren\u8217\'20\'19t complying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Su was widely criticized over the billions of dollars that California\u8217\'20\'19s unemployment insurance paid out due to fraud during the pandemic. But Su\u8217\'20\'19s defenders noted that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/opinion/campaign/542959-julie-su-is-the-right-choice-to-help-lead-bidens-labor-department/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other states also experienced plenty of such fraud}}}\uc2 , that California\u8217\'20\'19s unemployment insurance system was a mess long before Julie Su and that the nationwide rush to keep the pandemic-induced unemployed from going hungry made unemployment screening less rigorous than usual.\par \par \uc2 The Franchise Association said that \u8220\'20\'1Cbased on her record, she does not deserve a promotion from a largely operations role to the [department\u8217\'20\'19s] principal policymaker\u8221\'20\'1D. It urged the Senate to reject her just as it rejected David Weil, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to head the labor department\u8217\'20\'19s wage and hour division.\par \par \uc2 Weil, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/senate-turns-back-david-weil-as-labors-top-wage-hour-enforcer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  headed that division under President Barack Obama}}}\uc2 , was voted down 53 to 47. Business groups lobbied hard against Weil because he had pushed to stop gig companies, like \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2 , from what he said was improperly classifying their drivers as independent contractors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom my own experience, I know what a razor\u8217\'20\'19s edge the Senate is right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Weil said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s all about two senators\u8217\'20\'19 willingness to support her,\u8221\'20\'1D in a reference to Joe Manchin and Kysten Sinema, senators who were elected as Democrats but have voted with Republicans against progressive actions.\par \par \uc2 Weil said Su would have a lot to do as labor secretary, although if the Senate fails to confirm her, she would remain as acting secretary of labor. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are two or three major rules that have to be finalized,\u8221\'20\'1D Weil said, \u8220\'20\'1Cand that gets harder and harder as you get closer to an election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He mentioned rules to make it harder to misclassify workers as independent contractors and to increase the threshold, currently $35,500, below which employees would have to be paid overtime if they work over 40 hours a week.\par \par \uc2 Erica Smiley, executive director of Jobs with Justice, a labor rights group, praised Su for being innovative. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s been on the cutting edge of trying new stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D Smiley said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe has an appetite for experimenting with policies that will benefit everyday people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Normally the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which is independent from the labor department \u8211\'20\'13 handles cases in which companies are accused of illegally shutting stores or operations in retaliation for unionization efforts. Pointing to \uc2 Amy\u8217\'20\'19s Kitchen\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision and close its food prep operation in San Jose and lay off 331 workers as that facility faced a union drive, Smiley suggested that Su have the labor department provide emergency assistance to workers who lose jobs in such situations, just as other federal agencies provide disaster relief. She urged Su to speak out against companies like \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  that she said were engaged in aggressive union-busting.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Congress have enacted three far-reaching laws that will create hundreds of thousands of jobs \u8211\'20\'13 on infrastructure, semiconductor investment and transitioning to clean energy. Many worker advocates are looking to Su to use her sway as secretary to make sure the bulk of those new jobs are good, middle-class jobs, and many hope they\u8217\'20\'19re unionized jobs, too.\par \par \uc2 One of Su\u8217\'20\'19s biggest champions is \uc2 Sara Nelson\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2  and someone Senator Bernie Sanders urged Biden to nominate as labor secretary. Right after Su was nominated, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FlyingWithSara/status/1630641757992960000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nelson tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CFantastic news for the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I know that she will be fighting the good fight from the inside\par \par \uc2 Sara Nelson\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was very clear from the very beginning that we already had someone eminently qualified for this position,\u8221\'20\'1D Nelson said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s way more qualified for this job than I would be, depending on what you think the job should be, in terms of understanding policy and how to use it as a tool to help average Americans. She wants to be a strong adviser to a president who wants to be the most pro-worker president ever.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about one person filling a position,\u8221\'20\'1D Nelson added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about all of us working together to lift standards for the American people. I know that she will be fighting the good fight from the inside, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be fighting the good fight from the outside.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some worker advocates voiced concern that Su is not a White House insider the way Walsh was and the way former labor secretary \uc2 Tom Perez\uc2  was under Obama. That could make it harder for Su to get the White House\u8217\'20\'19s and Office of Management and Budget\u8217\'20\'19s blessing to finalize important regulations.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Shuler voiced confidence: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s very persuasive, relentless and persistent. It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to ignore Julie Su.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230312ej3c000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
