\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 A four-day week can work for US small business owners. Hear me out\b0\par\par\uc2 Gene Marks \par \uc2 720 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 March 2023\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Many of my clients are doubtful of a four-day work week. But embrace it \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a carrot to dangle, and it\u8217\'20\'19ll help you attract talent\par \par \uc2 When I ask my clients about the four-day work week I generally get the same response: the eye roll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me see if I understand this,\u8221\'20\'1D they will inevitably say. \u8220\'20\'1CThe employee works for four days, but I pay them for five, right? Thanks, I\u8217\'20\'19m out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to these business owners, my clients, this kind of thing just won\u8217\'20\'19t happen in America. And don\u8217\'20\'19t you roll your eyes at them either: these are very smart and profit-minded people who care very much for their employees. But they are deeply dubious when they hear of the studies of the companies in the UK, Europe and elsewhere that implemented a four-day work week and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2023/feb/21/four-day-week-uk-trial-success-pattern"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who were}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Creally pleased\u8221\'20\'1D and believe that the arrangement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2023/feb/26/campaign-for-four-day-week-aims-to-sign-up-more-firms-after-uk-trial-success"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would result}}}\uc2  in people living \u8220\'20\'1Chappier and more fulfilled lives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I understand their reaction, really, I do. We\u8217\'20\'19re Americans. No one works as hard as us, right? These other people prefer to do silly things like take vacations, drink wine and spend more time with their families and friends. Now they only want to work four days a week? My God, what a bunch of lazy bums. Shame on them.\par \par \uc2 Actually, shame on us. We just don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what\u8217\'20\'19s going on with this trend.\par \par \uc2 This is not just about working four days a week. It\u8217\'20\'19s about marketing. We market to attract and retain customers. But we don\u8217\'20\'19t do enough to market and retain employees. The labor market couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be any tighter. There are close to 11 million unfilled jobs out there. My clients complain frequently about how tough it is to compete for talent.\par \par \uc2 And yet, here is something that drops right on our laps and which can help us fix this labor shortage problem and we\u8217\'20\'19re rolling our eyes? Yeah, shame on us for not recognizing the potential of the four-day workweek. All we need to do is fiddle with the scheduling.\par \par \uc2 Do you have hourly workers on the shop floor? Construction workers on the job site? Service techs out in the field? Customer service reps in the office? Then change their hours. Instead of an eight-hour day over five days offer the option of working 10 hours over four days. Congratulations, you\u8217\'20\'19re now offering a four-day work week.\par \par \uc2 This is not a new concept. I see this frequently in healthcare, on the manufacturing floor and in other service industries. My daughter, a veterinarian and a millennial, works three 12-hour shifts a week for her employer, a national chain. The work gets done. She couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be happier. So are they (I think).\par \par \uc2 What about salaried people? Look at their schedules, too. Can they take responsibility for delivering whatever is in their job description in however many hours it takes them to do the work? Do you care if your marketing manager is creating leads in four days or five days as long as the leads are coming in? Is it your concern that your accounting staff works four days if your bills are being paid and cash is being collected as always? Is there anything your HR manager is not doing in the flexible time offered? Stop thinking hours. Think deliverables.\par \par \uc2 You don\u8217\'20\'19t even have to do this right away. You can make the four-day work week a program that only those employees working for your company for longer than a specified time can enjoy. It\u8217\'20\'19s a carrot to dangle. A prize for the good employee. And a test to make sure the person has been a good hire.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t fight this trend. Don\u8217\'20\'19t pooh-pooh or give me the stink-eye. Instead, embrace the buzz. Go with it. Tell the world that you offer a four-day work week and how awesome it is to work for your company, and how pro-worker you are. People \u8211\'20\'13 particularly young people \u8211\'20\'13 love to hear this. And what do you care, as long as your people are getting the work done?\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230312ej3c000ru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
