\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Idle no more: how automatic mouse jigglers are taking on nosy bosses\b0\par\par\uc2 Matthew Cantor \par \uc2 937 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 March 2023\par 06:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mouse movers have existed for years, but have recently become a symbol of resistance against workplace surveillance\par \par \uc2 Watching Premier League matches can be difficult when you live in the US. For midweek games, the kickoff is often in the middle of the work day, posing a challenge even for remote workers: how do you keep your online status from going idle?\par \par \uc2 The solution is a mouse mover: a tool that keeps your cursor jiggling even as you turn your full attention to the game. And last month, the Premier League\u8217\'20\'19s US \uc2 Twitter\uc2  feed endorsed goofing off by offering a \u8220\'20\'1CPLinUSA mouse mover\u8221\'20\'1D to a lucky winner.\par \par \uc2 Working hard or hardly working during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ARSMCI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ARSMCI}}}\uc2  today?\par \par \uc2 Take a break during those workday matchdays with a PLinUSA mouse mover! ??\par \par \uc2 To enter for a chance to win:\par \par \uc2 1?? RT\par \par \uc2 2?? Reply with ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/L4zquaVBFj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/L4zquaVBFj}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Premier League USA (@PLinUSA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PLinUSA/status/1625887673587040259?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The devices have existed for years, but their popularity soared as people began working from home early in the pandemic. They come in different varieties, ranging from cradles with spinning discs in the middle to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reddit.com/r/lego/comments/oljnak/made_a_mouse_mover_for_my_husband/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DIY creations made from Legos}}}\uc2 . But they are united as a symbol of resistance against workplace surveillance \u8211\'20\'13 even if their very existence points to a dystopian future.\par \par \uc2 As working from home was normalized in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/88gqgp/mouse-mover-jiggler-app-keep-screen-on-active"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerns grew about bossware}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 software that keeps a close eye on remote workers by, for instance, tracking their mouse movements. Work-communication platforms like \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Teams might be less Big Brother-ish, but they can still show when a worker has been \u8220\'20\'1Cidle\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a word that implies they\u8217\'20\'19re in a hammock with a cocktail when they might have perfectly legitimate reasons to have stepped away from their computer: caring for a child, going to the bathroom, rescuing the dog from a standoff with a rabid raccoon. And even if they are just taking a break, does the boss really have to know?\par \par \uc2 When bosses keep such close tabs on their staff, it fosters a \u8220\'20\'1Clack of trust between employer and employee\u8221\'20\'1D, says Diana Rodriguez of Tech8 USA, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tech8usa.com/home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas-based company}}}\uc2  that makes popular mouse movers, including small pads that physically move your mouse and USB sticks that simply shift the cursor. What\u8217\'20\'19s more, a lot of remote work \u8211\'20\'13 reading reports, listening to meetings \u8211\'20\'13 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t require moving the mouse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat kind of talent, you can\u8217\'20\'19t really micromanage,\u8221\'20\'1D Rodriguez says, so measuring performance by \u8220\'20\'1Chow long you\u8217\'20\'19ve been on the computer \u8230\'20\'26 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really hold weight\u8221\'20\'1D. And research would seem to back this claim: a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2021/03/210316132124.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2021 study on \u8220\'20\'1Cmicro-breaks\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 in which tired workers eat a snack or work on a crossword puzzle \u8211\'20\'13 helped them recover from fatigue and work better.\par \par \uc2 Tech8 began making mouse movers focused on gamers who didn\u8217\'20\'19t want their sessions to time out when they took a break. Initially, the mouse movers were made using a 3D printer. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then when the pandemic hit, people started buying the mouse movers for home use. And we were like: \u8216\'20\'18OK, this is getting crazy.\u8217\'20\'19 Our five or six printers that we had couldn\u8217\'20\'19t keep up with the demand.\u8221\'20\'1D Sales have continued to increase, and the company expects its 2023 sales volume to be triple the 2020 figure.\par \par \uc2 Even as workers have returned to the office, sales have increased \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps in part due to the wide variety of uses for the product. Healthcare workers use mouse movers to keep their computers awake while they talk to patients; IT teams use them to test software; students may need them to make it easier to take notes while they watch a lecture. (Of course, computers can be set to remain awake for long periods of time, but often these settings are inaccessible if your organization controls the device.)\par \par \uc2 Of course, even if these uses are entirely above-board, reviews on \uc2 Amazon\uc2  suggest plenty of people are more interested in outsmarting workplace surveillance \u8211\'20\'13 and loving the results. \u8220\'20\'1CA must-have for any work from home employees,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Undetectable-Computer-Simulate-Movement-Entering/product-reviews/B097ZXZLVR/ref=cm_cr_getr_d_paging_btm_prev_1?ie=UTF8&reviewerType=all_reviews&pageNumber=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote one user}}}\uc2  in a review of a mouse jiggler by a company called Phiginoo. \u8220\'20\'1CNeed to go step away for a snack? No problem! Want to play on your phone for a bit? It\u8217\'20\'19s got you covered! Want to take a nap? Have at it!\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Undetectable-Computer-Simulate-Movement-Entering/product-reviews/B097ZXZLVR/ref=cm_cr_getr_d_paging_btm_next_4?ie=UTF8&reviewerType=all_reviews&pageNumber=4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Others}}}\uc2  are simply trying to avoid tech frustration: \u8220\'20\'1CWorks great, to give the appearance of \u8220\'20\'1Cbusy\u8221\'20\'1D on all work laptops. It\u8217\'20\'19s not that I\u8217\'20\'19m not working, but I have multiple systems that I\u8217\'20\'19m \u8220\'20\'1Csupposed\u8221\'20\'1D to be logged into, on multiple laptops, and I can\u8217\'20\'19t be in two places at once. Or can I :) ??\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of course, even as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/technology/2021/12/mouse-movers-market-corporate-productivity-tracking.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mouse movers grow more popular}}}\uc2 , so does {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2021/09/24/remote-work-from-home-surveillance/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sophisticated workplace tracking}}}\uc2  that monitors keyboard movements or uses facial recognition software. Eight in 10 of the biggest private companies in the US track individual productivity, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/08/14/business/worker-productivity-tracking.html?unlocked_article_code=AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACEIPuomT1JKd6J17Vw1cRCfTTMQmqxCdw_PIxfs9gGPzNiGeVTdcwqNPW9LavB-dIvM_INEuxDWdScRad6AoXv9_1KpHJUthVgK0o4WFhIVAPz88ooGyWGxw347IWfpw1w7WWVSDCbU1wqyj7VXBMT6sDOeMgzB6Y1p4psBnIV_9jCMXlfqWEfpy3NZ9wfZyUctlEG9UNiCJuvXpXhgoK8zGOk-HknQ-XO9eXT3Yn8fNqO5TNVUPVi-VCS938m0-69hDOdIIPKqZLxQoecD2g7x5GXU_Zc7yRMV3H96I4u0s5b3dqhWMy960z-E1EchXvrDGsGW7NTU_Wd3hef_deFHr7NeTL08aj-Q&smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2 . And workplace computers may be able to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.digitaltrends.com/computing/what-are-mouse-jigglers/#dt-heading-are-mouse-jigglers-legal-will-i-get-in-trouble-using-one"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detect the use of peripherals}}}\uc2 , which could reveal some mouse movers to your boss. If your employer has remote access to your computer screen, they might notice repetitive mouse movements that would be a red flag.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe would love to go obsolete but we see that mouse movers like this help increase productivity and people are less stressed, believe it or not, because they\u8217\'20\'19re not worried about their computer timing out,\u8221\'20\'1D Rodriguez says. \u8220\'20\'1CThey can step away and go take care of a personal thing or go put laundry in or check on the baby.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230306ej36000uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
