\par\par \uc2 UK news\par \b \uc2 Amazon\uc2  union leader flies in to help UK strikers \u8216\'20\'18kick down the door\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stokel-Walker \par \uc2 766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2023\par 09:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chris Smalls, who set up the retailer\u8217\'20\'19s first union in New York, came to Coventry to back its workers in their pay dispute\par \par \uc2 The leader of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first union has made his first trip outside the United States to support striking workers at the online retail giant\u8217\'20\'19s Coventry warehouse.\par \par \uc2 Chris Smalls, who helped coordinate a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/01/amazon-union-groups-see-hope-workers-vote-alabama-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successful unionisation drive}}}\uc2  at an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in Staten Island, New York, in April 2022, travelled to the UK last week to provide advice to British workers as they try to gain recognition from the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important that we amplify each other\u8217\'20\'19s fight and struggles because we want to build that international solidarity,\u8221\'20\'1D Smalls told the Observer. \u8220\'20\'1CJust like they\u8217\'20\'19re refusing to talk to these workers and negotiate a fair contract, we\u8217\'20\'19re in the same process back at home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smalls\u8217\'20\'19s trip has been in the making for a month, with the 34-year-old specifically registering for a passport in order to make his first journey. \u8220\'20\'1CI booked my flight the same week I got my passport,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs soon as I got that letter that I\u8217\'20\'19m free to leave, I made sure this trip was a priority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That Smalls made the visit \u8211\'20\'13 and that it was his first \u8211\'20\'13 has been seen as a vindication for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/feb/13/amazon-workers-coventry-warehouse-strike-seven-days"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 400 staff striking}}}\uc2  at the Coventry warehouse. They are seeking higher pay, but also complaining about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jan/22/first-industrial-action-at-amazon-uk-hopes-to-strike-at-firms-union-hostility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overbearing management and long working hours}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor Chris to say the first thing he wanted to do was come out here has got me,\u8221\'20\'1D said Darren Westwood, one of the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers picketing the Coventry facility. \u8220\'20\'1CIt blows my mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The dispute is the first official organised strike of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in the UK. Previous actions in Tilbury, Essex which saw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/aug/05/amazon-staff-essex-protest-pay-dispute-coventry-bristol-rugeley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staff gather in the warehouse canteen}}}\uc2  to protest at pay and conditions, were wildcat strikes.\par \par \uc2 The Coventry strikers, who account for around one-fifth of the 2,000 staff at the site, are seeking a 43% increase in pay to \u163\'00\'A315 an hour. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  pays an hourly wage of between \u163\'00\'A310.50 and \u163\'00\'A311.45, depending on location. The national living wage is \u163\'00\'A310.42 an hour for those over the age of 23.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re getting paid \u163\'00\'A310, minimum wage, for the same time of work we\u8217\'20\'19re doing back in the States, and we\u8217\'20\'19re getting paid twice as much,\u8221\'20\'1D said Smalls. \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make any sense. Because of the cost of living, even us making twice as much, we are still living cheque to cheque.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson said \u8220\'20\'1Ca tiny proportion of our workforce is involved\u8221\'20\'1D in the strikes. \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, only a fraction of 1% of our UK employees voted in the ballot \u8211\'20\'13 and that includes those who voted against action.\u8221\'20\'1D The spokesperson added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe appreciate the great work our teams do throughout the year and we\u8217\'20\'19re proud to offer competitive pay.\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Amazon\uc2  also claims to offer \u8220\'20\'1Ccomprehensive benefits that are worth thousands more\u8221\'20\'1D to staff.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s US union got a higher wage for its workers by continuing to press the company to improve its offer \u8211\'20\'13 something Smalls believes can be done by UK workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the union does is say: \u8216\'20\'18Well, yes, we got breadcrumbs, but imagine what we can get if we have a contract,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Smalls said that in the US, unionised \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers are now fighting to get $30 an hour. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re doubling that up, because we know \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has the money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smalls spoke with striking workers on the picket line last week as part of the visit, and exchanged advice on how to organise and work for recognition by the e-commerce giant. It does, however, take time. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just the start. Every marathon you have to take that first step,\u8221\'20\'1D said Westwood.\par \par \uc2 Smalls said that the striking \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers will make Coventry \u8220\'20\'1Cthe stronghold and the catalyst for the UK\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI promise you that when they win, there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be warehouses all over this country that are going to do the same thing We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get one crack in the door, then we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to kick the door down and let everybody in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smalls suggests Coventry \u8211\'20\'13 and the UK \u8211\'20\'13 will just be the start of his \uc2 Amazon\uc2  unionisation drive, with potential future visits to similar movements in Europe. \u8220\'20\'1CThey messed up,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey let me out. I\u8217\'20\'19m going everywhere I need to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230301ej2q00345\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
