\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Lavatory waste comes on us\u8217\'20\'19: New York airport workers protest unsanitary conditions\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,155 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2023\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2  employees also allege ground services firm violates sick leave policy and retaliates against those who speak out\par \par \uc2 These days Omar Rodriguez, a ramp worker and cabin cleaner at LaGuardia airport in New York, dreads cleaning planes \u8211\'20\'13 especially the toilets.\par \par \uc2 The 19-year-old works for \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2 , which services \uc2 Spirit Airlines\uc2  and \uc2 Air Canada\uc2  at LaGuardia, and claims that faulty equipment used for cleaning airplane lavatories often results in workers getting sprayed with human waste. When it happens, he said, workers are expected to continue cleaning the airplane cabins without being provided time or products to properly clean themselves.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are holes, and all the lavatory waste comes on us and they don\u8217\'20\'19t give us products to clean up. It\u8217\'20\'19s broken, they\u8217\'20\'19ve never fixed it, are still using it, and people are getting dirty because of that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rodriguez. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to go upstairs and clean the plane after we just did the lavatory, and we can have some waste on our shirt, and they send us right up to go upstairs to clean.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In light of these conditions and other issues, Rodriguez and other workers at the airport are pushing to organize a union among their colleagues and claim their efforts have triggered retaliation from their employer.\par \par \uc2 Ramp and cargo workers for \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2 , an airline contractor, argue they are working while severely understaffed, do not receive proper or promised compensation for taking on extra duties because of short staffing, including overtime and paid sick day violations, and have to work with broken or faulty equipment.\par \par \uc2 Since organizing a protest in early December 2022, workers heavily involved in the union organizing effort say they have faced unfair suspensions and have been intimidated by their supervisors, prompting them to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/29-CA-310875"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 file}}}\uc2  an unfair labor practice charge against the contractor. Other unfair labor practice charges have recently been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hudsonreporter.com/2022/12/08/swissport-cargo-workers-on-strike-in-wake-of-unfair-labor-practices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  against the same contractor at Newark international airport.\par \par \uc2 The protest was part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiu32bj.org/press-release/charlotte-airport-protest/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationwide campaign}}}\uc2  in which airport workers demanded better pay, benefits and working conditions, and called on Congress to pass the good jobs for good airports act, highlighting the work and sacrifices essential airport workers made throughout the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Rodriguez claims that after participating in a protest with his co-workers on 8 December 2022 over low pay and poor working conditions and speaking out to the media, he\u8217\'20\'19s been suspended several times in retaliation.\par \par \uc2 According to filed unfair labor practice charges, nearly a dozen workers have faced suspensions after participating in protests and speaking out about working conditions. Complaints have also been filed with New York City\u8217\'20\'19s department of consumer and worker protection alleging \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2  failed to provide paid time off that workers had earned, in violation of local paid safe and sick leave laws.\par \par \uc2 I had to work through injuries and pain because I was the only person in the bag room, lifting hundreds of bags a day\par \par \uc2 Airport service worker Chad Infiesta\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was denied my sick pay, even though I had a crippling migraine and a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s note,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chad Infiesta, an airport service worker with \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2  organizing with \uc2 SEIU\uc2 , in a statement. He was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://documentedny.com/2023/02/10/laguardia-airport-workers-swissport-protest/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terminated}}}\uc2  in December 2022 after participating in the protest. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been through so much. I had to work through injuries and pain because I was the only person in the bag room, lifting hundreds of bags a day.\u8221\'20\'1D He also experienced being sprayed with human waste due to a faulty hose while emptying airplane bathrooms.\par \par \uc2 A third ramp worker at \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2 , who requested anonymity due to fear of retaliation, also criticized the lack of protective equipment and resources \u8211\'20\'13 such as gloves or opportunities to change uniforms or dry off when employees are sprayed with wastewater when emptying the airplane bathrooms \u8211\'20\'13 provided to workers to perform their duties, and the company\u8217\'20\'19s retaliation against employees for speaking out about the poor conditions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have a chance to wipe yourself down. You have to go right back up to clean the plane,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have issues where the water has fallen on me, because the tubes that connect to the aircraft don\u8217\'20\'19t connect very good, and then when I\u8217\'20\'19m standing on the ladder, there\u8217\'20\'19s water that just goes on me, and it could be a day when it\u8217\'20\'19s cold, and I have to deal with it. I just keep those clothes on because they don\u8217\'20\'19t have anything else to provide me with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 William Alston, another ramp agent and cabin cleaner for \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2  at LaGuardia, also claimed he has received retaliatory suspensions since the December 2022 protest and echoed similar complaints about working conditions, broken equipment, understaffing and low pay.\par \par \uc2 He makes $18 an hour and claims he has yet to receive a pay raise to the $21 an hour he said was promised to him and other workers for adding cabin cleaner job duties to their work handling plane cargo.\par \par \uc2 We only have six minutes or less to clean the cabins and it\u8217\'20\'19s not a thorough clean\par \par \uc2 Ramp agent William Alston\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe only have six minutes or less to clean the cabins and it\u8217\'20\'19s not a thorough clean. It\u8217\'20\'19s just time to clean behind the seat pockets, and another person would just take out the trash that\u8217\'20\'19s in the front and rear of the plane and take the garbage out that\u8217\'20\'19s in the restrooms and that\u8217\'20\'19s about it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alston.\par \par \uc2 Alston also said that workers are retaliated against for not coming in on days off when requested or for not working overtime with suspensions, write-ups or retaliatory changes to their schedules. He was suspended twice this year in what he alleges to be retaliation \u8211\'20\'13 the first time for calling out sick and attempting to use his accrued sick time, which he was never paid for, and the second time for not completing a training he claims other workers have also not completed but had not received any reprimand for missing it and are still working.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re working too many hours for the bare minimum,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alston. \u8220\'20\'1CThe retaliation has been affecting me a lot. I really want to get back to work, and I have credit cards and bills to pay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Swissport USA\uc2  did not comment on specific allegations, but denied all allegations of retaliation, unfair labor practice charges, and health and safety claims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSwissport denies any unfair labor practices, fully complies with applicable labor regulations, and provides competitive wages and benefits. In all the cities we operate in the United States, Swissport fully complies with operating permit requirements,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CThe health and safety of all our employees is the highest priority for Swissport, as evidenced by our Best-in-Class record.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230223ej2n001mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
