\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Tesla\uc2  fires more than 30 workers after union drive announcement\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 February 2023\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at the Gigafactory 2 in Buffalo, New York, allege employees were fired in response to a union organizing drive\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers at the Gigafactory 2 in Buffalo, New York, allege over 30 workers were fired on 14 February in response to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-02-14/tesla-autopilot-workers-launch-union-campaign-in-buffalo-new-york-tsla?leadSource=uverify%20wall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement}}}\uc2  of a union organizing drive at the 1,000-worker facility.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Tesla\uc2  chief executive, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , has fought union drives in the past. The campaign, Tesla Workers United, is affiliated with the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 SEIU\uc2 ) affiliate Workers United and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/16/business/tesla-buffalo-union.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  an injunction with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) seeking to halt the firings.\par \par \uc2 The workers say they\u8217\'20\'19re seeking to unionize in response to the need for better wages and job security, and productivity pressures, including the surveillance of workers\u8217\'20\'19 tasks and the monitoring of keystrokes, that deter some employees from taking bathroom breaks.\par \par \uc2 A now-fired \uc2 Tesla\uc2  employee and organizing committee member, Arian Berek, stated in a press release: \u8220\'20\'1CI feel blindsided, I got Covid and was out of the office, then I had to take a bereavement leave. I returned to work, was told I was exceeding expectations and then Wednesday came along. I strongly feel this is in retaliation to the committee announcement and it\u8217\'20\'19s shameful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sara Costantino, a current \uc2 Tesla\uc2  employee and organizing committee member, added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re angry. This won\u8217\'20\'19t slow us down. This won\u8217\'20\'19t stop us. They want us to be scared, but I think they just started a stampede. We can do this. But I believe we will do this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers also cited the announcement of a new policy prohibiting employees from recording workplace meetings without all participants\u8217\'20\'19 permission, which they say undermines federal labor law and the state of New York\u8217\'20\'19s one-party consent law on recording conversations.\par \par \uc2 The union, if successful, would be a first at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . Workers attempted to organize a union at the Fremont, California, production plant in 2017 with the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  before several employees involved in the union campaign were also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2018/sep/10/tesla-workers-union-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terminated}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/25/business/musk-labor-board.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  the reinstatement of one fired worker from that campaign, Richard Ortiz, in 2021, and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has also faced other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://buffalonews.com/business/local/tesla-accused-of-firing-pro-union-workers-at-buffalo-solar-plant/article_90e5c79a-adbc-5669-939a-276ab24385ad.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allegations}}}\uc2  of firing workers in retaliation for organizing efforts at the company\u8217\'20\'19s solar plant in Buffalo, New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnionizing will further accelerate the world\u8217\'20\'19s transition to sustainable energy because it will give us a voice in our workplace and in the goals we set for ourselves to accomplish,\u8221\'20\'1D said a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-02-14/tesla-autopilot-workers-launch-union-campaign-in-buffalo-new-york-tsla?leadSource=uverify%20wall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to management announcing the union campaign.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has not commented in response to the firings and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=2ahUKEwi5vMe34Zr9AhW4m2oFHZUABvcQFnoECAkQAQ&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.reuters.com%2Farticle%2Fus-tesla-media%2Ftesla-disbands-u-s-media-relations-team-electrek-idUSKBN26R2CX&usg=AOvVaw0kxL7ed7ejkiL1cWtwXBxk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disbanded}}}\uc2  its US media relations team in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230217ej2h000p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
