\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s just crazy\u8217\'20\'19: Republicans attack US child labor laws as violations rise\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,284 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 February 2023\par 07:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Changes lawmakers are seeking, such as expanding types of approved work, will potentially \u8216\'20\'18put kids in dangerous situations\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 As child labor law violations have been on the rise in the US, some state legislators are pushing for changes at state and federal levels to roll back protections in what some see as a threat to return child labor to the country.\par \par \uc2 The laws aim to expand permissible work hours, broaden the types of jobs young workers are permitted to do, and shield employers from liability for injuries, illnesses or workplace fatalities involving very young workers.\par \par \uc2 Child labor law violations have increased in the US, with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-11426465/The-number-kids-working-breach-labor-rules-spiked-37-year.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 37% increase}}}\uc2  in fiscal year 2022, including 688 children working in hazardous conditions, with the number likely much higher as the recorded violations stem from what was found during labor inspections.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Labor issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20220729"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release}}}\uc2  in July 2022 noting child labor violations and investigations have increased since 2015.\par \par \uc2 Several high-profile investigations involving child labor have been exposed over the past year, including the use of child labor in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/investigates/special-report/usa-immigration-hyundai/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hyundai and Kia supply chains}}}\uc2  in Alabama, at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/feds-dhs-investigating-human-trafficking-children-slaughterhouses-rcna66081"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JBS meatpacking plants}}}\uc2  in Nebraska and Minnesota, and at fast-food chains including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/12/07/1141139724/mcdonalds-child-labor-laws-violations-pittsburgh#:~:text=The%20fast%20food%20franchisee%2C%20Santonastasso,its%20restaurants%2C%20according%20to%20officials."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/boston/news/dunkin-stores-child-labor-lawviolations-westford-group/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dunkin Donuts}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.qsrmagazine.com/legal/chipotle-pay-775-million-over-child-labor-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chipotle}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Amid these increases in child labor violations, legislative efforts have been introduced in several states to roll back child labor protections.\par \par \uc2 In Iowa, Republican legislators introduced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legis.iowa.gov/legislation/BillBook?ba=SF167&ga=90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  in January to expand the types of work 14- and 15-year-olds would be permitted to do as part of approved training programs, extend allowable work hours, and exempt employers from liability if these young workers are sickened, injured or killed on the job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just crazy to me that we are re-litigating a lot of things that seem to have been settled 100, 120 or 140 years ago,\u8221\'20\'1D said Charlie Wishman, president of the Iowa AFL-CIO, which is opposing the bill.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s just crazy to me that we are re-litigating a lot of things that seem to have been settled 100, 120, or 140 years ago\par \par \uc2 Charlie Wishman, president of the Iowa \uc2 AFL-CIO\par \par \uc2 Wishman added: \u8220\'20\'1CAll of these protections have been put in place for a reason. Child labor law is there to make sure that kids are working in age-appropriate work activities or occupations that are appropriate for their age. We think this is a rewrite of our child labor laws in Iowa that are going way, way, way too far and has the potential to put kids in dangerous situations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iowastartingline.com/2023/01/31/bill-expands-iowa-child-labor-limits-teens-protection-if-hurt/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  would permit the director of Iowa workforce development or the Iowa department of education to grant exceptions from any provision that restricts the types of jobs 14- and 15-year-olds can do if the work is classified as part of a work-based learning program and also strips workers\u8217\'20\'19 compensation rights for these workers.\par \par \uc2 The protections being sought for companies are of particular concern to labor activists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the Iowa legislation, one of the provisions is to exempt employers from civil liability due to the company\u8217\'20\'19s negligence. It is astounding that they would have the gall to knowingly acknowledge that more young people will be harmed, but focus on exempting businesses,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marcy Goldstein-Gelb, co-executive director of the National Council for Occupational Safety and Health.\par \par \uc2 Goldstein-Gelb explained that throughout her career she has worked with families and co-workers of young workers who have died on the job, oftentimes in violation of child labor laws that industry groups have fought to repeal, such as in a case where a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/face/stateface/ma/00ma050.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16-year-old}}}\uc2  in Massachusetts was killed in 2000 while operating a golf cart on the job.\par \par \uc2 Young workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/69/wr/mm6935a3.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 much higher rates}}}\uc2  of non-fatal injuries on the job and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/topics/youth/default.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest rates}}}\uc2  of injuries that require emergency department attention, Goldstein-Gelb noted. She argued that due to the vulnerability and inexperience of young workers, data on these workers is likely an undercount due to fears or barriers in being able to speak up and report dangerous situations or child labor law violations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there is this myth that you need to put young people in any possible job because there are openings. I think we are moving into a new age where we need to recognize that workers of all ages are seeking to earn a sustainable living and not put themselves in harm\u8217\'20\'19s way,\u8221\'20\'1D added Goldstein-Gelb. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why there are workers taking actions around the country and that needs to be supported rather than just saying we\u8217\'20\'19re going to find people who have no alternative, the most vulnerable, and put them in jobs that are completely inappropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other states are currently or have pushed similar legislation to roll back child labor protections.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, legislators reintroduced a bipartisan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiocapitaljournal.com/2023/02/07/bill-to-extend-working-hours-for-ohio-teens-reintroduced-by-lawmakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  this year to extend working hours for 14- and 15-year-olds with permission from a parent or legal guardian, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legislature.ohio.gov/legislation/134/scr14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on Congress to adopt the same rollbacks at the federal level.\par \par \uc2 Legislators in Minnesota introduced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/bill.php?f=HF878&b=house&y=2023&ssn=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  in January 2023 to extend work hours for 14- and 15-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Wisconsin passed a bill that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/best-states/wisconsin/articles/2022-02-04/evers-vetoes-bill-that-would-have-allowed-teens-to-work-late"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vetoed}}}\uc2  by Governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  in this month that would have expanded work hours for 14- and 15-year-olds. The New Jersey governor, Phil Murphy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/education/2022/07/06/phil-murphy-law-expands-teens-work-hours-summer-nj/65368145007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  a similar law in 2022 that expanded work hours for 14- and 15-year-olds to work longer hours during summer months and on holidays and expanded allowable work hours for 16- and 17-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 At the federal level, Republican congressman \uc2 Dave Joyce\uc2  of Ohio drafted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gOcsYUm2CWFTwEWpjVOwvObY7aB8xtLm/view?usp=share_link"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  in 2022 to expand working hours for 14- and 15-year-olds during periods when school is in session.\par \par \uc2 Advocates for legislative efforts to roll back child labor regulations have cited labor shortages, particularly in industries that rely on young workers, and have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prospect.org/labor/conservative-astroturf-organization-rolling-back-child-labor-protections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strongly backed}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 National Federation of Independent Business\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We think these laws are really ill advised and just asking kids to have negative educational impacts\par \par \uc2 Reid Maki\uc2  of the Child Labor Coalition\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe think these laws are really ill advised and just asking kids to have negative educational impacts,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Reid Maki\uc2 , director of child labor issues and coordinator at the Child Labor Coalition, who argued it took significant efforts to enact child labor laws over 100 years ago, when there were thousands of children working long hours in unsafe jobs such as factories and mines.\par \par \uc2 Maki added: \u8220\'20\'1CNow there are states that want to go back toward that direction to deal with labor shortages by using teens, even to the extent of placing them in dangerous work environments \u8211\'20\'13 [it] doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make sense. It\u8217\'20\'19s disregarding their welfare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He argued that child labor laws in the US need to be strengthened and updated, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/7345/text?r=52&s=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closing existing loopholes}}}\uc2  that permit young workers, some as young as 12 years old, to work unlimited hours in many jobs in the agriculture industry with parental permission when school is not in session.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nfwm.org/resource-center/harvest-of-justice/harvest-of-justice-2022-child-labor-in-agriculture/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated 300,000 to 500,000 minors}}}\uc2  work in the US agriculture industry annually, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://marshfieldresearch.org/Media/Default/NFMC/National%20Childrens%20Center/2022_Child_Ag_Injury_Fact_Sheet.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 48% of all young worker fatalities}}}\uc2  between 2001 to 2015 occurring in the agriculture industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my office, we can\u8217\'20\'19t bring in a 12-year-old to make copies, 12 is too young, but we will take that same 12-year-old and put them in a field. The actual law allows them to work unlimited hours as long as school is not in session,\u8221\'20\'1D added Maki. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is basically no protection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230211ej2b000mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
