\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US adds 517,000 jobs in January in huge gain for labor market\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 641 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 February 2023\par 16:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Total is far higher than what economists expected even as \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  continues to raise interest rates to bring down inflation\par \par \uc2 The US job market added 517,000 jobs in January, a huge gain for the labor market even as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has pushed up interest rates to bring down inflation and try to temper hiring.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the unemployment rate has held relatively steady at 3.4% \u8211\'20\'13 a 0.1% decrease compared with last month. Economists had expected the unemployment rate to rise slightly last month, but the rate still remains on par with what was seen before the pandemic. The rate is a 53-year low, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-02-03/us-job-gains-post-surprise-surge-jobless-rate-hits-53-year-low"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Far higher than what economists expected \u8211\'20\'13 estimates put the job increase at 185,000 \u8211\'20\'13 January\u8217\'20\'19s growth in the job market is an acceleration of activity in the job market which, while showing signs of cooling at the end of last year, is still growing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jan/06/us-jobs-report-december-2022-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December}}}\uc2  saw 223,000 jobs added to the labor market that, while still an overall increase, was lower than the average 539,000 new jobs a month that were being added at the beginning of 2022.\par \par \uc2 Job increases were seen across the board, led by leisure and hospitality, retail, healthcare and professional and business services.\par \par \uc2 Predictions that the labor market was cooling was led by multiple data points published this week that showed jobs were being added to the economy, but at a slower pace than previous months. ADP, the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest payroll supplier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/02/01/adp-jobs-report-january-2022-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Wednesday that private employers added 106,000 jobs in January, less than half the jobs that were added by private employers in December.\par \par \uc2 ADP partly attributed the slowdown to poor weather interrupting work in December, according to ADP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn January, we saw the impact of weather-related disruptions on employment during our reference week,\u8221\'20\'1D the ADP chief economist, \uc2 Nela Richardson\uc2 , said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CHiring was stronger during other weeks of the month, in line with the strength we saw late last year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the labor department released data this week that showed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-02-01/us-job-openings-unexpectedly-surge-to-more-than-11-million?leadSource=uverify%20wall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued rise}}}\uc2  in job vacancies in December, with 11m job openings last month compared with 10.4m in December.\par \par \uc2 The recent figures show resilience in the job market even as the Fed continues to hike interest rates to bring down record levels of inflation.\par \par \uc2 Inflation finally started to ease in the second half of last year, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jan/12/us-inflation-rate-december-cpi-cost-living"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the inflation rate}}}\uc2  reaching 6.5% in December and the month-over-month cost of living dropping for the first time since May 2020. On Wednesday, the Fed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/feb/01/fed-small-interest-hike-inflation-eases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased interest rates}}}\uc2  by a quarter point \u8211\'20\'13 its smallest increase since it started raising rates last March \u8211\'20\'13 raising interest rates to 4.5% to 4.75%.\par \par \uc2 The Fed chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , indicated on Wednesday that despite the decrease in inflation, the central bank will continue to increase rates \u8220\'20\'1Ca couple more\u8221\'20\'1D times in the future as it looks to bring down inflation even more.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would say it is a good thing the disinflation we have so far has not come at the expense of a weaker labor market,\u8221\'20\'1D Powell said on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I would say the inflationary process you see under way is really at an early stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe covered a lot of ground, and the full effects of our rapid tightening so far are yet to be felt. Even so, we have more work to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are some signs that the labor market could tighten more in the coming months. Amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jan/06/amazon-apple-tesla-elon-musk-job-cuts-tech-sector"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 layoffs}}}\uc2  from tech firms like \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Meta\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2 , employment firm \uc2 Challenger\uc2 , Gray and Christmas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.challengergray.com/blog/jan-23-recession-or-correction-highest-january-since-2009-highest-monthly-total-since-september-2020/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  an increase in job cuts in January, with cuts rising to 102,943 in January, up from 43,651 cuts in December.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230203ej23001ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
