\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It can be scary\u8217\'20\'19: how corporate America is hitting back against unions\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,420 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 January 2023\par 18:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employers are using heavy-handed tactics to prevent workers from organizing, and US labor union density is falling as a result\par \par \uc2 Workers at a Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s store in Louisville, Kentucky, are now pushing to become the third store at the trendy US supermarket chain to unionize since 2022.\par \par \uc2 Connor Hovey, a worker and organizer at the Louisville store, said unionizing efforts began as other high-profile union organizing efforts such as at Louisville\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/2022/09/09/heine-brothers-coffees-baristas-union-vote-passes-louisville/67292820007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Heine Brothers}}}\uc2 , a local coffee shop chain, were taking off. Like those workers, the Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s organizers sought to address issues stemming from inadequate corporate policies and safety precautions, and how workers have been treated during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 But during the organizing drive Hovey claimed opposition from Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s management has been intense, resulting in workers filing several unfair labor practice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SethGoldstein13/status/1615859416556834817"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ). \u8220\'20\'1CThe company has made it very clear that they will do whatever they can to stop this effort in its tracks,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hovey.\par \par \uc2 This sort of intense pushback against unionization is becoming the norm in the US \u8211\'20\'13 and it is having an impact. The intense opposition from many major US employers to workers who are trying to unionize is a major factor in the recent decline in labor union density in the US, with the US having among the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stats.oecd.org/Index.aspx?DataSetCode=TUD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowest union densities compared}}}\uc2  with other industrialized countries.\par \par \uc2 The decline comes even as the US labor movement experienced a surge in popular support in 2022, with a spike in union election filings, growing support for unions in polls and more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/12/19/worker-strikes-surged-in-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 work stoppages}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to a 2022 poll conducted by Gallup, support for labor unions reached its highest point since 1965, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/398303/approval-labor-unions-highest-point-1965.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 71%}}}\uc2  of Americans approving of unions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/election-petitions-up-53-board-continues-to-reduce-case-processing-time-in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Petitions}}}\uc2  filed for union elections increased by 53% in fiscal year 2022, resulting in the largest number filed since fiscal year 2016.\par \par \uc2 The number of unfair labor practice charges filed with \uc2 NLRB\uc2  field offices increased by 23% in fiscal year 2022\par \par \uc2 But despite this growth, US labor union density {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/union2.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  in 2022, with the share of workers represented by a labor union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unionization-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decreasing}}}\uc2  from 11.6% in 2021 to 11.3% in 2022, and union membership density decreasing from 10.3% in 2021 to 10.1% in 2022. The number of workers represented by unions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unionization-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased by 200,000}}}\uc2 , but this was offset by a 5.3% increase in the total number of workers in the US workforce.\par \par \uc2 The number of unfair labor practice charges filed with \uc2 NLRB\uc2  field offices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/election-petitions-up-53-board-continues-to-reduce-case-processing-time-in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  by 23% in fiscal year 2022, the largest single-year percentage increase in decades, revealing how widespread employer opposition is to unionization efforts.\par \par \uc2 US employers spend an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unionization-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  $340m annually on hiring union avoidance consultants to oppose unionization efforts and employers are charged with violating federal labor law in 41.5% of all union elections, according to a 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unlawful-employer-opposition-to-union-election-campaigns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis }}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Labor experts have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cepr.net/mixed-union-membership-report-shows-need-for-sustained-movement-effort-pro-worker-policy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted}}}\uc2  the disparity between support for labor unions and decreasing union density as revealing a need for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unionization-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public policy reforms}}}\uc2  to protect workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to organize and enact meaningful penalties on employers for violating labor laws. They also say the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  needs more funding as workers face long delays for charges to be reviewed and adjudicated.\par \par \uc2 Workers have won union elections for the first time at many US locations of high-profile corporations, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2 , Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s, REI, Chipotle and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nwitimes.com/business/local/starbucks-workers-in-valparaiso-file-for-union-election/article_6c0f79a2-3741-5b1a-8fe1-9878439f8153.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 270}}}\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores that have unionized since December 2021.\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , Workers United has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/16/fired-workers-starbucks-retaliation-union-organising-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  the company of firing dozens of workers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/04/new-york-starbucks-closed-union-drive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shutting down stores}}}\uc2  in retaliation for union organizing, and the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has issued more than 60 official complaints involving more than 1,200 labor law violations, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 Workers have organized numerous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/nov/17/workers-over-100-us-starbucks-stores-strike-red-cup-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strikes}}}\uc2  at stores around the US to protest alleged retaliation against workers and delays in bargaining a first union contract. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has disputed all allegations of retaliation and disputed all \uc2 NLRB\uc2  complaints and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2022/12/31/starbucks-illegally-terminated-union-leader-jaz-brisack-us-officials/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  rulings}}}\uc2  against the company so far.\par \par \uc2 I felt like they were trying to send a message of \u8216\'20\'18if you act like a problem, we will figure out how to fire you\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Sarah Pappin\par \par \uc2 Sarah Pappin, a shift supervisor at a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in Seattle for nine years, claimed she had experienced retaliation for being heavily involved in union organizing efforts and pushing for bargaining a first union contract.\par \par \uc2 Pappin said her store manager left at the end of 2021 to go to Buffalo, New York, as numerous store managers from around the US descended on that area to oppose unionization efforts at stores there. Pappin explained that shortly thereafter, she began getting in arguments over unionization with her store manager, who wrote her up for policy infractions such as swearing in the backroom that weren\u8217\'20\'19t enforced with other workers or managers.\par \par \uc2 She also received a final written warning for being late and explained the fear and anxiety that treatment has created for her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI definitely felt like they were trying to send a message of \u8216\'20\'18if you act like a problem, we will figure out how to fire you,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Pappin. \u8220\'20\'1CTo clock into your work every single day and not know if that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be the last day you work there, that\u8217\'20\'19s just really stressful and it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult as somebody who\u8217\'20\'19s really, really worked really hard for this company for years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unionizing efforts at other US household corporate names have also been fiercely contested.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-new-york-business-oklahoma-city-3faca3dea5a53225f49f73a974a6d895"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two Apple stores}}}\uc2 , one in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, with the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2 , and the other in Towson, Maryland, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goiam.org/news/imail/iam-core-members-first-u-s-apple-store-to-unionize-prepare-for-negotiations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 IAM CORE}}}\uc2 , won union elections in 2022, the first two stores at \uc2 Apple\uc2  to ever do so. \uc2 Apple\uc2  is currently facing intense scrutiny from the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/17/business/economy/apple-labor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investors}}}\uc2  over how the company responded to these union campaigns and others in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/2022/12/5/23495357/apple-atlanta-union-cwa-nlrb-complaint-coercing-interrogating"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/04/business/apple-store-nlrb-ruling.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York City}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnet.com/tech/union-files-us-labor-board-complaint-against-apple-alleges-anti-union-actions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbus}}}\uc2 , Ohio.\par \par \uc2 In Columbus, Ohio, workers are still pushing to organize a union amid allegations in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/apple-created-pseudo-union-to-defeat-organizers-complaint-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaint}}}\uc2  issued by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  that \uc2 Apple\uc2  created a pseudo union to stop unionization efforts at the store.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Apple\uc2  store worker in Columbus explained they started getting involved in union organizing at the store in response to degrading working conditions in recent years. They claimed the store has forced workers into captive audience meetings, which included corporate videos in which company executives try to dissuade workers from unionizing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen videos from our corporate bigwigs who have kind of slyly tried to say, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, we\u8217\'20\'19re here for you, we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to create another bridge in this relationship because we already do such a good job of being there for you,\u8217\'20\'19 and a lot of it is a facade to keep up a good image,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said.\par \par \uc2 Apple{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/17/business/economy/apple-labor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  recently reached}}}\uc2  a deal with investors to audit the company\u8217\'20\'19s labor practices in response to how the company has responded to union organizing in line with the company\u8217\'20\'19s human rights policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m incredibly hopeful that this will be done in an unbiased manner and \uc2 Apple\uc2  will kind of change direction instead of actively trying to dissuade organizing efforts and take a more active approach in ensuring a healthy relationship with any stores that choose to organize,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Forsythe, an employee and organizer at the \uc2 Apple\uc2  store in Oklahoma City that won its union election in October 2022.\par \par \uc2 Forsythe explained he had not been surprised by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  complaints filed against \uc2 Apple\uc2  for its behavior during union organizing campaigns, but he was hopeful as his store is now preparing to begin bargaining for a first union contract with \uc2 Apple\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think organizing my store is probably the hardest thing I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever done. It was a lot of work \u8211\'20\'13 six months of talking to people, campaigning, things like that, and then six weeks of some of the most intense working conditions as far as the fear that people end up having because people are just very anti-change in a lot of cases, and it can be scary,\u8221\'20\'1D said Forsythe.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut at the end of the day, when you\u8217\'20\'19re gaining better working conditions for yourself, the ability to take better care of yourself and things like that, it\u8217\'20\'19s worth six months of a struggle in order to lay a foundation for yourself and your co-workers so everybody else can have a much better experience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230131ej1v001jo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
