\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Shock and anger after fired worker killed by police at Oklahoma pork plant\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 968 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 January 2023\par 12:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chiewelthap Mariar, 26-year-old Sudanese refugee, shot dead after police called to escort him from Seaboard Foods factory in Guymon\par \par \uc2 Workers at a pork processing plant in Oklahoma have condemned the use of police by management that resulted in the killing of a worker who had just been fired.\par \par \uc2 Chiewelthap Mariar, a 26-year-old refugee from Sudan, was killed by police officers while working at the Seaboard Foods meatpacking plant in Guymon on 9 January.\par \par \uc2 A worker who filmed parts of the incident on his cellphone, and was later fired for doing so, requested to remain anonymous for fear of further retaliation. The worker claimed Mariar was fired from his job by a supervisor but was told by human resources to finish his shift.\par \par \uc2 The worker said the supervisor who fired him confronted Mariar on the shop floor after he was fired, and police arrived soon after to escort Mariar from the site. Seaboard Foods did not comment on but did not refute this characterization of the situation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI witnessed the entire thing, from when they started arguing with him until he was shot,\u8221\'20\'1D said the worker. \u8220\'20\'1CHe had a company-issued band-cutter in his hand. When the police got to the plant, the guy was already working, minding his own business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The worker provided cellphone footage leading up to and following the incident, where Mariar can be seen with the band-cutter in his hand working around other employees and being confronted by officers on the shop floor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey made him out to be a danger when they said he had a knife in his hand, when it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t. And that\u8217\'20\'19s wrong on so many levels,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said.\par \par \uc2 The worker claimed employees were told to keep working after the incident occurred.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI worked in maintenance. All they had us do was cover the scene with plastic, and we proceeded to finish what was on the production line,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker added. \u8220\'20\'1CThis company fired me for recording the truth they were trying to brush under the mat. They never asked me if I was OK. It was my first time seeing a guy get killed \u8211\'20\'13 and then I get fired.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The worker also claimed they were asked to sign an incident report, despite not agreeing with what was pre-filled out on the report.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Seaboard Corporation\uc2 , the parent company of Seaboard Foods, said: \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing the incident, operations were ceased for the remainder of the evening and the following day, and we provided in-person counseling services for employees throughout the week, in addition to ongoing phone counseling services available 24 hours, seven days a week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe express our heartfelt sorrow to Chiewelthap Mariar\u8217\'20\'19s family, co-workers, friends and those affected by his death following an incident at our Guymon processing plant involving the Guymon police department on 9 January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProviding our employees with a safe work environment and their wellbeing is extremely important to us. Following repeated attempts to bring calm to the situation, we requested assistance from the Guymon police as we felt it was in the best interest for everyone\u8217\'20\'19s safety.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company did not comment on any details regarding the situation or comment on the worker who claimed they were fired for taking cellphone footage, saying the company does not comment on personnel matters. They deferred further questions to the Oklahoma state bureau of investigation.\par \par \uc2 On 10 January, the OSBI issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/OSBI.OK/posts/pfbid0jCNbEPxtidbCvv1FFAUyJmXHJAz3yBjsmQCs9dkUPCXnF1CUxvAEh577aqZepb3sl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release}}}\uc2  that said the incident was being investigated.\par \par \uc2 The press release claimed Mariar brandished a knife, approached officers who attempted to use a Taser that failed, and then Mariar was shot by the officers at the scene. Mariar was then transported to a hospital where he was pronounced dead.\par \par \uc2 The OSBI declined to comment beyond the press release and did not clarify whether the knife the police referred to was the company-issued band-cutter seen in cellphone video footage.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seaboardfoods.com/facts-figures/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 2,600 employees}}}\uc2  work at the Guymon plant, operated under a subsidiary of the \uc2 Seaboard Corporation\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/company/seaboard/fortune500/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the largest }}}\uc2  companies in the world with over $9bn in annual revenue. The plant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seaboardcorp.com/our-companies/seaboard-foods/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 processes}}}\uc2  6 million pigs annually.\par \par \uc2 The plant was criticized during the Covid pandemic due to the high rates of infection among employees. By April 2021, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kosu.org/food-drink/2021-04-15/local-union-files-covid-safety-complaint-against-seaboard-foods-in-guymon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 41%}}}\uc2  of workers at the plant had tested positive for Covid. Some sick workers died from the virus.\par \par \uc2 In June last year, the plant was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://investigatemidwest.org/2022/06/08/osha-cites-seaboard-foods-pork-plant-for-failing-to-document-worker-injuries-and-illnesses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  cited }}}\uc2  by Osha, the \uc2 federal Occupational Safety and Health Administration\uc2 , for failing to properly document worker injuries and illnesses 51 times in the span of two months. The plant had also been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://investigatemidwest.org/2022/05/19/in-rare-case-a-large-meatpacking-plant-is-being-forced-to-address-workers-repetitive-motion-injuries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  by Osha in December 2021 for ergonomic problems facing workers on the job.\par \par \uc2 US police killings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/06/us-police-killings-record-number-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reached }}}\uc2  a record high in 2022, with at least 1,176 deaths, about 100 people per month.\par \par \uc2 Another employee at the Seaboard plant who works a different shift criticized management for calling police on a worker and bringing them into the plant. The worker claimed the human-resources unit on site was difficult to deal with.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to bring the police in,\u8221\'20\'1D said the worker. \u8220\'20\'1CThe whole thing is unfair. He did not have to have his life taken away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union representing workers at the plant, \uc2 United Food and Commercial Workers (UFCW)\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/ufcw2/posts/pfbid02tc6V597eBtoRboAGQkHPfykRsDB2ZDSGoe1YraqdW1aiDPrhUMFHMJZdnuKhTD3Zl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called }}}\uc2  for a federal investigation into the incident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr Mariar and his family came to this country to escape the violence and strife of Sudan, settled in Guymon, Oklahoma, to contribute to the economy of our country, and died senselessly on the shop floor,\u8221\'20\'1D said Martin Rosas, \uc2 UFCW\uc2  local 2 president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChiewelthap, his family, his community, and his fellow workers deserve justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230120ej1k001mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
