\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Congress must listen to working families and overhaul healthcare, minimum wage and education\b0\par\par\uc2 Bernie Sanders \par \uc2 1,106 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 January 2023\par 17:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Americans are united on some of the most important issues facing our country and they want government to address them\par \par \uc2 I am proud to be assuming the chairmanship of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s health, education, labor and pensions committee (Help), a committee with wide jurisdiction over some of the most important issues facing the American people. As I move into that position I\u8217\'20\'19m thinking about how we can best address some of the serious challenges facing my fellow Vermonters and working families all across the country.\par \par \uc2 Today, in terms of health, we have a dysfunctional healthcare system in which we spend the astronomical and unsustainable sum of nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cms.gov/research-statistics-data-and-systems/statistics-trends-and-reports/nationalhealthexpenddata/nationalhealthaccountshistorical"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $13,000}}}\uc2  for every man, woman and child, twice as much as most developed countries and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cms.gov/research-statistics-data-and-systems/statistics-trends-and-reports/nationalhealthexpenddata/nhe-fact-sheet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost 20%}}}\uc2  of our GDP. Yet, despite that huge expenditure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/publications/issue-briefs/2022/sep/state-us-health-insurance-2022-biennial-survey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 85 million}}}\uc2  Americans are uninsured or underinsured and we have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/press-release/2021/new-international-study-us-health-system-ranks-last-among-11-countries-many"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worse health outcomes}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.healthsystemtracker.org/chart-collection/u-s-life-expectancy-compare-countries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lower life expectancy}}}\uc2  than many other nations. While the insurance companies make huge profits, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2019/02/11/this-is-the-real-reason-most-americans-file-for-bankruptcy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 500,000 people}}}\uc2  declare bankruptcy each year from medically related debt, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(19)33019-3/fulltext#%20?eType=EmailBlastContent&eId=ac666dcf-c1bb-4eb0-a6ea-39c4a9bb5321"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 68,000 die}}}\uc2  because they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford the care they need. Our complicated and fragmented system is so broken that it cannot even produce the number of doctors, nurses, dentists and mental health personnel that we desperately need.\par \par \uc2 As a nation, we must focus on the reality that the function of a rational healthcare system is to provide quality care for all, not simply huge profits for the insurance industry.\par \par \uc2 Today, as we pay by far the highest prices in the world for prescription drugs, the pharmaceutical industry is making record-breaking profits and more than a few executives in drug companies are becoming billionaires. Meanwhile, despite billions in government investment in prescription drug research and development, nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/health-costs/press-release/poll-nearly-1-in-4-americans-taking-prescription-drugs-say-its-difficult-to-afford-medicines-including-larger-shares-with-low-incomes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one out of four Americans}}}\uc2  are unable to afford the medicine their doctors prescribe and too many seniors are splitting their lifesaving pills in half because they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford them. And because Medicare doesn\u8217\'20\'19t cover dental, hearing and vision, there are millions of seniors who are trying to survive without these basic healthcare needs.\par \par \uc2 The American people know that no one can survive on $7.25 an hour minimum wage\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s not just our healthcare \u8220\'20\'1Csystem\u8221\'20\'1D which needs a major overhaul. In terms of education, we need to take a hard look at how we are educating our kids \u8211\'20\'13 from childcare to graduate school.\par \par \uc2 While psychologists tell us that the first four years of life are the most important in terms of human intellectual and emotional growth, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to deny that our childcare system is in disarray. The cost is unaffordable for many working parents, there are not enough slots available, the quality is spotty and the pay and benefits childcare workers receive is unconscionably low. This is not how we should be treating our children, the future of America.\par \par \uc2 The situation in K-12 education is not much better. For a variety of reasons \u8211\'20\'13 lack of respect, low pay, the stress of Covid and the politicization of school boards \u8211\'20\'13 thousands of gifted and dedicated teachers are quitting the profession, leaving students unprepared for the challenges they face as they enter the adult world. The future of this country depends upon the quality of education we provide our kids, and there is no reason why we cannot create the best public educational system in the world.\par \par \uc2 In terms of higher education, we face the absurd situation of hundreds of thousands of bright young people who have the desire and ability to get a college education but cannot do so because their families lack the money. How many great doctors, scientists, and teachers are we losing as a result? There are also millions of young people who need training in order to become skilled mechanics, carpenters, welders, and electricians who are not getting the post-high school training they need. Further, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/education/2022/05/22/student-loan-borrowers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 45 million Americans}}}\uc2  are struggling with student debt \u8211\'20\'13 sometimes in the hundreds of thousands of dollars.\par \par \uc2 In terms of labor and our economy, we must recognize that we live in a period of more income and wealth inequality than at any time in the last hundred years. While the very rich become richer and three people now own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2019/jul/03/bernie-sanders/bernie-sanders-target-saying-3-richest-have-much-w/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more wealth}}}\uc2  than the bottom half of American society, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/11/18/60percent-of-americans-live-paycheck-to-paycheck-heading-into-2022-holiday.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60%}}}\uc2  of American workers live paycheck to paycheck and millions are trying to exist on starvation wages. Meanwhile, we have a pathetic federal minimum wage of $7.25 per hour which has not been raised since 2009.\par \par \uc2 As more and more workers try to improve their standard of living by forming unions, they are facing fierce and illegal union busting from such employers as \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , Amazon, \uc2 McDonalds\uc2  and other major employers.\par \par \uc2 There is a lot of discussion in the media about how \u8220\'20\'1Cdivided\u8221\'20\'1D our nation is and, on many issues, that is absolutely true. But what we don\u8217\'20\'19t appreciate is that on some of the most important issues facing our country the American people \u8211\'20\'13 Democrats, Republicans, independents \u8211\'20\'13 are quite united.\par \par \uc2 The American people know we are being ripped off by the drug companies and they want lower prescription drugs prices.\par \par \uc2 The American people know that our healthcare system is outrageously expensive and they want universal and lower cost health care.\par \par \uc2 The American people know that education is essential to our lives and the future of this country and they want high quality and affordable education from childcare to graduate school.\par \par \uc2 The American people know that no one can survive on a $7.25-an-hour minimum wage, and they want to raise the minimum wage to a living wage.\par \par \uc2 The American people know that workers have a constitutional right to form unions and that corporations that engage in illegal union busting activities must be held accountable.\par \par \uc2 And these are just a few of the issues within the jurisdiction of the Help committee that a strong majority of the American people want us to address.\par \par \uc2 At a time when too many Americans are giving up on democracy, now is the time to attempt to restore faith in our government. Now is the time for Congress to have the courage to take on the lobbyists and powerful special interests and show the American people that our government can work for them, and not just the 1%. Let\u8217\'20\'19s do it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders is a US senator, and the ranking member of the Senate budget committee. He represents the state of Vermont, and is the longest-serving independent in the history of Congress\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230110ej1a000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
