\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Holidays are the hardest\u8217\'20\'19: striking US workers rally round over festive season\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 955 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mine workers in Alabama among those organizing gift drives and strike funds to try to spread some holiday cheer\par \par \uc2 Groups of US workers have been on strike for long periods of time and they remain at loggerheads with their employers over the holiday period on issues such as pay, benefits, quality of life and staffing.\par \par \uc2 Workers have been forced to ramp up organizing efforts to mitigate the effects of lost income for those on strike, to ensure families are taken care of financially and with holiday gift drives.\par \par \uc2 Over 1,000 coalminers at \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  in Alabama, represented by the \uc2 United Mine Workers of America\uc2 , have been on strike for more than 600 days, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/01/striking-coalminers-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since 1 April last year}}}\uc2 , over lagging pay and the recoupment of concessions workers made through a bankruptcy in their previous contract.\par \par \uc2 The strike is currently the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/alabama-coal-strike-women-families-1849812070"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 longest}}}\uc2  in the US and the longest in Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe members are holding up really well, but they are tired and ready for a contract. Warrior Met doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to give them a decent contract after they took a substantial cut in benefits to help \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  become a very profitable company,\u8221\'20\'1D said Larry Spencer of the \uc2 UMWA\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe men and women of the \uc2 United Mine Workers\uc2  are sticking together through these hard times, and holidays are some of the hardest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strike has been contentious, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/picketing-alabama-miners-stopped-by-rare-non-federal-court-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restraining orders}}}\uc2  issued against workers holding picket lines outside company sites, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://umwa.org/news-media/journal/keeping-the-pressure-on-blackrock/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallies }}}\uc2  in New York City to pressure the private equity firm \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 , \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s largest shareholder.\par \par \uc2 Haeden Wright, the wife of a striking coalminer and auxiliary president of the \uc2 UMWA\uc2  locals 2245 and 2368, helps organize rallies for workers and helps to coordinate a pantry for miners and their families. It provides groceries, hygiene products and toiletries, and organizes events like a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MineWorkers/status/1598337162143055873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Santa brunch }}}\uc2  before Christmas to keep morale up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have ever imagined that we would now be on strike for the second Christmas, or the second time during the holidays,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wright. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is hard when you have to learn to tell your kids now that we can\u8217\'20\'19t afford things, you have to go without that. You don\u8217\'20\'19t have satellite TV any more, you don\u8217\'20\'19t go on vacation, you don\u8217\'20\'19t really go anywhere to eat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor a lot of us it meant that when heaters went out, when air conditioning went out, we can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to replace those.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said holiday gift registries for workers\u8217\'20\'19 families were already all fulfilled by early November, as a testament to the public\u8217\'20\'19s support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour union is your family, it\u8217\'20\'19s your community. If you ask for help, people are going to help. You\u8217\'20\'19re there for each other,\u8221\'20\'1D Wright added.\par \par \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  has not made any recent comments on the strike.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=cnh+strike+starts+april&sxsrf=ALiCzsY2sNVrIiVvS6GH3eAznJFM81Knfg%3A1670783426347&ei=wiGWY8XjFKW6ggess7G4DA&ved=0ahUKEwjFzP6kmfL7AhUlneAKHaxZDMcQ4dUDCBA&uact=5&oq=cnh+strike+starts+april&gs_lcp=Cgxnd3Mtd2l6LXNlcnAQAzIFCCEQoAE6CggAEEcQ1gQQsAM6BwgAELADEEM6BAgAEEM6BQgAEIAEOgsIABCABBCxAxCDAToGCAAQFhAeOgUIIRCrAkoECEEYAEoECEYYAFCvA1iDJGCIJmgBcAF4AIAB-QGIAaMQkgEFMS44LjSYAQCgAQHIAQrAAQE&sclient=gws-wiz-serp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 1,000 workers}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Case New Holland (CNH)\uc2 , an agriculture and construction equipment manufacturer, in Burlington, Iowa, and Racine, Wisconsin, represented by the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 , have been on strike since 1 May, when their union contract expired.\par \par \uc2 Workers are still holding the strike line and organizing support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gofundme.com/f/help-the-striking-uaw-local-807-cnh-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike funds }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.target.com/gift-registry/gift-giver?registryId=8f976a90-5369-11ed-8f43-8df68657f04c&type=CHARITY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 holiday gift registries}}}\uc2 , with a solidarity day of rallies and caravans planned in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Tracy Chew, an employee at CNH in Burlington and chair of the women\u8217\'20\'19s committee for \uc2 UAW\uc2  local 807, said the unions have had few workers cross the strike line and are optimistic in pushing for the US labor secretary, Marty Walsh, to mediate the dispute now that the railroad contract fight and midterm elections are over.\par \par \uc2 Chew said the distance between the unions and CNH on any agreement revolves around rising health insurance costs CNH is trying to impose on workers that would cancel out settled wage increases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at the 23% wage increase, it looks good, but it will be consumed by the insurance. So it\u8217\'20\'19s not a gain, and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to sign a contract that we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to gain [from],\u8221\'20\'1D said Chew.\par \par \uc2 Chew is currently organizing gift drives and coordinating with community groups to ensure families on strike are taken care of.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re working diligently. But I know it\u8217\'20\'19s tough. I know that it\u8217\'20\'19s a mental fog for a lot of these people. Our mental health has probably gone through the roof,\u8221\'20\'1D added Chew. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a war situation right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for CNH said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been negotiating in good faith to reach an agreement that is fair and reasonable to our employees, our company and our customers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Hawaii, over 50 mental health care workers have been on strike at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  since August, over staffing problems that have disrupted patient care and for improvements to wages and benefits. Workers first unionized at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  in Hawaii in 2018 and have yet to reach a first contract agreement.\par \par \uc2 The strike is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawaiipublicradio.org/local-news/2022-11-11/kaiser-mental-health-workers-have-been-on-strike-for-over-70-days"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 longest }}}\uc2  by mental health therapists in US history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe got into this wanting Kaiser to hire more therapists. That\u8217\'20\'19s the only thing that is going to reduce the wait times and improve care for our patients,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andrea Kumura, a social worker at \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  in Oahu.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s difficult going without a paycheck, but people have been very generous in donating to our strike fund, which makes it possible for us to keep up the good fight. Kaiser obviously isn\u8217\'20\'19t concerned about the care their patients have been getting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kaiser Permanente\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kpinhawaii.org/laborupdate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disputed}}}\uc2  allegations of failing to address staffing concerns and says it continues to bargain in good faith with the union.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej14001qq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
