\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Touchscreens, conveyor belts: \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opens first largely automated location\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Test restaurant near Fort Worth, Texas, has drawn ire of activists calling for living wage\par \par \uc2 The first mostly non-human-run McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s is open for business just outside Fort Worth, Texas.\par \par \uc2 At just one location so far, customers can drive to the golden arches and expect to be served a Big Mac or a Happy Meal by a food and beverage conveyor instead of an actual, real-life human being.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s told the Guardian that the test concept \u8220\'20\'1Cis not fully automated\u8221\'20\'1D, emphasizing that the restaurant does employ a team comparable to that of a traditional store.\par \par \uc2 Smaller than a typical \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s, the location is geared towards customers on the go rather than those who plan to dine inside. It limits interactions between team members and customers and uses \u8220\'20\'1Cenhanced technology that allows the restaurant team to begin preparing customers\u8217\'20\'19 orders when they\u8217\'20\'19re near the restaurant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The goal of the test is to improve order speed and accuracy.\par \par \uc2 Customers can pick up their meals in a drive-through \u8220\'20\'1Corder ahead lane\u8221\'20\'1D or order at the touchscreen kiosk inside the store.\par \par \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s called the concept \u8220\'20\'1Cmore seamless than ever before\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the stunt drew the ire of activists, who criticized the fast food corporation for entertaining the idea of a costly automatic restaurant rather than pay its workers a living wage.\par \par \uc2 The minimum wage in Texas is $7.25/hour. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GVqCtW2VpO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GVqCtW2VpO}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Nina Turner (@ninaturner) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ninaturner/status/1605935263712022529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In Texas, the minimum wage is $7.25 an hour and hasn\u8217\'20\'19t increased in nearly a decade. It ranks above only Georgia and Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage of $5.15, which is $2.10 less than the US federal minimum wage. Five other states have not adopted a set minimum wage: Alabama, Louisiana, Mississippi, South Carolina, and Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 Across the country, most \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s workers earn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/how-much-retail-food-companies-pay-workers-per-hour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than $15}}}\uc2  an hour \u8211\'20\'13 far below a living wage in nearly every state. \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s is one of 300 publicly held companies with the lowest median worker wages, according to a 2021 Institute for Policy Studies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ips-dc.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/report-executive-excess-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The test restaurant plays into fears that jobs will one day be taken over by robots and automation, replacing the need for human employees.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej14001c6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
