\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Largest-ever US higher education strike ends after \u8216\'20\'18landmark\u8217\'20\'19 deal\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 526 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Agreement hailed as a new national standard, boosting wages and working conditions for students employed at public universities\par \par \uc2 Academic workers in California have ended a nearly six-week strike, described as the largest ever to hit US higher education, after approving a \u8220\'20\'1Clandmark\u8221\'20\'1D agreement for higher wages on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The strikes across the University of California (UC) system {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/02/closed-labs-cancelled-classes-inside-us-higher-education-largest-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ground campus life to a halt}}}\uc2 , disrupting classes and exams as thousands formed picket lines and staged noisy protests to demand better pay.\par \par \uc2 The strike was groundbreaking in its size, bringing together 48,000 teaching assistants, researchers, tutors and other graduate student instructors across the nine-campus system, which includes famous universities such as \uc2 UC Berkeley\uc2  and UCLA. Striking workers said the low wages they earn make it impossible to live in the cities where they work.\par \par \uc2 Academic workers represented by the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 will return to work in January after the winter break, union leaders said, after ratification votes by large majorities of two fractious \uc2 UAW\uc2  bargaining units.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe University of California welcomes the ratification of these agreements with our valued graduate student employees,\u8221\'20\'1D executive director of system-wide labor relations Letitia Silas said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://universityofcalifornia.edu/press-room/university-california-graduate-student-workers-end-strike-ratify-three-year-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s ratification demonstrates yet again the university\u8217\'20\'19s strong commitment to providing every one of our hardworking employees with competitive compensation and benefit packages that honor their many contributions to our institution, to our community, and to the state of California,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 When the strike began, the union said its members were working themselves into extreme debt with a base salary for part-time employees starting at $24,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 The thousands of striking academic workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reut.rs/3YPffOQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began voting}}}\uc2  last week on whether to ratify the deal that was reached by union leaders and university administrators after a series of negotiations.\par \par \uc2 The agreement was hailed by union and university supporters as a landmark labor deal that would set a new national standard, boosting wages and working conditions for graduate students employed at public universities.\par \par \uc2 The agreement would provide wage increases of up to 66% over the two-and-a-half-year life of the contract, according to leaders of the two \uc2 UAW union\uc2  locals representing the 36,000 graduate students covered by the deal.\par \par \uc2 By the fall term of 2024, the minimum nine-month salary for teaching assistants would rise to $36,500 at \uc2 UC Berkeley\uc2 , \uc2 UC San Francisco\uc2  and UCLA, and to $34,000 at other campuses, according to the university. Graduate student researchers will make at least $40,000, according to union representatives, and workers can get childcare subsidies of more than $2,000 a semester.\par \par \uc2 Some detractors said the pact falls short in meeting the living costs grad students face in pricey cities where many UC campuses are located \u8211\'20\'13 such as Berkeley, Los Angeles and San Diego \u8211\'20\'13 and critics faulted the deal for giving up on union demands to tie wage gains to housing costs.\par \par \uc2 The university system applauded the new contracts, which it said will take immediate effect and run through 31 May 2025.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej14000p3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
