\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Railroad workers pressure Congress and Biden to address working conditions\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 673 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2022\par 10:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers and labor activists criticize Congress after it blocked a strike by voting to impose a contract agreement\par \par \uc2 Railroad workers and unions are ramping up pressure on the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to address poor working conditions in the wake of the recent move to block a strike when Congress voted to impose a contract agreement.\par \par \uc2 Workers and labor activists in America have criticized that action for undermining the collective bargaining process in the US and workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to strike.\par \par \uc2 Twelve labor unions representing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2022/12/01/rail-deal-strike-senate-vote-congress/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 115,000 railroad workers}}}\uc2  across the US had been negotiating with railway carriers since 2019 on a new union contract. By September the prospect of a strike threatened to shut down down the US railroads and hit the US economy to an estimated $2bn a day. That eventually prompted Congress \u8211\'20\'13 backed by the president \u8211\'20\'13 to impose the settlement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou always knew that this was the culmination of the process, you knew that Congress was going to push you back to work, you just didn\u8217\'20\'19t know when and under what conditions that you\u8217\'20\'19d be put back to work,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ross Grooters, a locomotive engineer based in Iowa and co-chair of Railroad Workers United.\par \par \uc2 Railroad workers had pushed for paid sick days to provide relief for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/14/completely-demoralized-us-railroad-workers-pushed-to-brink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grueling schedules}}}\uc2  caused by of labor cuts, with many workers on call 24/7 every day of the year, often having to work while sick or forgo doctor\u8217\'20\'19s appointments because of their scheduling demands and strict disciplinary policies around attendance.\par \par \uc2 As conditions have worsened, railroad carriers have made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.progressiverailroading.com/bnsf_railway/news/BNSF-posts-record-earnings-for-2021--66004#:~:text=For%20full%2Dyear%202021%2C%20BNSF,up%2010%25%20year%20over%20year."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record profits}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/sep/14/us-railroad-strike-union-pacific-bnsf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent }}}\uc2  billions of dollars on stock buybacks and dividends to shareholders. Meanwhile, US railroad jobs have declined significantly in recent years, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/sep/14/us-railroad-strike-union-pacific-bnsf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1m}}}\uc2  in the 1950s to fewer than 150,000 in 2022, with drastic recent losses as the industry experienced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2021/article/employment-in-rail-transportation-heads-downhill-between-november-2018-and-december-2020.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduction of 40,000 workers}}}\uc2  between November 2018 and December 2020.\par \par \uc2 Now the imposed contract provides just one extra day of personal time off, with no days allotted for illnesses, and three days a year for doctor appointments with stipulations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight to guarantee paid sick leave for rail workers is not over and we will not back down until we win,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Transportation Trades Department of AFL-CIO in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ttd.org/news-and-media/press-releases/rail-labor-will-not-rest-until-the-freight-rail-industry-is-fixed-and-rail-workers-are-treated-fairly/?link_id=0&can_id=215fcd9e80e1ae942196713f39151192&source=email-rail-labor-will-not-rest-until-the-freight-rail-industry-is-fixed-and-rail-workers-are-treated-fairly&email_referrer=email_1762304&email_subject=rail-labor-will-not-rest-until-the-freight-rail-industry-is-fixed-and-rail-workers-are-treated-fairly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are committed to aggressively pursuing further action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Railroad workers\u8217\'20\'19 unions held a rally at the US Capitol in Washington DC earlier this week to push for action on issues facing railroad workers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://smart-union.org/2022-rail-solidarity-rally/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Additional rallies }}}\uc2  are planned in Massachusetts, Iowa, Colorado, Illinois, Minnesota, Nevada, New Mexico, Ohio, Utah and Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 More than 70 members of Congress have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mobile.twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1601293615166525440"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a letter}}}\uc2  urging Biden to guarantee seven days of paid sick leave for railroad workers.\par \par \uc2 The Federal Railway Administration also held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.progressiverailroading.com/federal_legislation_regulation/news/FRA-sets-hearing-on-two-person-train-crew-rule--67861"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2  on 14 December on a proposed rule to mandate a two-person train crew safety rule which is being opposed by the rail industry that has been trying to impose train crews of one worker. This week the \uc2 Surface Transportation Board\uc2  is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stb.gov/news-communications/latest-news/pr-22-49/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  holding hearings}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in supply chain issues.\par \par \uc2 Since the contract was imposed without sick time, investors at two railroad carriers, \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2  and \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2 , have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-railroad-investor-resolutions-urge-paid-sick-leave-workers-2022-12-05/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  shareholder resolutions to provide workers with a reasonable amount of paid sick time.\par \par \uc2 As the fight continues on paid sick leave, workers are already mobilizing ahead of the next contract fight, which begins in two years.\par \par \uc2 Grooters explained the recent contract fight had increased public awareness of the plight railroad workers face.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are very difficult jobs and the people doing them deserve lives outside of the railroad,\u8221\'20\'1D said Grooters. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we can\u8217\'20\'19t get relief, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very hard to find people that are willing to do this work and we don\u8217\'20\'19t want that. Continuing to reduce railroad staffing feeds into the problems we have with quality of life. We need more people working for the railroad, not less.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221216eicg001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
