\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 University of California workers continue strike amid threat of arrests\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 490 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 December 2022\par 08:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Strike of 48,000 is largest in history of US higher education as some workers protest at offices of high-level university administrators\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of academic workers throughout the University of California are currently on their fourth week of striking for a new union contract and the situation is intensifying amid the threat of arrests after direct actions by some strikers.\par \par \uc2 The strike of 48,000 academic workers, including graduate workers, academic researchers, postdoctoral scholars and teaching assistants, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/12/california-university-strike-graduate-workers-pay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began}}}\uc2  on 14 November and is the largest in the history of higher education in the US.\par \par \uc2 This week workers have participated in numerous direct actions across the state, protesting at the offices of high-level university administrators as academic workers are pushing for pay increases, job security protections, childcare reimbursements, sustainable transit incentives and stronger disability accommodations.\par \par \uc2 Seventeen people were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kron4.com/news/bay-area/17-people-cited-for-trespassing-after-sit-in-at-uc-office-of-the-president-sacramento/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  for trespassing during a sit-in protest on 5 December at the University of California president\u8217\'20\'19s office in Sacramento.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m engaging in this act of civil disobedience because the stakes are incredibly high, and the UC is not demonstrating that they understand that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jess Banks, a member of the bargaining team at \uc2 UC Berkeley\uc2 , in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CUC thinks they can end negotiations and send us back to work, but this strike will continue until they stop breaking the law and settle a fair contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On 7 December, 10 academic workers from UCLA were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/uaw2865/status/1600593225575591936"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  at the University of California\u8217\'20\'19s regents office on trespassing charges.\par \par \uc2 About 12,000 postdoctoral researchers and academic researchers reached a tentative agreement with the University of California on 29 November, which included pay increases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/02/closed-labs-cancelled-classes-inside-us-higher-education-largest-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 up to 29%}}}\uc2 , but have continued striking in solidarity with other academic workers still pushing for a deal and while the agreement is put to the membership for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fairucnow.org/bargaining/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Michael Dean, a PhD candidate in the history department at UCLA and bargaining committee member with UAW Local 2865, said the most recent offer from the university included language that would demand the union halt the strike before membership votes on whether to approve or reject the tentative agreement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are trying to cut off negotiations,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dean. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s just an impasse of will on the UC\u8217\'20\'19s part, so we\u8217\'20\'19ve been organizing these direct actions all over the state to call on the UC to make more progress in addressing the economic precarity that grad workers face.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Graduate workers at UC have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/12/california-university-strike-graduate-workers-pay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  issues in affording rent, food and basic necessities in the cities they work and live in on salaries averaging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/02/closed-labs-cancelled-classes-inside-us-higher-education-largest-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about $23,000 annually}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re preparing to come back with counter proposals of our own,\u8221\'20\'1D added Dean. \u8220\'20\'1CIn terms of the strike and the pickets, we\u8217\'20\'19re out here every day and we\u8217\'20\'19re not planning to go away until they offer us fair contracts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221210eica00108\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
