\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Grossly underpaid\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 Disney\uc2  workers demand higher wages as living costs soar\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 789 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 December 2022\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees at Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Magic Kingdom say paychecks have not kept up even as company records $3.6bn operational profit\par \par \uc2 Earl Penson has worked for 11 years as a food handler, managing and distributing deliveries for the Disney World theme park in Orlando, Florida, but makes just 50 cents more an hour than a new employee starting at \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s current minimum wage set at $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 He works over 40 hours a week at the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CMagic Kingdom\u8221\'20\'1D, starting work around 2am, working anywhere from eight to 10 hours or more, and takes side gigs as an electrician to make extra money.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re grossly, grossly underpaid for the hours that we work and the heavy lifting, it\u8217\'20\'19s like warehouse and driver work. A lot of us have the same story in not being able to afford the cost of living on the pay that we make,\u8221\'20\'1D said Penson. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of \uc2 Disney\uc2  workers are barely squeaking by. You have workers with families sleeping in their car.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Around 70,000 employees at Disney World, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bizjournals.com/bizwomen/news/latest-news/2022/02/disney-kicks-off-fiscal-2022-with-big-growth.html?page=all#:~:text=Walt%20Disney%20World%2C%20the%20nation's,previous%20years%20%E2%80%94%20many%20of%20those"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest single-site }}}\uc2  employer in the US and world\u8217\'20\'19s largest theme park, are currently pushing for wage increases through new union contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 The Services Trades Council Union (STCU), a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2022/11/walt-disney-world-workers-march-near-park-wage-increase-1235185689/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coalition}}}\uc2  of six unions that represents 42,000 workers, are pushing for wage increases that account for inflationary pressures and the high cost of living in the Orlando area. The current contract that expired in October 2022, which includes a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uniteherelocal362.org/wp-content/uploads/FINAL-2014-Part-Time-STCU-CBA.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no-strike clause}}}\uc2 , is extended until a new contract is reached.\par \par \uc2 In the previous contract in 2018, \uc2 Disney\uc2  workers successfully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/xwma3q/when-working-in-disney-world-means-being-stuck-living-in-a-cheap-motel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed }}}\uc2  for a $15 minimum wage, which they received in late 2021.\par \par \uc2 But workers say these wages currently don\u8217\'20\'19t correlate with the workloads and job duties they perform and aren\u8217\'20\'19t enough to keep up with the rising costs of living. According to the MIT Living Wage Calculator, a living wage for an individual with no dependents in Orange county, Florida, is currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://livingwage.mit.edu/counties/12095"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $18.19 an hour}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A lot of \uc2 Disney\uc2  workers are barely squeaking by. You have workers with families sleeping in their car\par \par \uc2 Earl Penson\par \par \uc2 Penson\u8217\'20\'19s father was a chef at \uc2 Disney\uc2  and encouraged him to start working there over a decade ago after he was struggling to find work as an electrician, and had moved back in with his parents due to the soaring costs of rent. He criticized \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s current wage offerings and opposition to the union\u8217\'20\'19s current proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really heartbreaking, it\u8217\'20\'19s a morale downer, because you would think they would recognize how hard the cast members work,\u8221\'20\'1D added Penson. \u8220\'20\'1CI wish they would let us know that they appreciate the magic that we bring. Every one of us is a part of the magic of \uc2 Disney\uc2  and we enjoy making the magic. We just want to be compensated for making the magic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other workers agree. A \uc2 Disney\uc2  housekeeping worker who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation, explained the pay is nowhere close to where it needs to be in line with the costs of living in the Orlando area. They recently had a newborn son and received no paid leave.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith Christmas around the corner we\u8217\'20\'19re beyond stressed,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CGroceries are limited because we just can\u8217\'20\'19t afford it. It\u8217\'20\'19s genuinely an emergency for our survival at this point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uniteherelocal737.org/wp-content/uploads/L737-Orlando-Tourism-Workers-Need-a-Raise-06.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent report}}}\uc2  published by \uc2 UNITE HERE\uc2  found tourism workers in the Orlando area are experiencing issues in affording rent and food as the industry has surpassed pre-pandemic profits, with average rents in the area surging by 23.7% over the past year.\par \par \uc2 The unions are pushing for an immediate wage increase to $18 an hour and a path to $20 an hour for all employees. Workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wdwnt.com/2022/11/cast-members-protest-low-working-wages-by-walt-disney-world/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organized }}}\uc2  a protest outside of \uc2 Disney\uc2  in Kissimmee, Florida, on 30 November, calling on the company to enact immediate wage increases to stave off issues in affording rent, healthcare and basic needs.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  has currently offered a path to $20 an hour in five years, with $1 an hour raise annually. \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s parks division {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/10/business/disney-earnings-profit.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  $28.7bn in revenue in fiscal year 2022, with a $3.6bn operating profit.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Disney\uc2  said in regards to the proposals: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have presented a strong and meaningful offer that far outpaces Florida minimum wage by at least $5 an hour and immediately takes starting wages for certain roles including bus drivers, housekeepers and culinary up to a minimum of $20 an hour while providing a path to $20 for all other full-time, non-tipped STCU roles during the contract term.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221208eic8001be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
