\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Ukraine says it has shot down 60 of over 70 missiles launched after explosions at two Russian airbases \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Tom Ambrose (now); Miranda Bryant and Samantha Lock (earlier) \par \uc2 8,036 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 December 2022\par 19:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 No reports of missile impacts in Kyiv but two killed in Zaporizhzhia and Odesa hit hard after Russian strike follows blasts at Russian airfields. This blog is now closedAt a glance: what we know on day 285 of the invasion\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 The time in Kyiv is coming up to 9pm. Here is a round-up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s main news stories:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine shot down more than 60 of over 70 missiles launched by Russia in a massed missile strike on Monday, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s air force command said. The strikes targeted Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s critical infrastructure, the air force said in a statement on the Telegram messaging app.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russian missiles have crashed into buildings in the southern Ukrainian region of Zaporizhzhia, destroying several houses and killing at least two people, a senior Ukrainian official has said. \uc2 Kyrylo Tymoshenko\uc2 , deputy head of the presidential office, gave no further details of the attacks, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Air defences shot down most of the Russian missiles fired at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  on Monday and energy workers have already begun work on restoring power supplies, Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said. Russia carried out the latest in a wave of airstrikes on Ukraine, destroying homes in the south and knocking out power in the north and killing at least two people, Ukrainian officials said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mysterious explosions took place at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638dc6188f08ec68b60189fc#block-638dc6188f08ec68b60189fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Russian airbases}}}\uc2  far from the frontlines on Monday, raising the possibility that Kyiv has found a way to target Russian long-range bombers used in attacks against Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Spanish police have intercepted three more envelopes containing animal eyes addressed to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s embassy in Madrid and its consulates in Barcelona and M\u225\'00\'E1laga, police sources close to the investigation said. Last week, Ukraine said a series of \u8220\'20\'1Cbloody packages\u8221\'20\'1D were sent to its missions across {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2 , soon after a letter bomb detonated at Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s embassy in Spain and police defused others sent to, among others, prime minister Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Canadian-made parts have been found in the \u8220\'20\'1Ckamikaze\u8221\'20\'1D Iranian drones used by Russia to attack {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , according to a report. An investigative project from the NGO Statewatch found components from 30 European and American companies, concluding antenna parts from Tallysman Wireless, a Canadian manufacturer. Iranian-made Shahed 136 drones have been used by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  in attacks against Ukraine, targeting civilian infrastructure. According to \uc2 Statewatch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s project Trap Aggressor, the Russian military renamed the drone Geran-2 to mask its origins.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House has said that the latest Russian strikes against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  are a reminder of the Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s brutality. John Kirby, the White House national security spokesperson, also told reporters that an oil price cap would not have any long-term impact on global oil prices, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia said that three of its military personnel were killed in what it said were Ukrainian drone attacks on two Russian airbases. Two aircraft were lightly damaged, the defence ministry said in a statement. Four other people had been wounded, it said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moldovan police on Monday found fragments of a missile that came down in a region of northern Moldova near the border with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , state information portal Prima Sursa quoted the police as saying. Moldovan authorities did not immediately comment publicly on the incident, which was reported after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  carried out a new wave of missile strikes on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s recent mobilisation has increased its military threat in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , with better-trained soldiers now arriving at the frontline, the commander of Ukrainian ground forces said. But he said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  was now using a lot of old equipment because it had no other way of replenishing supplies, and that Russian forces had made only slow progress around Bakhmut, one of the main battle zones in eastern Ukraine, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has driven across the Kerch Bridge, linking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  and the Crimean peninsula, after it was damaged by a truck bomb in October. The Russian president drove across the bridge today and spoke to workers and a senior government official, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 India gave a list of Indian products to Moscow for access to Russian markets, foreign minister \uc2 Subrahmanyam Jaishankar\uc2  said, as his country seeks to narrow a growing trade deficit with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  at a time when Moscow faces acute shortages of some crucial materials following western sanctions. Reuters reported last week that Moscow had sent India a list of more than 500 products for potential delivery, including parts for cars, aircraft and trains, as sanctions following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  squeeze its ability to keep vital industries running.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638dc6408f082ef70a2453e0#block-638dc6408f082ef70a2453e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has warned}}}\uc2  the new western price cap on Russian oil will destabilise global energy markets, but claimed it would not impact its invasion of Ukraine. Spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  was preparing its response to the move by the \uc2 G7\uc2  and allies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  has warned the west to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638daeaf8f08ec68b6018935#block-638daeaf8f08ec68b6018935"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoid creating a new cold war}}}\uc2  by dividing the world into blocs. Writing in an opinion piece for Foreign Affairs magazine, published today, the German chancellor called for every effort to be made to build new partnerships. He singled out China and Russia as two countries that pose a threat to a multipolar world.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638daafc8f082ef70a245302#block-638daafc8f082ef70a245302"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nine people have been killed}}}\uc2  in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern Luhansk, Russian-backed military officials have said. It came after Ukraine shelled the city of Alchevsk, Reuters reports, citing state-run TASS news agency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chinese foreign ministry\uc2  has said it will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638da1618f08f5eb2e3179cc#block-638da1618f08f5eb2e3179cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue energy cooperation}}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  after the \uc2 G7\uc2 , \uc2 EU\uc2  and Australia imposed a price cap on Russian oil exports. China, which said it would continue on the basis if respect and mutual benefit, has increased its purchases of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Urals oil blends this year.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Tom Ambrose, and indeed the Ukraine live blog for today. I\u8217\'20\'19ll be back tomorrow morning. Goodnight for now.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian officials have recently been hinting at developments in the country\u8217\'20\'19s grinding war with Russia. A long-range rocket, perhaps? Or a homemade modified drone? The apparent evidence of a new and unexpected weapon was visible on Monday morning, when mysterious explosions hit two Russian airbases.\par \par \uc2 Both took place a long way from the frontlines. Video from Russian social media showed a blast at the Engels-2 airbase in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Saratov region. Another happened at the Dyagilevo military airbase near Ryazan, a city just 150 miles from Moscow and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Kremlin. According to Russian state media, three people at the base were killed and five injured when a fuel truck went up in flames. At least two planes were reportedly damaged.\par \par \uc2 The exact cause of the explosion was uncertain. But it appears Ukraine has found a way to target Russia\u8217\'20\'19s long range Tu-95 and Tu-22M aircraft, which are stationed at the airstrips. Since October the Kremlin had used these strategic bombers to wreck Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s energy infrastructure, bit by bit, leaving millions without heat and electricity as winter arrives.\par \par \uc2 There is speculation Kyiv has developed a strike drone with an astonishing 1,000km range. Late last month a Ukrainian serviceman said the weapon had already been used against the Russian military. If accurate, this means much of European Russia is now in reach. And that the asymmetric advantage Moscow has enjoyed this year \u8211\'20\'13 the ability to launch cruise missiles safely from deep inside Russia itself \u8211\'20\'13 is under threat.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/05/strikes-deep-inside-russia-highlight-ukraines-tactical-ingenuity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Strikes deep inside Russia highlight Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s tactical ingenuity }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Details of the two Russian airbases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/05/explosions-russia-airbases-far-from-ukraine-frontline-bombers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rocked by explosions}}}\uc2  that may have been pre-emptive strikes by Kyiv in a bid to protect the Ukrainian electrical grid.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/05/details-of-the-two-russian-military-airbases-hit-by-explosions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Details of the two Russian military airbases hit by explosions }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Spanish police have intercepted three more envelopes containing animal eyes addressed to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s embassy in Madrid and its consulates in Barcelona and M\u225\'00\'E1laga, police sources close to the investigation said.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Ukraine said a series of \u8220\'20\'1Cbloody packages\u8221\'20\'1D were sent to its missions across Europe, soon after a letter bomb detonated at Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s embassy in Spain and police defused others sent to, among others, prime minister Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez.\par \par \uc2 The postal service\u8217\'20\'19s security staff detected the new envelopes during screening on Monday morning and alerted police, the sources said. Officers found no explosive or flammable substances inside, the sources added.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian embassy in Madrid received a package with animal eyes on Friday that the interior ministry said carried a foreign stamp, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Evidence from that package shared with the postal service helped its staff detect the latest one, police sources added.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, a source familiar with the investigation told Reuters the six letter bombs appeared to have been posted from the northern city of Valladolid.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Ukrainian foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson \uc2 Oleg Nikolenko\uc2  confirmed the latest interceptions on Monday and said there were now 21 known cases in which such threats had been sent to diplomatic missions in 12 countries.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has said that the latest Russian strikes against Ukraine are a reminder of the Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s brutality.\par \par \uc2 John Kirby, the White House national security spokesperson, also told reporters that an oil price cap would not have any long-term impact on global oil prices, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia says three servicemen killed in explosions at Russian airbases\par \par \uc2 Russia said that three of its military personnel were killed in what it said were Ukrainian drone attacks on two Russian airbases.\par \par \uc2 Two aircraft were lightly damaged, the defence ministry said in a statement. Four other people had been wounded, it said.\par \par \uc2 The defence ministry highlighted that it had launched a strike on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s military and energy infrastructure on Monday, \u8220\'20\'1Cdespite the attempts of the Kyiv regime to disrupt the combat work of Russian long-range aviation with a terrorist act\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 enltrMeeting with human rights defenders in underground shelter in Kyiv as missiles strike & air raid sirens sound again. Unbelievable that this is happening almost daily in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2 . This must not become a new normal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/My22JGkOWO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/My22JGkOWO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Volker T\u252\'00\'FCrk (@volker_turk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/volker_turk/status/1599761657403613185?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Canadian-made parts have been found in the \u8220\'20\'1Ckamikaze \u8221\'20\'1D Iranian drones used by Russia to attack Ukraine, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 An investigative project from the NGO Statewatch found components from 30 European and American companies, concluding antenna parts from Tallysman Wireless, a Canadian manufacturer.\par \par \uc2 Iranian-made Shahed 136 drones have been used by Russia in attacks against Ukraine, targeting civilian infrastructure. According to \uc2 Statewatch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s project Trap Aggressor, the Russian military renamed the drone Geran-2 to mask its origins.\par \par \uc2 Tallysman\u8217\'20\'19s president told the Globe and Mail he was \u8220\'20\'1Cpainfully aware\u8221\'20\'1D that his company\u8217\'20\'19s product has been used to target civilians in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is sometimes assumed that we are somehow complicit in this usage. We absolutely are not,\u8221\'20\'1D Gyles Panther told the newspaper. \u8220\'20\'1CTallysman is 100% committed to supporting Ukraine in the face of Russian aggression.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Because of sanctions against Iran, Panther suspects he inadvertently sold parts to \u8220\'20\'1Cfake company fronts\u8221\'20\'1D and said his company was working with Canadian customs officials, but admitted it could be difficult to prevent largely innocuous parts such as wireless antennas, which aren\u8217\'20\'19t covered by exports controls, from ending up in the wrong hands.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Moldovan police on Monday found fragments of a missile that came down in a region of northern Moldova near the border with Ukraine, state information portal Prima Sursa quoted the police as saying.\par \par \uc2 Moldovan authorities did not immediately comment publicly on the incident, which was reported after Russia carried out a new wave of missile strikes on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Ukrainian foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson \uc2 Oleg Nikolenko\uc2 , responding to media reports about the incident, repeated calls for Kyiv to receive more missile defence systems from its allies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis once again proves that Russian missile terror poses a huge threat not only to the security of Ukraine, but also to the security of neighbouring countries,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Russia did not immediately comment on the reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine shoots down most missiles launched by Russia, air force says\par \par \uc2 Ukraine shot down more than 60 of over 70 missiles launched by Russia in a massed missile strike on Monday, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s air force command said.\par \par \uc2 The strikes targeted Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s critical infrastructure, the air force said in a statement on the Telegram messaging app.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Air defences shot down most of the Russian missiles fired at Ukraine on Monday and energy workers have already begun work on restoring power supplies, Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Russia carried out the latest in a wave of airstrikes on Ukraine, destroying homes in the south and knocking out power in the north and killing at least two people, Ukrainian officials said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The governor of the Kyiv region has said 40% of it is without electricity and some infrastructure was hit, but that there were no \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical consequences\u8221\'20\'1D, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has driven across the Kerch bridge, linking Russia and the Crimean pen insula, after it was damaged by a truck bomb in October.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president drove across the bridge today and spoke to workers and a senior government official, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The bomb attack, on 8 October, disrupted travel on one of the two lanes of the bridge. Russia blamed Ukraine and responded with a wave of strikes on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s energy facilities and other key infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  visits the bridge over the Kerch Strait which was damaged in October. Photograph: Mikhail Metzel/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 All clear sounded in Kyiv as Ukrainian capital appears to emerge unscathed by missile strikes\par \par \uc2 The all clear has been sounded in Kyiv. It is possible there will be further waves of strikes, but for now the capital appears to have emerged unscathed. The air defences could be heard in action. So far there have been no reports of any missile impacts in the city. Odesa seems to have been hit hardest meanwhile and there are reports of a missile landing over the border in Moldova, near Briceni.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Moldovan police say they have found missile fragments in the Briceni region near the border with Ukraine, Reuters reports, citing state information portal Prima Sursa.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s state-run Ukrenergo energy company said its infrastructure had been hit in Russian missile strikes on Monday, causing emergency power outages.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUkrenergo\u8217\'20\'19s dispatchers are working to maintain balance in the energy system,\u8221\'20\'1D it said in a statement. It did not say which facilities had been struck\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian officials reported a new barrage of Russian missile strikes across the country, an attack that was anticipated as Russia seeks to disable Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s energy supplies and infrastructure with the approach of winter.\par \par \uc2 Media reports referred to explosions in several parts of the country, including the cities of Odesa, Cherkasy and Kryvyi Rih. In Odesa, the local water supply company said a missile strike cut power to pumping stations, leaving the entire city without water.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe enemy is again attacking the territory of Ukraine with missiles!\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kyrylo Tymoshenko\uc2 , the deputy head of the Ukrainian president\u8217\'20\'19s office, wrote on Telegram.\par \par \uc2 Air raid alerts sounded across the country, and authorities urged people to take shelter, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the Ukrainian air force, Yuriy Ihnat, said Russia had launched land-based missiles from southern Russia and shipborne missiles from the Caspian and Black seas. Russian strategic bombers also launched missiles, he said.\par \par \uc2 Ihnat warned the Russians could attack in several waves to make it more difficult for the Ukrainian air defences to shoot down the missiles.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Power outages in Sumy after wave of Russian missile strikes\par \par \uc2 Power has been knocked out in Sumy after the latest Russian missile strikes, according to the northern region\u8217\'20\'19s energy provider.\par \par \uc2 However, the governor of the Kyiv region said its air defences were working there and told residents to remain in shelters. There were also reports of loss of power and water in Odesa after strikes there.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s world affairs editor Julian Borger reports that he has still not heard or seen reports of a strike landing in Kyiv city.\par \par \uc2 But there are fears this was the first of a double punch, with the first wave designed to soak up the air defences, giving the second wave a better chance of getting through to its targets, potentially the power grid, on a day that started with lows of -7C.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Two killed in Russian missile strikes in Ukraine - senior official\par \par \uc2 Russian missiles have crashed into buildings in the southern Ukrainian region of Zaporizhzhia, destroying several houses and killing at least two people, a senior Ukrainian official has said.\par \par \uc2 Kyrylo Tymoshenko\uc2 , deputy head of the presidential office, gave no further details of the attacks, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 A city official said buildings had been hit in the suburbs of the city of Zaporizhzhia and some Russian missiles had been shot down.\par \par \uc2 The governor of the Kyiv region said air defences were working in the region, and told residents to remain in shelters.\par \par \uc2 An energy provider said power had been knocked out on the northern region of Sumy in the latest missile strikes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 India gave a list of Indian products to Moscow for access to Russian markets, foreign minister \uc2 Subrahmanyam Jaishankar\uc2  said, as his country seeks to narrow a growing trade deficit with Russia at a time when Moscow faces acute shortages of some crucial materials following western sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported last week that Moscow had sent India a list of more than 500 products for potential delivery, including parts for cars, aircraft and trains, as sanctions following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine squeeze its ability to keep vital industries running.\par \par \uc2 Russia has been India\u8217\'20\'19s largest supplier of military equipment for decades and it is the fourth-biggest market for Indian pharmaceuticals. But with India\u8217\'20\'19s purchases of Russian oil soaring and coal and fertiliser shipments also strong, the South Asian nation is looking for ways to rebalance trade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have given Russians a set of products which we believe we are very competitive in and which we feel should be getting access to the Russian market,\u8221\'20\'1D Jaishankar told reporters in a briefing with his German counterpart \uc2 Annalena Baerbock\uc2 , who is on a visit to India.\par \par \uc2 The minister added that discussions on expanding trade have been going on for some time, and even before Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian air defences have managed to shoot down some of the incoming missiles ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638ddc198f082ef70a24550d#block-638ddc198f082ef70a24550d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see 11.58am}}}\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 The reported interceptions so far have been four in the Kharkiv region, one in Dnipro and one in Poltava, with other explosions reported elsewhere that could be air defence interceptions.\par \par \uc2 After the sirens went off in Kyiv, people began gathering in the underground stations, which are beginning to fill up.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has not heard or seen reports of the impact on the capital, but there are lots of reports of air defences in action, including in Odesa, suggesting that there are incoming Kalibr missiles fired from Russian warships in the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is a map showing where mysterious explosions took place at two Russian airbases far from the frontlines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2022/12/airbase_map-zip/giv-6562ZHL1nM8JHlwb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Air raid sirens sound in Kyiv as Russia launches new missile attack\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has said Russia ha s unleashed a new barrage of missiles, as air alerts blared in many parts of the country inc luding Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Sirens sounded in the capital and across much of Ukraine in what officials described as the latest in a wave of Russian missile strikes, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMissile have already been launched,\u8221\'20\'1D said Yuriy Ihnat, an air force spokesperson. There was no immediate word of any damage or casualties.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  understands there are more than 100 missiles incoming, fired from Russian bombers and most likely sea-launched Kalibr missiles as well.\par \par \uc2 Some have already crossed into Ukrainian territory, with impact time in Kyiv is estimated as 2.15pm local time. There could also be a second wave of missiles aimed at the capital, due to take off in the next few minutes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t ignore the alarm,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Andriy Yermak\uc2 , head of the Ukrainian presidential staff.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe anticipated large scale Russian missile strike is on the way. Reportedly 104 missiles fired from 13 aircraft, plus possible strikes from sea-launched Kalibr missiles. Expected to reach Kyiv 2.15pm local.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julian Borger (@julianborger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/julianborger/status/1599729970284216323?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Winter has arrived. Temperatures in the frontline Ukrainian city of Bakhmut, under remorseless attack from the Russians, plunged to -11C (12.2F) this weekend, and at no point got above freezing. Gradually the mud and rain of late autumn will give way to snow and cold of -20C or worse. Yet both sides have their reasons to carry on fighting.\par \par \uc2 The weather is a neutral party to the near-10-month war, but in winter it inevitably acts as a constraint. Simple operations take far longer to conduct in the cold, cover from foliage is reduced or eliminated, white camouflage is required when snow has arrived and more rations are needed because soldiers consume more calories.\par \par \uc2 Shelter and warmth is vital, above all because the armies have to ensure soldiers can dry once they get wet, or they will risk hypothermia or frostbite. A report from Channel 4 News on the Donbas frontline concludes in the kind of well-prepared, deep-dug warm bunker required for winter troops, complete with a kitten to hunt down the inevitable mice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTraining, morale and leadership become critical,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ben Barry, a former British army tank commander who served in Bosnia with the Nato postwar stabilisation force during the chilly winter of 1995-6. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is easy to become demoralised in the cold: imagine a badly run skiing holiday, without good organisation and equipment. In Bosnia, I saw shivering local soldiers who were disinclined to do anything other than go back to their bunkers and drink.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A key element of the winter struggle will be who has the best kit, and donations have been pouring in from western allies. Canada said in October it would send 500,000 items of winter clothing, Germany 100,000 warm jackets and Britain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/news/prime-minister-announces-crucial-winter-kit-delivery-for-ukrainian-forces-as-he-meets-nato-chief#:~:text=The%20UK%20is%20set%20to,the%20plunging%20temperatures%20in%20Ukraine."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 25,000 full sets}}}\uc2 , with Nordic countries also contributing. For the Ukrainians, the challenge will be ensuring the kit reaches the frontline.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/05/ukraine-war-winter-phase-russian-troops"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kit and morale may prove decisive as Ukraine war enters winter phase}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s recent mobilisation has increased its military threat in Ukraine, with better -trained soldiers now arriving at the frontline, the commander of Ukrainian ground forces said.\par \par \uc2 But he said Russia was now using a lot of old equipment because it had no other way of replenishing supplies, and that Russian forces had made only slow progress around Bakhmut, one of the main battle zones in eastern Ukraine, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn the eastern front, the situation is very tense, the enemy attacks our units every day,\u8221\'20\'1D Gen Oleksandr Syrskyi told national television.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the mobilisation ordered by Moscow in September, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CSuch a number of personnel increased the threat for us and these are not just words \u8211\'20\'13 these are new brigades, new battalions that have been trained, this is the replenishment that the army was waiting for because it was exhausted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose who come now have a better level of training than those who were previously sent to the front,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here's a summary of the latest developments...\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mysterious explosions took place at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638dc6188f08ec68b60189fc#block-638dc6188f08ec68b60189fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Russian airbases}}}\uc2  far from the frontlines on Monday, raising the possibility that Kyiv has found a way to target Russian long-range bombers used in attacks against Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638dc6408f082ef70a2453e0#block-638dc6408f082ef70a2453e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has warned}}}\uc2  the new western price cap on Russian oil will destabilise global energy markets, but claimed it would not impact its invasion of Ukraine. Spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  was preparing its response to the move by the \uc2 G7\uc2  and allies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  has warned the west to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638daeaf8f08ec68b6018935#block-638daeaf8f08ec68b6018935"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoid creating a new cold war}}}\uc2  by dividing the world into blocs. Writing in an opinion piece for Foreign Affairs magazine, published today, the German chancellor called for every effort to be made to build new partnerships. He singled out China and Russia as two countries that pose a threat to a multipolar world.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638daafc8f082ef70a245302#block-638daafc8f082ef70a245302"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nine people have been killed}}}\uc2  in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern Luhansk, Russian-backed military officials have said. It came after Ukraine shelled the city of Alchevsk, Reuters reports, citing state-run TASS news agency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chinese foreign ministry\uc2  has said it will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638da1618f08f5eb2e3179cc#block-638da1618f08f5eb2e3179cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue energy cooperation}}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  after the \uc2 G7\uc2 , \uc2 EU\uc2  and Australia imposed a price cap on Russian oil exports. China, which said it would continue on the basis if respect and mutual benefit, has increased its purchases of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Urals oil blends this year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Three people have reportedly been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638d9a5c8f08ec68b60188b8#block-638d9a5c8f08ec68b60188b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed and six injured }}}\uc2  after a fuel tanker exploded at a Russian airfield. The explosion was near the city of Ryazan, south-east of Moscow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In recent months, the number of sudden troop deployments conducted by Russian tactical combat aircraft over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638d94d78f08f5eb2e317974#block-638d94d78f08f5eb2e317974"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creduced significantly\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , according to the \uc2 UK Ministry of Defence\uc2 . Russian aircraft now probably conducts tens of missions per day, compared with a high of up to 300 a day in March 2022, the latest British intelligent report suggests.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me for now. Handing over to Tom Ambrose. Thanks for reading.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russian airbase explosions suggest Kyiv may have found way to target long-range bombers\par \par \uc2 Mysterious explosions took place at two Russian airbases far from the frontlines on Monday, raising the possibility that Kyiv has found a way to target Russian long-range bombers used in attacks against Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 Russian media reports and video posted to social media indicated that an explosion took place early on Monday morning at the Engels-2 airbase in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Saratov region that hosts Tu-95 bombers that have taken part in cruise missile strikes against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Another explosion took place at a military airbase near the city of Ryazan, less than 150 miles from Moscow. Three were killed and five wounded after a fuel truck exploded, Russian state media reported. That base also hosts Tu-95 and Tu-22M long-range bombers.\par \par \uc2 Video of the explosion showed a fiery blast illuminating the night sky. Locals reported that the sound of the explosion could be heard from miles away.\par \par \uc2 The cause of the two explosions has not been confirmed.\par \par \uc2 But Baza, a Russian media outlet with sources in the security services, reported that the Russian airfield at Engels was attacked by a loitering munition that targeted the airbase\u8217\'20\'19s runway. \uc2 Astra\uc2 , another independent Russian media outlet, claimed that two nuclear-capable Tu-95 bombers were damaged in the explosion. Neither indicated a source for their information.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin said that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  had been informed of the incidents. Local authorities in the Saratov region said that security services were investigating reports of the explosion at the Engels airbase.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian monitoring reports in the last week suggested that Russia was delivering cruise missiles to the Engels airbase and transferring aircraft to the Ryazan airbase in preparation for another attack against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine is not known to have any loitering munitions that would allow it to attack hundreds of miles beyond the frontlines of the conflict, although there have been reports of such UAVs under development.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2022/12/dyagilevo-zip/giv-6562ANxe6S4r4dkf/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2022/12/engels_google-zip/giv-6562vms6ljzpXg3c/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kremlin claims western oil price cap will destabilise global markets\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin has warned the new western price cap on Russian oil will destabilise global energy markets but claimed it would not impact its invasion of Ukraine ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638da1618f08f5eb2e3179cc#block-638da1618f08f5eb2e3179cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see also 7.51am}}}\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 Spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said Russia was preparing how it would respond to the move by the \uc2 G7\uc2  and allies to ban countries and companies from dealing with Russian sea-borne exports of oil where the price is above $60 a barrel, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia and the Russian economy have the required capacity to fully meet the needs and requirements of the special military operation,\u8221\'20\'1D Peskov said today when asked whether the price cap would affect Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military campaign in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 He added that the price cap would \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely destabilise\u8221\'20\'1D the global energy markets, and told Europeans that should brace themselves for higher prices.\par \par \uc2 Global benchmark Brent crude was up 1.7% at $87.01 a barrel on Monday, following the \uc2 European Union\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move to adopt the price cap on Russian oil.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Finnish government has asked its parliament to formally adopt \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s founding treaty in preparation for joining the alliance.\par \par \uc2 Hungary and Turkey have yet to approve the membership of Finland and Sweden, which also applied in May in response to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur Nato membership moving forward is important for us Finns but also for \uc2 Nato\uc2  members,\u8221\'20\'1D Finland\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, \uc2 Pekka Haavisto\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 Finland\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, \uc2 Pekka Haavisto\uc2 , with his Swedish counterpart, Tobias Billstr\u246\'00\'F6m, at a Nato meeting on 29 November in Bucharest. Photograph: Andrei Pungovschi/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Volker Turk, the \uc2 UN\uc2  human rights chief, has visited Ukraine to hear accounts of deportation of children, tortured civilians and executed prisoners of war.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian government has praised the move:\par \par \uc2 enltrI congratulate the decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/volker_turk?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @volker_turk}}}\uc2  to visit ???? after his appointment immediately to hear first-hand about deported ???? children, tortured civilians, and executed prisoners of war. It is necessary to make a joint effort to achieve a fair trial for criminals. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/UN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #UN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/HumanRights?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HumanRights}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BQWPlZ79ox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BQWPlZ79ox}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oleksandr Korniyenko (@OlekKorn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OlekKorn/status/1599698552413831168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kyiv is to provide backup drinking water in case of shortages, the city\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, \uc2 Vitali Klitschko\uc2 , has announced.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn case of shortages in water supply in the capital, a system of backup sources of drinking water will be provided, first of all, pump-room complexes, most of which have the ability to connect to generators, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Kyiv?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Kyiv}}}\uc2  mayor \uc2 Vitali Klitschko\uc2  has announced. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IQlPlpkk46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IQlPlpkk46}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 KyivPost (@KyivPost) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyivPost/status/1599693299924619264?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  warns west to avoid new cold war\par \par \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  has warned the west to avoid creating a new cold war by dividing the world into blocs.\par \par \uc2 Writing in an opinion piece for Foreign Affairs magazine, published today, the German chancellor called for every effort to be made to build new partnerships.\par \par \uc2 Singling out China and Russia as two countries that pose a threat to a multipolar world, he said there must be stronger European and transatlantic unity.\par \par \uc2 While he said the west must stand up for democratic values and protect open societies, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe must also avoid the temptation to once again divide the world into blocs,\u8221\'20\'1D reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis means making every effort to build new partnerships, pragmatically and without ideological blinders,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGermans are intent on becoming the guarantor of European security that our allies expect us to be, a bridge builder within the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and an advocate for multilateral solutions to global problems,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nine killed in eastern Luhansk region \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 Nine people have been killed in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern Luhansk, Russian-backed military officials have said.\par \par \uc2 It came after Ukraine shelled the city of Alchevsk, Reuters reports, citing state-run TASS news agency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Staff at a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital in Kherson have described how they secretly planned how to save babies from Russia capture after the city was invaded in February.\par \par \uc2 Russian forces were suspected of taking orphan children and sending them to Russia, prompting the children\u8217\'20\'19s regional hospital in Kherson to start fabricating medical records so that it looked like they were too ill to move.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe deliberately wrote false information that the children were sick and could not be transported,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Olga Pilyarska, head of intensive care, told the Associated Press. \u8220\'20\'1CWe were scared that [the Russians]would find out [but] we decided that we would save the children at any cost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hospital staff take care of orphaned children at the children's regional hospital maternity ward in Kherson on 22 November. Photograph: Bernat Armangu\u233\'00\'E9/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 China says it will continue energy cooperation with Russia after \uc2 G7\uc2  price cap on oil exports\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chinese foreign ministry\uc2  has said it will continue energy cooperation with Russia after the \uc2 G7\uc2 , \uc2 EU\uc2  and Australia imposed a price cap on Russian oil exports.\par \par \uc2 China, which said it would continue on the basis if respect and mutual benefit, has increased its purchases of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Urals oil blends this year, reports Reuters, citing Russia\u8217\'20\'19s RIA news agency.\par \par \uc2 It comes after the UK, Japan, Germany, Italy, France, Canada, the US, \uc2 EU\uc2  member states and Australia came to an agreement to put a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/02/eu-states-agree-60-a-barrel-cap-on-russian-oil-after-polish-green-light"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $60 a barrel price cap }}}\uc2  on the world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest oil exporter ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638d710d8f08f5eb2e31789b#block-638d710d8f08f5eb2e31789b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see 6.01am}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  has said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cmore responsible than I am brave\u8221\'20\'1D and hates to let people down.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the FT, who named him \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/9599247f-c3cb-4d3c-a0b6-771f0aac8699"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 person of the year}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and compared him with Churchill for the social media age, the Ukrainian president said that after nine months fighting Russia, he misses fishing with his son.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 I am more responsible than I am brave \u8230\'20\'26 I just hate to let people down.\par \par \uc2 He also told the newspaper:\par \par \uc2 I just want to catch a carp in the Dnipro River.\par \par \uc2 enltrVolodymyr Zelenskyy is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FT?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FT}}}\uc2  's person of the year for his "extraordinary display of leadership and fortitude" - a Churchill for the social media age. With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/khalafroula?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @khalafroula}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChristopherJM?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ChristopherJM}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yTjFaCDnAU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yTjFaCDnAU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Hall (@hallbenjamin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hallbenjamin/status/1599665887409152000?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Three killed and six injured after explosion in Russian airfield\par \par \uc2 Three people have reportedly been killed and six injured after a fuel tanker exploded at a Russian airfield.\par \par \uc2 The explosion was near the city of Ryazan, south-east of Moscow, reports Reuters, citing news agency RIA Novosti.\par \par \uc2 Hi, I\u8217\'20\'19m looking after the Ukraine blog for the next few hours. Please get in touch with any tips or suggestions: miranda.bryant@guardian.co.uk\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Number of Russian sorties 'reduced significantly' in recent months: UK MoD\par \par \uc2 In recent months, the number of sudden troop deployments conducted by Russian tactical combat aircraft over Ukraine has \u8220\'20\'1Creduced significantly\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the \uc2 UK Ministry of Defence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Russian aircraft now probably conducts tens of missions per day, compared with a high of up to 300 a day in March 2022, the latest British intelligent report suggests.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has now lost over 60 fixed-wing aircraft in the conflict, likely including an additional Su-24M FENCER fighter-bomber and a Su-25 FROGFOOT ground attack aircraft last week,\u8221\'20\'1D the ministry adds.\par \par \uc2 The decrease in sorties is likely a result of continued high threat from Ukrainian air defences, limitations on the flying hours available to Russian aircraft, and worsening weather.\par \par \uc2 With Russia\u8217\'20\'19s ground attack tactics largely reliant on visual identification and unguided munitions, the Russian air force will likely continue a low rate of ground attack operations through the poor winter weather.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrLatest Defence Intelligence update on the situation in Ukraine - 05 December 2022\par \par \uc2 Find out more about the \uc2 UK government\uc2 's response: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pmOwk4EqC5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/pmOwk4EqC5}}}\par \par \uc2 ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandWithUkraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandWithUkraine}}}\uc2  ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KEWi93TjT1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KEWi93TjT1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ministry of Defence ???? (@DefenceHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DefenceHQ/status/1599656286873915393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 5, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russian forces shelled the Kherson region 46 times on Sunday, killing one civilian, according to senior Ukrainian presidential aides.\par \par \uc2 Kyrylo Tymoshenko\uc2 , the deputy head of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s presidential office, made the claim in a Telegram {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/tymoshenko_kyrylo/2957"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 update}}}\uc2  late on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CDuring the day, the occupiers shelled the region 46 times with mortars, tanks, artillery and MLRS. Private and apartment buildings and other buildings were destroyed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said citing the Kherson city council.\par \par \uc2 Anton Gerashchenko\uc2 , a senior adviser to \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s interior ministry\uc2 , said a 65-year-old woman was killed in the attack. He made the claim in a Telegram {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/Pravda_Gerashchenko/54382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  early this morning:\par \par \uc2 As a woman and her husband were crossing the Dnieper in a boat in the Golopristansky district, the rashists [Russians] opened fire from machine guns. The pensioner died from her wounds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 US thinktank the Institute for the Study of War (ISW) has responded to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/dec/05/russia-ukraine-war-live-news-russian-oil-cap-comes-into-force-kyiv-resumes-rolling-power-outages?page=with:block-638d76228f082ef70a2451bc#block-638d76228f082ef70a2451bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier claims }}}\uc2  made by senior \uc2 US government\uc2  officials, saying they were mistaken in identifying the optimal window of opportunity for Ukraine to conduct more counteroffensives as the spring rather than winter.\par \par \uc2 Its latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.understandingwar.org/backgrounder/russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-december-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  reads:\par \par \uc2 US Director for National Intelligence (DNI) Avril Haines assessed on December 3 that the pace of the war in Ukraine will slow over the winter so both sides can refit, resupply, and reconstitute, despite evidence that conditions on the ground favour a renewed offensive and despite the demonstrated tendency of Ukrainian forces to initiate new counteroffensive efforts relatively quickly after the previous effort has culminated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 A 'reduced tempo' in fighting to continue over winter, US predicts\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2022/dec/04/us-expects-reduced-tempo-in-ukraine-conflict-to-continue-says-top-intelligence-official-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creduced tempo\u8221\'20\'1D in fighting}}}\uc2  is expected continue over the winter months as brighter prospects for Ukrainian forces emerge in the coming months, the US has said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking during a defence forum at the weekend, \uc2 Avril Haines\uc2 , the US director of national intelligence, said:\par \par \uc2 Most of the fighting right now around Bakhmut and the Donetsk area has slowed down with the withdrawal of Russia from the western Kherson area to the east of the river. And we expect that\u8217\'20\'19s likely to be what we see in the coming months.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/04/vladimir-putin-better-informed-now-about-ukraine-war-says-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter informed\u8221\'20\'1D about the difficulties facing his forces }}}\uc2  in Ukraine, Haines added, indicating the Russian president was no longer as insulated from bad news arising from his invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Alluding to past assessments that Putin\u8217\'20\'19s advisers could be shielding him, Haines said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cbecoming more informed of the challenges that the military faces\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/04/vladimir-putin-better-informed-now-about-ukraine-war-says-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin better informed now about Ukraine war, says US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kyiv resumes power shutdowns\par \par \uc2 Cities across Ukraine will resume scheduled power outages today.\par \par \uc2 Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s mayor \uc2 Vitali Klitschko\uc2  promised there would be \u8220\'20\'1Cas few deviations as possible\u8221\'20\'1D in a Telegram {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/vitaliy_klitschko/1659"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  late on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Starting tomorrow, Monday, Kyiv will return to stabilisation shutdowns according to the schedule,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 But the situation in the energy system remains difficult. Therefore, as noted by energy experts, there may be some deviations from the schedule for balancing the energy system.\par \par \uc2 There is a further need to save electricity. And it must be done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Price cap on Russian oil comes into force\par \par \uc2 A price cap on Russian seaborne oil agreed upon by \uc2 G7\uc2  nations comes into force today as the west aims to reduce the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s income from fossil fuels as well as curtailing Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s ability to finance its war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The UK, Japan, Germany, Italy, France, Canada and the US, as well as EU member states and Australia came to an agreement to put a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/02/eu-states-agree-60-a-barrel-cap-on-russian-oil-after-polish-green-light"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $60 a barrel price cap on Russian oil}}}\uc2  after Poland, which was holding out, gave the green light to the deal. Russia is the world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest oil exporter.\par \par \uc2 The agreement allows Russian oil to be shipped to third-party countries using \uc2 G7\uc2  and EU tankers, insurance companies and credit institutions, only if the cargo is bought at or below the $60 per barrel cap.\par \par \uc2 The price cap would \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately cut into Putin\u8217\'20\'19s most important source of revenue\u8221\'20\'1D US treasury secretary, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 But critics, including Ukraine, say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/01/hawkish-estonia-under-pressure-to-accept-higher-cap-on-russian-oil-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the cap is toothless}}}\uc2  since it is above the price of existing Russian oil prices of about $52 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 An oil tanker moored at the Sheskharis complex, part of Chernomortransneft JSC, a subsidiary of \uc2 Transneft PJSC\uc2 , in Novorossiysk, Russia. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t call it a serious decision to set such a limit for Russian prices, which is quite comfortable for the budget of a terrorist state,\u8221\'20\'1D Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s only a matter of time before stronger tools will have to be used anyway. It is a pity that this time will be lost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Russian authorities rejected the price cap and on Saturday threatened to stop supplying the nations that endorsed it.\par \par \uc2 Russian deputy prime minister \uc2 Alexander Novak\uc2  said on Sunday it was a gross interference that contradicted the rules of free trade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are working on mechanisms to prohibit the use of a price cap instrument, regardless of what level is set, because such interference could further destabilise the market,\u8221\'20\'1D said Novak, the Russian government official in charge of its oil, gas, atomic energy and coal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will sell oil and petroleum products only to those countries that will work with us under market conditions, even if we have to reduce production a little,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary and welcome\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome back to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of the war in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 . I\u8217\'20\'19m Samantha Lock and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you all the latest developments as they unfold over the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 A price cap on Russian seaborne oil agreed upon by \uc2 G7\uc2  nations comes into force today as the west aims to reduce the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s income from fossil fuels as well as curtailing Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s ability to finance its war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 For any updates or feedback you wish to share, please feel free to get in touch via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:samantha.lock@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 email}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Samantha__Lock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If you have just joined us, here are all the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/04/vladimir-putin-better-informed-now-about-ukraine-war-says-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter informed\u8221\'20\'1D about the difficulties facing his forces }}}\uc2  in Ukraine, the head of US intelligence has said. Speaking during a defence forum at the weekend, \uc2 Avril Haines\uc2 , the US director of national intelligence, indicated the Russian president was no longer as insulated from bad news arising from his invasion of Ukraine. Alluding to past assessments that Putin\u8217\'20\'19s advisers could be shielding him, Haines said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cbecoming more informed of the challenges that the military faces\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US expects a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2022/dec/04/us-expects-reduced-tempo-in-ukraine-conflict-to-continue-says-top-intelligence-official-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creduced tempo\u8221\'20\'1D in fighting}}}\uc2  to continue over the winter months, adding that there could be brighter prospects for Ukrainian forces in the coming months. \u8220\'20\'1CMost of the fighting right now around Bakhmut and the Donetsk area has slowed down with the withdrawal of Russia from the western Kherson area to the east of the river. And we expect that\u8217\'20\'19s likely to be what we see in the coming months,\u8221\'20\'1D Haines said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Heavy fighting continues around the key Donbas town of Bakhmut, where Russian forces have been struggling for six months to make minimal progress. Reports on social media suggested Ukrainian forces were making progress in operations on the east bank of the Dnipro River, opposite the recently liberated city of Kherson, after a reported amphibious landing on the Kinburn Spit last month. Russian forces have also intensified artillery attacks on the Kherson region since withdrawing from the western bank of the Dnipro.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A draft resolution is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/dec/04/russian-war-crimes-draft-resolution-circulated-un-ukraine-zelenskiy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 circulating at the United Nations}}}\uc2  for a Nuremberg-style tribunal to hold Russia accountable for crimes of aggression in Ukraine. Signs also indicate that US opposition to the proposal may be softening in the face of lobbying by the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 . Beth Van Schaack, the US ambassador for global criminal justice, said this week: \u8220\'20\'1CSo far, all of the [\uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly] resolutions on Ukraine have prevailed. The numbers have been quite strong.\u8221\'20\'1D The international criminal court has already started investigating war crimes in Ukraine but cannot prosecute the Kremlin leadership over the broader crime of aggression since Russia is not a signatory to the relevant statute.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s leadership has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/04/iran-locked-into-vicious-cycle-over-protests-and-arming-russia-says-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 locked itself into a \u8220\'20\'1Cvicious cycle\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  over protests and arming Russia, the US special envoy has said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe more Iran represses, the more there will be sanctions; the more there are sanctions, the more Iran feels isolated,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Rob Malley\uc2 , the US special envoy on Iran, told a conference in Rome. \u8220\'20\'1CThe more isolated they feel, the more they turn to Russia; the more they turn to Russia, the more sanctions there will be, the more the climate deteriorates, the less likely there will be nuclear diplomacy. So it is true right now the vicious cycles are all self-reinforcing.\u8221\'20\'1D US intelligence chief \uc2 Avril Haines\uc2  said there was worrying evidence that Russia was seeking to deepen military cooperation with Iran.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia will not sell oil that is subject to a western price-cap even if it has to cut production, Russian deputy prime minister \uc2 Alexander Novak\uc2  said on Sunday. The \uc2 G7\uc2  and Australia agreed to the price cap on Friday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Opec+ agreed to stick to its oil output targets at a meeting on Sunday. Opec+, which comprises the Organisation of the Petroleum Exporting Countries (Opec) and allies including Russia, angered the US and other western nations in October when it agreed to cut output by 2m barrels a day, about 2% of world demand, from November until the end of 2023.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 500 Ukrainian localities remained without power on Sunday following weeks of Russian airstrikes on the electric grid, an interior ministry official said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine is imposing sanctions on 10 senior clerics linked to a pro-Moscow church on the grounds they agreed to work with Russian occupation authorities or justified Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s invasion, the security service said.\par \par \uc2 An elderly woman carrying a trolley bag crosses the river on a destroyed bridge in Bakhmut, Donetsk region, on 4 December. Photograph: Yevhen Titov/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221205eic5000ru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
