\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s workers upset about new work schedule policy: \u8216\'20\'18a veiled threat\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 751 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 December 2022\par 13:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The grocery is pressuring part-time employees to add work hours, a constraint on some with parenting or school commitments\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s, a specialty grocery chain with about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/28/business/economy/trader-joes-brooklyn-union.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  500 locations}}}\uc2  in the US and 50,000 employees, is rolling out new, unofficial policies at stores across the US starting in January 2023, according to workers, that will mandate part-time workers work a minimum of three days a week to maintain their employment with the company.\par \par \uc2 A Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s worker in the north-east US who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation criticized the changes. The employee learned of the policy in August because they had planned to reduce their work days to one or two days a week to have time to start their own business and had already seen a co-worker affected by it for trying to return from a maternity leave to a reduced schedule.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn October, our captain started having conversations with anyone who was working less than three days a week, to see how we would feel about increasing our hours and days to stay employed,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said. \u8220\'20\'1CMost people I talked to were upset about it. They have kids and no one to look after them, have other jobs, are older and happy just working a few hours a week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They claimed management said the changes were being made because of hiring issues, wanting workers to be more engaged and knowledgable on the job, and complaints that part-time and full-time workers received the same wage raises.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an ultimatum. It\u8217\'20\'19s a vaguely veiled threat that they are now trying to spin another way. What are people supposed to say, \u8216\'20\'18no I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to work here more hours so fire me?\u8217\'20\'19 People with kids, multiple jobs, who are in school, who have debt and are just trying to get by in our current economic crisis?\u8221\'20\'1D the worker argued. \u8220\'20\'1CMost people can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to just give up a job when they are faced with a threat like that. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care how nicely a boss asks you, when a \u8216\'20\'18choice\u8217\'20\'19 comes from higher up, it is mired in some fear. Most people who are increasing their hours are doing so out of fear of losing their job, not because they truly want to be there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They added: \u8220\'20\'1CTiming wise, all of this seems to be piggybacking on recent calls to unionize in some north-eastern stores and the closing of the New York alcohol store.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s has been opposing unionization efforts of workers through Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s United.\par \par \uc2 The first store {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/trader-joes-union-employees-massachusetts#:~:text=The%20store%20in%20Hadley%2C%20about,locations%20have%20initiated%20unionization%20efforts.&text=The%20union%20vote%20passed%2045%2D31."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won }}}\uc2  its union election in July in Hadley, Massachusetts, with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://minnesotareformer.com/2022/08/12/minneapolis-trader-joes-becomes-countrys-2nd-unionized-store/#:~:text=Workers%20at%20the%20Trader%20Joe%27s,crew%20member%20at%20the%20store."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second store winning a union election}}}\uc2  in Minneapolis, Minnesota, in August. Workers at a third store in Brooklyn, New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/28/business/economy/trader-joes-brooklyn-union.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost }}}\uc2  their union election in October and the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ny.eater.com/2022/8/19/23312851/trader-joes-closed-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shut down}}}\uc2  a wine store in Manhattan shortly after a union campaign was launched there. The \uc2 United Food and Commercial Workers (UFCW) \uc2 also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/04/trader-joes-union-workers-labor-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled }}}\uc2  a union election petition from a store in Boulder, Colorado, after company-wide wage and benefit increases undermined support for the union right before an election was to be held.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s United said the part-timer policy was rolling out unofficially, with the two unionized stores not experiencing the policy change because the company cannot implement it without bargaining with the union. The group has expressed concern over the new policy mandating three days a week from crew members across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a concerning change because this policy will unfairly discriminate against parents, students, older crew for whom Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s is a \u8216\'20\'18retirement job\u8217\'20\'19, crew with disabilities, veteran crew who have cut back their hours due to work injuries, and other crew members that need to work one or two days a week. Flexibility is one of the draws of the job, and a lot of folks have come to depend on this part-time option,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maeg Yosef, a longtime Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s worker and union organizer in Hadley, Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 She estimated about 15% of crew members at the unionized stores work one or two days a week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a crew member, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard for me to see why the company would risk pushing out experienced, fully trained employees,\u8221\'20\'1D Yosef added.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221201eic1001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
