\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: US House moves to block rail strike, mandate paid sick leave\b0\par\par\uc2 Mattha Busby \par \uc2 1,794 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 December 2022\par 11:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawmakers vote to impose contract deal on dozen unions despite majority of workers rejecting deal. Plus, China altering Covid lineDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 A looming US rail strike in protest against an absence of paid sick leave \u8211\'20\'13 a norm in every other leading democratic country \u8211\'20\'13 as well as concerns about pay, staff shortages and time off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/30/us-rail-strike-congress-house-senate-union-sick-leave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looks likely to be blocked legally by Congress}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives voted yesterday to approve a bill to block the potentially crippling US rail strike despite a majority of workers rejecting a tentative contract deal in part brokered by the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 In the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , Bernie Sanders, the Vermont independent who caucuses with Democrats, announced he would object to fast-tracking \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposal that Congress impose an industrial settlement, until he can get a roll-call vote on the amendment that would guarantee seven paid sick days for rail workers.\par \par \uc2 The US president, who built a reputation on being pro-labor, has put himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/30/us-rail-strike-unions-decry-biden-proposal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at loggerheads}}}\uc2  with the unions after asking Congress to avert a strike.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The economic consequences of a strike. A rail stoppage that could begin as early as 9 December and could cost the US economy about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aar.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/AAR-Rail-Shutdown-Report-September-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $2bn a day}}}\uc2  by some estimates, with chaos hitting freight and passenger traffic.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No brakes on the gravy train. As railroad carriers implemented cuts and more grueling scheduling systems, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/30/us-rail-strike-unions-decry-biden-proposal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they have reported}}}\uc2  record profits and paid out $196bn in stock buybacks and dividends to shareholders since 2010.\par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s vice-premier signals shift in Covid stance as some lockdowns eased\par \par \uc2 One of China\u8217\'20\'19s most senior pandemic response officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/01/chinas-vice-premier-signals-shift-in-covid-stance-as-some-lockdowns-eased"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said the country is entering}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew stage and mission\u8221\'20\'1D in the latest indication of the government\u8217\'20\'19s changing approach after mass protests against its zero-Covid policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the decreasing pathogenicity of the Omicron variant, the increasing vaccination rate and the accumulating experience of outbreak control and prevention, China\u8217\'20\'19s pandemic containment faces a new stage and mission,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Sun Chunlan\uc2 , China\u8217\'20\'19s vice-premier, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 It came as several regions including Shanghai began to lift lockdowns despite continuing high case numbers.\par \par \uc2 At a meeting, Sun said China was also taking a more \u8220\'20\'1Chumane approach\u8221\'20\'1D with its outbreak responses. She did not refer to the \u8220\'20\'1Cdynamic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/29/china-zero-covid-policy-explained-30-seconds-lockdowns-outbreaks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 zero-Covid}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D policy by name, instead emphasising vaccination and other measures.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Omicron narrative flip. In recent days Chinese officials have begun to emphasise the lower severity of the Omicron strain of Covid-19. Meanwhile, authorities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/30/us-and-canada-urge-china-not-to-harm-zero-covid-protesters-amid-calls-for-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly lifted Covid restrictions}}}\uc2  in the cities of Guangzhou and Chongqing, where protesters scuffled with police on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People want to live\u8217\'20\'19. Four people in various Chinese cities spoke to the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/30/people-want-to-live-views-from-china-on-the-covid-lockdown-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on condition of anonymity}}}\uc2  to share their views on the protests.\par \par \uc2 Biden urged to threaten Israel weapons halt over far\par \par \uc2 right\par \par \uc2 Two former senior US diplomats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/30/biden-israel-weapons-palestinian-territories-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  have made a highly unusual call}}}\uc2  for the Biden administration to cut weapons supplies to Israel if the incoming far-right government uses them to annex Palestinian land, expel Arabs or finally kill off the diminishing possibility of a Palestinian state.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Kurtzer, a former US ambassador to Israel under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , and Aaron David Miller, a US Middle East peace negotiator during several administrations, have called for what they described as an \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented and controversial\u8221\'20\'1D break from the US\u8217\'20\'19s largely unconditional military and diplomatic support for Israel if \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most extreme government in the history of the state\u8221\'20\'1D pursues the stated aims of some of its members.\par \par \uc2 The pair warned against increased use of force against Arabs in the occupied territories and Israel by incoming ministers who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/02/king-bibi-is-back-again-but-what-next-for-netanyahus-latest-attempt-at-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 espoused openly racist views, }}}\uc2  escalating settlement construction, and moves \u8220\'20\'1Cto build infrastructure for settlers that is designed to foreclose the possibility of a two-state solution\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sign of increased sympathy towards Palestinian plight. \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael should be told that \u8230\'20\'26 [the US] will not provide offensive weapons or other assistance for malign Israeli actions in Jerusalem or the occupied territories,\u8221\'20\'1D the pair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/11/29/israel-government-netanyahu-biden-palestinians-arabs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in the Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roar footage:\par \par \uc2 Taronga\par \par \uc2 zoo releases video of lions escaping from their Sydney enclosure. The zoo says the investigation into the incident continues with a specialist forensic engineer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/dec/01/roar-footage-taronga-zoo-releases-video-of-lions-escaping-from-their-sydney-enclosure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 examining the failure of mesh fencing system}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US justice department has taken drastic action regarding the crisis in Jackson, Mississippi, that has affected drinking water for its 150,000 residents for several months. It has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/30/jackson-water-crisis-us-justice-department-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 imposed federal oversight of the failing water system}}}\uc2  to ensure improvements.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A lawyer for Hatice Cengiz, the fiancee of Jamal Khashoggi, has accused Mohammed bin Salman of engaging in an unprecedented and blatant attempt to \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulate\u8221\'20\'1D the US court system\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/30/mohammed-bin-salman-khashoggi-manipulate-us-court-system"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in order to}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Csecure impunity\u8221\'20\'1D after allegedly ordering the 2018 murder of the journalist.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest volcano oozed rivers of glowing lava yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/30/mauna-loa-hawaii-eruption-selfies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing thousands of awestruck viewers}}}\uc2  who jammed a Hawaii highway that could soon be covered by the flow after Mauna Loa awoke from its 38-year slumber.\par \par \uc2 World Cup: Poland squeeze out Mexico as\par \par \uc2 Australia progress\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s World Cup ended in agonizing fashion yesterday after they beat Saudi Arabia in their final group match but missed out on a place in the knockout stages on goal difference. It was Poland who took their place, squeaking through despite losing 2-0 to Argentina, who could easily have won by four or five goals. In the next round Argentina will face Australia, who only made it to Qatar after beating Peru on penalties in a playoff. France won Australia\u8217\'20\'19s group despite their loss to Tunisia.\par \par \uc2 Today, Belgium, one of the pre-tournament favorites, must beat 2018 finalists Croatia (10am ET) to guarantee progress after an unexpectedly shaky campaign. Canada play Morocco at the same time but are already out. In the 2pm ET kickoffs, Spain need only a draw against Japan to qualify for the next round, while the winner of Costa Rica v Germany will stand a good chance of progressing.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere at the World Cup:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Antonee Robinson won plenty of praise after the geopolitical minefield that was USA v Iran on Tuesday night. As his teammates celebrated, the US defender comforted some of the Iran players, winning plaudits on social media.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Iran, celebrations broke out among those who believed the country\u8217\'20\'19s government would have used victory over the US as a propaganda tool. One man, 27-year-old Mehran Samak, was shot dead after honking his car horn in Bandar Anzali, a city on the Caspian Sea coast, according to human rights activists.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US women\u8217\'20\'19s team must have been very happy at their male counterparts\u8217\'20\'19 progress. Under an agreement struck in May and signed in September, the men\u8217\'20\'19s and women\u8217\'20\'19s team share prize money from World Cups equally. The US are guaranteed $13m for reaching the last-16 in Qatar. For context, the US women earned $4m for winning the World Cup in 2019.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Kanye West is paying $200,000 a month in child support. Where did that number come from?\par \par \uc2 The goal is to ensure that children affected by divorce are able to carry on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/nov/30/kim-kardashian-kanye-west-divorce-child-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with the life that they are used to}}}\uc2 , said Jacqueline Newman, a managing partner of the New York divorce law firm Berkman Bottger Newman & Schein. \u8220\'20\'1CConceptually speaking, in settlements, you don\u8217\'20\'19t want one rich parent and one poor parent,\u8221\'20\'1D she explained. \u8220\'20\'1CA settlement should equalize things.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Given the family\u8217\'20\'19s wealth, that\u8217\'20\'19s hardly a concern, writes Alaina Demopolous. \u8220\'20\'1CHigh-income cases end up being a lifestyle analysis,\u8221\'20\'1D Newman said. Parents submit documentation of their kids\u8217\'20\'19 costly experiences \u8211\'20\'13 private planes, bodyguards \u8211\'20\'13 and those sums end up informing the final child support amount.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this:\par \par \uc2 in Buckingham Palace and outside it, we know what it means when people ask \u8216\'20\'18where are you from\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 When the journalist Kohinoor Sahota read that Ngozi Fulani, the head of a domestic abuse charity, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/nov/30/buckingham-palace-where-are-you-from-black-british"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was questioned where she was from}}}\uc2  while in Buckingham Palace, she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t surprised. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat did surprise me, however, is how it has become headline news and a sackable offence, as the honorary member of the royal household who asked the question has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/nov/30/buckingham-palace-aide-resigns-black-guest-traumatised-by-repeated-questioning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apologised and resigned}}}\uc2 . Dear, oh dear,\u8221\'20\'1D she writes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFulani\u8217\'20\'19s story is every person of color\u8217\'20\'19s story. I wish I could say it\u8217\'20\'19s unique. I wish I could say that nobody else has been asked such a thing. But that isn\u8217\'20\'19t the case; if it seems unique it is simply because not all of the people of colour get the chance to tell their story. I have had my own day out at Buckingham Palace, and found it similarly unwelcoming.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 from the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to Australia, why is your money funding Earth\u8217\'20\'19s destruction?\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s most destructive industries are fiercely protected by governments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/nov/30/amazon-public-money-earth-destruction-fossil-fuels-subsidies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes George Monbiot}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe three sectors that appear to be most responsible for the collapse of ecosystems and erasure of wildlife are fossil fuels, fisheries and farming. In 2021, governments directly subsidised oil and gas production to the tune of $64bn (\u163\'00\'A353bn), and spent a further $531bn on keeping fossil fuel prices low.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe latest figures for fisheries, from 2018, suggest that global subsidies for the sector amount to $35bn a year, over 80% of which go to large-scale industrial fishing. Most are paid to \u8216\'20\'18enhance capacity\u8217\'20\'19: in other words to help the industry, as marine ecosystems collapse, catch more fish.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last\par \par \uc2 thing: Cocaine Bear: the trailer for 2023\u8217\'20\'19s wildest film is everything and more\par \par \uc2 People know what they want the film to be, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/nov/30/cocaine-bear-trailer-2023-wildest-film-everything-and-more"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Stuart Heritage}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe trailer has hinted that it will also be this film. So now Cocaine Bear has to walk it like it talks it. To fulfill the promise of the trailer, it needs to only be a film about a bear on cocaine. There must be no heavy-handed moralizing about the drug trade. There must be minimal realistic depictions of a bear dying from a debilitating drug overdose.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere should be no subplots whatsoever. I am going to watch Cocaine Bear. I am going to pay for my own ticket. But I swear to god, if I so much as sense any dialogue whatsoever that does not directly discuss what a bear is like when it is on cocaine, I am demanding a refund.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221201eic1001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
