\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  blew it\u8217\'20\'19: rail unions decry plan to impose deal through Congress\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,086 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 November 2022\par 17:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers could be prevented by congressional decree from striking over paid sick leave and quality-of-life issues\par \par \uc2 Railroad workers have expressed dismay at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposed solution to a looming strike that threatens to derail the US economy, which they say belies his image as the most pro-union president in generations.\par \par \uc2 As a 9 December deadline looms for the long-running labor dispute between the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest railway companies and their unions, Biden has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/nov/28/biden-us-congress-railroad-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on Congress}}}\uc2  to intervene and block a strike that could cost the US economy about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aar.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/AAR-Rail-Shutdown-Report-September-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $2bn a day}}}\uc2  by some estimates.\par \par \uc2 The impending strike comes as the US struggles with a cost-of-living crisis driven by a 40-year high in inflation, and Biden has said that a railroad labor action could \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastate our economy\u8221\'20\'1D. On Wednesday Congress is expected to pass legislation that will force a settlement.\par \par \uc2 But union leaders are unhappy that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s solution appears to be the imposition of a settlement reached in September that has already been rejected by many for failing to address members\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about pay, sick days, staff shortages and time off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  blew it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hugh Sawyer, treasurer of Railroad Workers United, a group representing workers from a variety of rail unions and carriers. \u8220\'20\'1CHe had the opportunity to prove his labor-friendly pedigree to millions of workers by simply asking Congress for legislation to end the threat of a national strike on terms more favorable to workers. Sadly, he could not bring himself to advocate for a lousy handful of sick days. The Democrats and Republicans are both pawns of big business and the corporations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Matt Parker, a locomotive engineer and chairman of the Nevada State Legislative Board of the \uc2 Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe overly simplistic approach that the administration has taken to this whole issue shows how out of touch they are with the plight of railroad workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Railroad workers have threatened industrial action over their lack of paid sick time and the rail companies\u8217\'20\'19 disciplinary attendance systems in which they are penalized for taking unpaid time off, an issue workers say has contributed to a lack of a work-life balance on the job.\par \par \uc2 Four of the 12 railroad unions representing a majority of the railroad workforce have rejected a tentative new union contract agreement which fails to address their concerns. If any of the 12 unions go on strike, each union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/21/business/railroad-unions-votes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed }}}\uc2  to honor the picket line.\par \par \uc2 Under the Railway Labor Act, workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to legally strike is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://railroads.dot.gov/sites/fra.dot.gov/files/fra_net/1647/Railway%20Labor%20Act%20Overview.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  limited}}}\uc2  in transportation services. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/22/rail-strike-supply-chain-us-economy-travel#:~:text=The%20last%20time%20US%20railroads,two%20days%20before%20Congress%20intervened.&text=An%20extended%20rail%20shutdown%20has,harder%20for%20workers%20to%20strike."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last}}}\uc2  railroad strike in the US occurred in 1992 for two days before Congress intervened.\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , said Congress would take up legislation on Wednesday to stop a nationwide strike that would honor the original labor union agreement brokered by the Biden administration in September to avoid industrial action ahead of the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 She said the agreement \u8220\'20\'1Cis not everything I would like to see, I would like to see paid sick leave \u8211\'20\'13 every [leading democratic] country in the world has it. I don\u8217\'20\'19t like going against the ability of a union to strike but, weighing the equities, we must avoid a strike.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Parker expressed dismay and disappointment over the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s push to impose a tentative agreement most railroad workers voted against, and warned the impacts of doing so without addressing the quality-of-life issues will probably lead to higher attrition rates in a workforce that has already experienced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2021/article/employment-in-rail-transportation-heads-downhill-between-november-2018-and-december-2020.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant declines}}}\uc2  in employment in recent years.\par \par \uc2 As railroad carriers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/sep/14/us-railroad-strike-union-pacific-bnsf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implemented cuts}}}\uc2  and more grueling scheduling systems, they have also reported record profits and have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prospect.org/economy/how-americas-supply-chains-got-railroaded/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  paid out $196bn in stock buybacks and dividends}}}\uc2  to shareholders since 2010.\par \par \uc2 BNSF and Union Pacific, the two largest railroad corporations in North America, both reported record profits in 2021. \uc2 BNSF\uc2  is owned by billionaire investor \uc2 Warren Buffett\u8217\'20\'19s Berkshire Hathaway\uc2  conglomerate.\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders hit out at Buffett last week. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Warren Buffett\uc2 , the owner of \uc2 BNSF Railway\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s parent company, became $1.38bn richer yesterday,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1595555390783369216"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2 , referring to a boost to Buffett\u8217\'20\'19s net worth from a rise in \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stock price.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn one day, Mr Buffett made twice as much money as it would cost to guarantee 15 paid sick days a year to every rail worker in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe greed of the rail industry must end.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Parker claimed this action to call for imposing a rejected contract undermines Biden\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with labor, as he has repeatedly and proudly proclaimed to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/02/joe-biden-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most pro-union president ever}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat railroad workers are standing up for is a better quality of life, to get the respect that they deserve, and the benefits that they deserve and have earned. Sick time, reasonable time off to rest when the majority of the railroad workforce works on call 24/7 365 days a year,\u8221\'20\'1D Parker said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the increased demands that the railroads have put on with their personnel cuts and with these draconian attendance policies, railroaders are not given sufficient time off to rest, to recoup, to recover from illness or to spend time with their families,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what they\u8217\'20\'19re looking for. The failure to address that could have a profound effect in the future on the ability for railroads to hire and maintain workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jeff Kurtz, a locomotive engineer in Iowa for more than 40 years, severely criticized the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s tentative agreement. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not just about paid time off, it\u8217\'20\'19s about time off period,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kurtz, who has now retired. \u8220\'20\'1CBasically what the carriers, and now it looks like what Congress is going to say too, is you are pretty well tied to your job for the rest of your life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the railroad agreement, workers were provided with one paid day off and the ability to schedule three doctor appointments annually without being penalized, but Kurtz noted the parameters and restrictions make it nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freightwaves.com/news/leaked-tenative-agreement-for-rail-workers-reveals-paid-time-off-wage-increase#:~:text=The%20tentative%20agreement%20now%20guarantees,or%20surgeries%20cannot%20be%20penalized."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  impossible to use}}}\uc2  the time off and provide employers with even greater interference and control over their workers\u8217\'20\'19 healthcare. Workers had sought 15 paid days off in the contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Presidential Emergency Board was just no help whatsoever,\u8221\'20\'1D added Kurtz. \u8220\'20\'1CI thought it\u8217\'20\'19d be somewhat more labor-friendly than it was, but it could have been written by the carriers as far as I was concerned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221130eibu00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
