\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Sex parties and fast cars: US agent turned cartel mole claims DEA corruption\b0\par\par\uc2 J Oliver Conroy \par \uc2 997 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 November 2022\par 08:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As he enters prison, a disgraced former DEA agent who lived a decadent double life has claimed his own crimes were the tip of the iceberg\par \par \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Irizarry was cursed with a drug lord\u8217\'20\'19s tastes and a civil servant\u8217\'20\'19s salary.\par \par \uc2 An agent of the \uc2 US Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA)\uc2 , Irizarry liked yacht parties with sex workers, jewelry from Tiffany, Louis Vuitton luggage and luxury cars. To finance his lifestyle \u8211\'20\'13 which came to include a \uc2 BMW\uc2 , two Land Rovers and three houses \u8211\'20\'13 Irizarry embezzled millions of dollars in government funds.\par \par \uc2 In what prosecutors called a \u8220\'20\'1Cshocking breach of the public\u8217\'20\'19s trust\u8221\'20\'1D, Irizarry, 48, also laundered money with members of a Colombian drug cartel who were supposed to be his sworn foes.\par \par \uc2 The explosive revelation that one of its former rising stars spent years as a kind of cartel double agent has been deeply embarrassing to the DEA, and that and other scandals afflicting the agency show no signs of abating.\par \par \uc2 Last year, DEA agent Chad Scott was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/louisiana-new-orleans-sentencing-us-drug-enforcement-administration-83cdfbdc94ef01a4c4f312f237f22e74"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced}}}\uc2  to 13 years in prison for falsifying government records, perjury and stealing money from suspects during investigative work. Earlier this year, another agent, Nathan Koen, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/arkansas-little-rock-be77260621f384e2c979cfd2e41d3810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted}}}\uc2  of accepting bribes from a drug trafficker, and a third, John Costanzo Jr, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/us-drug-enforcement-administration-florida-miami-conspiracy-082ea2a3edbc347ffa35510cfa636755"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  with accepting bribes in exchange for leaking confidential information to defense lawyers.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/soccer-sports-la-liga-money-laundering-puerto-rico-38aed2da8cd0ac237aca28aa39321105"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interviews}}}\uc2  with the Associated Press, Irizarry, who recently began a 12-year prison sentence, has claimed that corruption is endemic in the powerful US drug agency, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dea.gov/foreign-offices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has}}}\uc2  92 foreign offices, about 4,600 special agents and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dea.gov/data-and-statistics/staffing-and-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 budget}}}\uc2  of more than $3bn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t win an unwinnable war,\u8221\'20\'1D Irizarry told the Associated Press. The \u8220\'20\'1CDEA knows this and the agents know this\u8221\'20\'1D. There is \u8220\'20\'1Cso much dope leaving Colombia. And there\u8217\'20\'19s so much money. We know we\u8217\'20\'19re not making a difference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The drug war is a game - a very fun game\par \par \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Irizarry\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe drug war is a game\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery fun game that we were playing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen my client joined the DEA he was schooled in how to be corrupt, he was schooled in how to break the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Irizarry\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Dom\u237\'00\'EDnguez, argued during his trial.\par \par \uc2 Some fellow agents describe Irizarry\u8217\'20\'19s claims as unfounded allegations by a fabulist trying to distract from his own admitted wrongdoing. A DEA spokesperson called Irizarry \u8220\'20\'1Ca criminal who violated his oath as a federal law enforcement officer and violated the trust of the American people. Over the past 16 months, DEA has worked vigorously to further strengthen our discipline and hiring policies to ensure the integrity and effectiveness of our essential work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As an agent, Irizarry had access to thousands or millions of dollars in DEA funds as well as drug proceeds that the agency had seized or was investigating. Even worse, \u8220\'20\'1Chis fingerprints are all over dozens of arrests and indictments,\u8221\'20\'1D David S Weinstein, a former federal prosecutor in Miami, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/colombia-miami-drug-cartels-us-news-ap-top-news-6c490312bef4c0600002c539d8c80cba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the Associated Press in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Irizarry, who was born in Puerto Rico and is bilingual, began his law enforcement career as a federal air marshal and an agent with the US border patrol. He was hired as a DEA special agent in 2009.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, Irizarry was hired despite a history of bankruptcy \u8211\'20\'13 with debts of almost half a million dollars \u8211\'20\'13 and a polygraph test he took during the screening process that indicated signs of deception.\par \par \uc2 Irizarry began his DEA career working out of Miami. He worked undercover and was eventually transferred to Cartagena, Colombia.\par \par \uc2 At some point, investigators and prosecutors said, Irizarry began collaborating with one of his most prized informants, the Venezuelan American Gustavo Yabrudi, to develop a money-laundering operation involving drug-world associates. They made a lot of money, fast, and Irizarry did not go to great pains to conceal his consumption habits or general recklessness.\par \par \uc2 A consummate hedonist renowned among fellow DEA agents for his extravagant tastes and fondness for sensuous and sensual pleasures, Irizarry organized parties on yachts with sex workers. The DEA was struck by scandal in 2015 when reports emerged that similar \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/666352da54e04840a37b5da740e1d79b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sex parties}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D involving its agents were occurring in Colombia. The DEA\u8217\'20\'19s then chief, Michele Leonhart, resigned in the wake of the scandal.\par \par \uc2 We had free access to do whatever we wanted. And once we got there it was about drinking and girls\par \par \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Irizarry\par \par \uc2 Irizarry claimed to the Associated Press that dozens of other agents joined in with his debauchery, and that they deliberately tailored drug operations so that they could visit party hotspots, international soccer matches and Amsterdam\u8217\'20\'19s red-light district. He said that agents referred to their frat house escapades as \u8220\'20\'1CTeam America\u8221\'20\'1D and that it spanned multiple continents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had free access to do whatever we wanted,\u8221\'20\'1D Irizarry told the Associated Press. \u8220\'20\'1CWe would generate money pick-ups in places we wanted to go. And once we got there it was about drinking and girls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe indictment paints a picture of me [as] the corrupt agent that did this entire scheme. But it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t talk about the rest of DEA. I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the mastermind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2017, after his boss became suspicious and recalled him from Colombia to Washington DC, Irizarry resigned. In 2020, after investigators closed in, he pleaded guilty to 19 federal charges, including bank fraud and embezzling drug money.\par \par \uc2 An alleged money-launderer served as godfather to his children. Irizarry\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Nathalia Gomez-Irizarry, is a relative of Diego Marin, a man many narcotics officials consider one of the biggest money-laundering suspects in Colombia.\par \par \uc2 Investigators with the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  have been quietly questioning many of Irizarry\u8217\'20\'19s former colleagues, the Associated Press reports, and last year the department\u8217\'20\'19s Office of the Inspector General released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/reports/21-109.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  asserting a dangerous shortage of oversight and accountability in the DEA.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221120eibk000mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
