\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Workers at over 100 US Starbucks stores strike on \u8216\'20\'18Red Cup Day\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 304 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 November 2022\par 21:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Strike was launched to protest against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 failure to bargain with unionized stores and failure to adequately staff stores\par \par \uc2 Workers at over 100 unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores around the US walked off the job on Thursday, coinciding with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Red Cup Day, a promotional day where customers receive a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/food/2022/11/16/free-starbucks-red-cup-2022/10703885002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 free red reusable holiday Starbucks cup }}}\uc2  when they order a holiday seasonal beverage.\par \par \uc2 The strike was launched to protest against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 failure to bargain with unionized stores and failure to adequately staff stores, especially on one of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 busiest days where no pay differential is offered to workers. About 2,000 workers at 112 stores {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2022/11/17/starbucks-strike-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 participated}}}\uc2  in the strikes in 25 states.\par \par \uc2 Workers have criticized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for delaying union bargaining after union elections and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/nov/17/starbucks-union-fight-delays"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently walking out}}}\uc2  on recent bargaining sessions across the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRed Cup Day is notoriously difficult on baristas and notoriously profitable for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 : striking on a day that affects both us and customers more so than an average day is a great way to connect with the community about why unions in the workplace are needed, and how they can help their local unions succeed while keeping businesses running,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Schule, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  barista in Massachusetts, in a statement on the strike actions.\par \par \uc2 More than 260 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores have unionized around the US since December 2021. Starbucks Workers United have accused the company of delaying and dragging out bargaining sessions for a first union contract and filed numerous unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has issued 39 complaints against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , encompassing more than 900 unfair labor practice charges. Starbucks Workers United has claimed over 150 union leaders have been fired around the country in 2022 in retaliation for union organizing.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221117eibh002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
