\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  workers picket over contracts as company reports record revenue\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 758 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2022\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unions say airline industry seeks to return to normal without addressing serious problems around pay and staffing\par \par \uc2 Flight attendants at \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  have held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mailchi.mp/apfa.org/its-time-to-turn-up-the-heat-on-american-airlines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 picket rallies }}}\uc2  at 11 major airports in the US, over the airline rejecting new union contract proposals from the \uc2 Association of Professional Flight Attendants\uc2 , which represents 25,000 of its flight attendants.\par \par \uc2 The move is the latest in a series of industrial actions and disputes to have hit the US airlines industry as it recovers from the Covid-19 pandemic. Workers and unions say that the industry has sought to return to normal without addressing serious problems, especially around pay and staffing levels.\par \par \uc2 Julie Hedrick\uc2 , national president of the \uc2 Association of Professional Flight Attendants\uc2 , explained negotiations were initially delayed due to the Covid-19 pandemic, but restarted in August 2021. Since that time the company has rejected improvements sought by workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been going without a raise since January 2019. It\u8217\'20\'19s been many years since our flight attendants got a raise and a lot of our bases are in very high cost of living cities, such as Boston, New York, Chicago and Miami, so we\u8217\'20\'19re definitely ready for a raise with the way everything has increased in price,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hedrick.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1COur staffing has also been cut. We\u8217\'20\'19re back to flying the same amount of flights and hours we flew back in 2019, prior to Covid, with thousands of fewer flight attendants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She noted the union is pushing for pay rises, better flexibility for flights, and improved operational reliability, as \uc2 American Airlines{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.aa.com/news/news-details/2022/American-Airlines-Reports-Third-Quarter-2022-Financial-Results-CORP-FI-10/default.aspx#:~:text=(NASDAQ%3A%20AAL)%20today%20reported,or%20%240.69%20per%20diluted%20share."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  a profit of $478m (\u163\'00\'A3402m) in the third quarter of 2022, including record revenue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEmployees at \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  helped \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  return to profitability,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve helped this airline return to profitability, so it\u8217\'20\'19s our time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  is not the only US carrier in conflict with its workers.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 10,000 pilots at \uc2 United Airlines{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/united-airlines-pilots-vote-reject-contract-offer-2022-11-01/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  down a tentative agreement on 2 November and picketed outside the United Airlines Flight Training Center in Denver, Colorado, on 15 November over delays in coming to an agreement acceptable to pilots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CManagement has chosen to delay the conclusion of our negotiations,\u8221\'20\'1D said United Master Executive Council chair Capt Mike Hamilton. \u8220\'20\'1CContinued stalling at the bargaining table puts the company\u8217\'20\'19s growth plans at risk and hinders the airline\u8217\'20\'19s overall goal of being the best airline in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In September 2022, flight attendants at \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2  and \uc2 United Airlines{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/28/1125525868/flight-attendants-picket-airports-demanding-that-airlines-fix-chronic-delays"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held picket protests}}}\uc2  at airports around the US to protest delays, operational issues and the working conditions posed by the delays.\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2 , nearly 15,000 pilots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dal.alpa.org/strike?utm_source=seattle_times&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=dal_mec_negotiations_111#pressrelease"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted }}}\uc2  to authorize a strike with 99% voting in favor, the first strike vote taken at Delta since 2006. Contract negotiations were paused due to Covid-19, but resumed in January 2022.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Mediation Board\uc2  must decide that additional mediation efforts would not be productive and release the airline and union, Delta Air Line Pilots Association (ALPA), to arbitration, and if either side declines, a 30-day cooling off period would proceed before a strike can begin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been working under pay rates, work rules, benefits that were all negotiated in 2016,\u8221\'20\'1D said Evan Baach, a pilot at \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  and spokesperson for the ALPA. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been in negotiations for quite some time. Our contract became amendable in 2019. We\u8217\'20\'19re approaching the end of 2022 here and our pilots are frustrated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Baach noted pilots at \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/transportation/3527227-delta-pilots-say-theyve-been-flying-record-amount-of-overtime-amid-flight-cancellations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working record overtime}}}\uc2 , as the airlines {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/delta-air-lines-announces-september-quarter-2022-profit-301648047.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  record quarterly revenue in the third quarter of 2022. The union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Delta_Pilots/status/1589620569992966144"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took offense}}}\uc2  to comments made by \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  CEO \uc2 Ed Bastian\uc2  in an interview on the Today Show, claiming there is no possibility of a pilots\u8217\'20\'19 strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDelta pilots played a huge role in helping the company get through the pandemic. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been working a record amount of overtime. In longer days, we have shorter nights at home, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been spending more time away from our families,\u8221\'20\'1D added Baach. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been working incredibly hard. We are long term stakeholders at \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2 . We dedicate decades of our lives to a career at Delta and we\u8217\'20\'19ve earned an industry leading contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  did not respond to multiple requests for comment on the picketing.\par \par \uc2 Delta Airlines{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/11/01/1133033107/delta-airlines-pilots-strike-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  strike concerns as a tactic to gain leverage in negotiations, but affirmed a new contract would be resolved before a strike is considered.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221116eibg000ss\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
